[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the fraction of 2 feet that is 3 inches, we need to convert both measurements to the same unit. Since 1 foot is equal to 12 inches, we can convert 2 feet to inches as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2 feet * 12 inches/foot = 24 inches
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we have 24 inches and 3 inches. To find the fraction, we divide the number of inches by the number of feet:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 24 inches / 2 feet = 12 inches/foot
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, 3 inches is 12/24 of 2 feet, which simplifies to 1/2 of 2 feet.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
