[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m According to the problem, the measure of an interior angle is 6.5 times the measure of an exterior angle. Therefore, we can write the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Measure of interior angle} = 6.5 \times \text{Measure of exterior angle}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substituting the expressions for the interior and exterior angles, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{360^\circ}{n} = 6.5 \times \frac{360^\circ}{n}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve for \( n \), we can divide both sides of the equation by \( \frac{360^\circ}{n} \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1 = 6.5
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This equation is not possible, which means there is no regular polygon with the given conditions. However, if we assume the problem is asking for the number of sides of a regular polygon that satisfies the given condition, we can use the relationship between the interior and exterior angles to find the number of sides.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The measure of an exterior angle of a regular polygon is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Measure of exterior angle} = \frac{360^\circ}{n}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The measure of an interior angle of a regular polygon is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Measure of interior angle} = 6.5 \times \text{Measure of exterior angle} = 6.5 \times \frac{360^\circ}{n}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For a regular polygon, the sum of the interior angles is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Sum of interior angles} = (n - 2) \times 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Setting the sum of the interior angles equal to the sum of the exterior angles, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (n - 2) \times 180^\circ = 6.5 \times \frac{360^\circ}{n}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (n - 2) \times 180^\circ = 6.5 \times \frac{360^\circ}{n}
