[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the maximum area of a square inscribed in a circle with radius 1 unit, we first need to find the diagonal of the square. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since the circle has a radius of 1 unit, the diameter is 2 units. Now, let's consider a square inscribed in the circle. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If we draw the symmetry line from one corner of the square to the midpoint of the opposite side, two equal triangles are formed. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since the height of each of the triangles is \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} (half of the diameter), the side length of the square will be twice the height, i.e., 1. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the area of the square is 1 * 1 = 1 square unit.
