[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the sum of the final three digits of the integer representation of $5^{100}$, we will first compute $5^{100}$ and then find the last three digits of this number. This can be done by finding the remainder when $5^{100}$ is divided by 1000. This will give us the last three digits of $5^{100}$, and the sum of these digits.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If the remainder is 000 or 0000, then the last three digits are 000; otherwise, the last three digits are the remainder from the division, which is 000 + remainder.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Here is the step-by-step Python code to compute this:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m import sympy as sp
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # Compute 5^100
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m power_result = 5**100
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # Find the last three digits (the remainder when 5^100 is divided by 1000)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m remainder = power_result % 1000
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # Calculate the sum of the last three digits
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m sum_of_digits = sum(int(digit) for digit in str(remainder))
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m print(sum_of_digits)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This code will give us the last three digits of $5^{100}$, and the sum of these digits. Running this code:
