[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve the problem, let's use Cramer's rule. We will first set up the system of equations in matrix form and then solve for \(a, b, c\). Finally, we'll use these values to compute the desired expression.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The given system of equations is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m -x + cy + bz = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m cx - y + az = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m bx + ay - z = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This can be written in matrix form as:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m -x & cy & bz \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m cx & -y & az \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m b & ay & -1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m a \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m b \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m c
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Using Cramer's rule, we find the values of \(a, b, c\) by solving the determinant of the coefficient matrix for each variable. Then, we substitute these values back into the expression \(a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + 2abc\) and solve for the desired quantity.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's assume the system of equations is consistent and the determinant of the matrix is non-zero. We'll proceed step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Step 1: Solve the system for \(a, b, c\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We can use substitution or another method to solve the system. Let's use the identity for the determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m -x & cy & bz \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m cx & -y & az \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m b & ay & -1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = -\det\begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m a & cy & bz \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m b & -y & az \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m b & ay & 1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Step 2: Calculate the determinant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x & cy & bz \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m b & y & az \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m b & ay & 1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = x(ay - aiaz) - cy(b - aby) + bz(b - by)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Step 3: Simplify the determinant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = -a(x(ay - zb) + y(ba - z^2))
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Step 4: Solve for \(c\)
