[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Determine the complex number $z$ satisfying the equation $2z-3\bar{z}=-2-30i$.  Note that $\bar{z}$ denotes the conjugate of $z$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve the equation $2z-3\bar{z}=-2-30i$, we can use the property that the conjugate of a product of two numbers is the product of their conjugates. Hence, we multiply both sides of the equation by $\bar{z}$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2z - 3\bar{z} &= -2 - 30i \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2\bar{z} - 3\bar{z} (z + \bar{z}) &= -2 - 30i 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We know that 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \bar{z} (z + \bar{z}) &= 0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, substituting back into the original equation, we have 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2\bar{z} - 3\bar{z} (z + \bar{z}) &= -2 - 30i \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2\bar{z} - 3 (z + \bar{z}) &= -2 - 30i 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We then rearrange and group terms involving $\bar{z}$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2\bar{z} &= -2 - 30i + 3z + 3\bar{z} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3\bar{z} &= -2 - 30i + 3z \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m z &= \frac{-2 - 30i}{3} - \bar{z}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Hence, directly:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$ z = -1 - 10i$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Explanation: We used the stepwise elimination method to systematically solve for \( z \). Then, substituting back the frequency of \( \bar{z} \). Therefore, we obtained \( \boxed{-1 - 10i} \).
