[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let \[g(x) = \left\{ \begin{aligned} 3x+6 & \quad \text{ if } x < 0 \\ 2x - 13 & \quad \text{ if } x \ge 0 \end{aligned} \right.\]Find all solutions to the equation $g(x) = 3.$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we need to consider the two parts of the function separately for $x \ge 0$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\begin{aligned} 3x + 6 & = 3 \\ & \Longleftrightarrow x + 2 &= 3 \\ & \Longleftrightarrow x &= 1. \end{aligned}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the solution to $x \ge 0$ is $x = 1$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we consider the part of the function for $x < 0$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\begin{aligned} \color{#1da7de}{2x - 13} & = 3 \\ & \Longleftrightarrow 2x &= 4 \\ & \Longleftrightarrow x &= 2. \end{aligned}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the solution to $x < 0$ is $x = 2$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Putting it all together, the solutions to the equation $g(x) = 3$ are $x = 1$ and $x = 2.$ NAFTA!
