[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This graph shows the linear relationship between the time in seconds, $x$, for Caroline's walk and the distance in meters, $y$, Caroline is from her starting point. The graph passes through the point $(20,30)$. According to the graph, how many meters will Caroline walk in exactly one hour? [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G;
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A=(-20,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m B=(120,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m C=(0,-20);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m D=(0,120);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m E=(-6.2,-8);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m F=(60,90);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m G=(70,105);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m dot(F);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m draw(A--B,Arrows);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m draw(C--D,Arrows);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m draw(E--G,Arrows);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m label("(20,30)",G,SE);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m label("$y=1.5x$",G,N);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m [/asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The positive slope indicates that the distance \( y \) is linearly related to \( x \) with a constant of 1.5 meters per second squared. Therefore, the relationship between \( y \) and \( x \) can be described as \( y = 1.5x \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine how many meters Caroline will walk in exactly one hour, we need to calculate \( y \) for \( x = 60 \) (which is 1 hour).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we calculate \( y \) when \( x = 60 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m y = 1.5 \times 60 = 90
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This means that in exactly one hour, Caroline will walk 90 meters.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the answer is \(\boxed{90}\).<|endoftext|>
