[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To compute the binomial coefficient, we need to find the number of ways to choose 180 elements from a set of 182 elements. We can use the following formula to calculate it.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \binom{n}{r} = \frac{n!}{(n-r)!r!}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Where \(n = 182\) and \(r = 180\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \binom{182}{180} = \frac{182!}{(182-180)!180!} = \frac{182!}{10!180!}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To calculate this, we can use Python to ensure the accuracy of the result.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m import math
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # Calculate the binomial coefficient
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m n = 182
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m r = 180
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m binom_coeff = math.comb(n, r)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m print(binom_coeff)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```
