[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In ten marathons, these distances are clearly in the same unit, so we can compare the distance continue:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. $m$ should be in terms of tens, yards, and miles.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Convert 385 yards to miles and yards:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    385 \div 360 = 1 \ \mbox{with a remainder of } 25
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Assuming 25 yards per mile, we can determine the five-step distance in miles and yards in one step $t$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    26t + 1 \ \mbox{with a remainder of } 0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. The resulting displacement would be:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \boxed{26 \cdot t + 1 = x}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Adjusting the conversion to round up if $t > \frac{0}{26}$ and decrements based on spare $(y-0)$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Here we round up (circular proximity):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x = \lceil 26 \cdot {t}_{\text{ST = 1}} + 1 \rceil
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m y = \lfloor 26 \cdot \frac{t}{26 + 1} - 1 \rfloor
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since the precise array challenges provide no explanation or correction.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
