[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the maximum value of $ab$ when $a$ is positive is $\boxed{3/2}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Case 2: When $a$ is negative, let's consider the situation where $y$ and $x$ are both negative, so $x$ and $y$ have the same magnitude. Then, $z$ is either positive or negative. If $z$ is positive, we have $|x + y| = 1$. So,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ab &= |x + y|xz(y + \frac{1}{2}y) + \frac{|x + y|}{2}y \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= -xz(x + y + \frac{1}{2}y) - \frac{|x + y|}{2}y \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= -x \left(\frac{1}{2}y z\right) - \frac{x}{2} \frac{1}{2}y \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= -x \left(\frac{1}{2}y z\right) - \frac{x}{4}y \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= \frac{1}{4} \left(y^2 - x \left(\frac{1}{2}y z\right)\right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= \frac{1}{4} \left(y\left(\frac{1}{2}xz - x\right)\right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &\leq \frac{1}{4} \cdot \frac{1}{4} \left(x \left(\frac{1}{2}yz - y\right)\right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= \frac{1}{16} \left(x \left(\frac{1}{2}yz - y + 2\right)\right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= \frac{1}{16} \left(x \left(\frac{1}{2}yz - y + 2\right)\right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= \frac{1}{16} \left(x \left(\frac{1}{2}yz - y + 2\right)\right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= \boxed{-\frac{1}{16}}\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the maximum value of $ab$ when $a$ is negative is $-\frac{1}{16}$.
