[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Determine the complex number $z$ satisfying the equation $2z-3\bar{z}=-2-30i$.  Note that $\bar{z}$ denotes the conjugate of $z$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Set up the given equation $2z-3\bar{z}=-2-30i$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Using the property of complex number, $\bar{z}=-\frac{2z+2+30i}{3}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Therefore, $2z-3\bar{z}=2z+3z+2+30i=5z+2+30i$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Rearrange the equation to $5z=2+z+30i$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. Simplify the equation to $5z=2+z+30i$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6. Use the property of complex number, $1+0i=1$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 7. Thus, $5z=0+z+30i$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 8. The conjugate of $z$ is $1+i$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 9. So, $z=0-i$.
