[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So the smallest possible value of \(x + y + z + w\) is \(15\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, let's find the smallest possible value of \(x + y + z + w\) if all participants are allowed to use each operation exactly once. We need to maximize the expression \(x + y + z + w\) by using each operation except for the one that equalizes the term \(2(a - b)\). Adding and subtracting \(x\) and \(z\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
