[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The function $f$ has the property that for each real number $x$ in its domain, $1/x$ is also in its domain and \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m f(x) + f\left(\frac{1}{x}\right) = x.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]What is the largest set of real numbers that can be in the domain of $f$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (a) ${\{x\mid x\ne0\}}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (b) ${\{x\mid x<0\}}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (c) ${\{x\mid x>0\}}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (d) ${\{x\mid x\ne-1\ \text{and}\ x\ne0\ \text{and}\ x\ne1\}}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (e) ${\{-1,1\}}$
