[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since the dimensions of the plates are invariant (since each plate has 26 letters and 5 digits), we can focus on analyzing the distribution of letter and digit frequencies in Florida and North Dakota. As they both have identical formats, each position in the plate will have each letter and number standardized.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To estimate how many more unique 6-position license plates that Florida can generate compared to North Dakota:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Count the number 6-letter combinations with alphabets ±_ (for encompassing all letters, as letters are both letters and numbers)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Calculate the number of 6-letter combinations without both letters being letters.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Find the lesser of the counts from step 1 and step 2.
