[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A sequence consists of $2010$ terms.  Each term after the first is 1 larger than the previous term.  The sum of the $2010$ terms is $5307$.  When every second term is added up, starting with the first term and ending with the second last term, what is the sum?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The terms after the first are $q^{1}$ and $q^{2010}$. The arithmetic series that we want to find is $$\begin{cases}5307&\\q^{2}&\end{cases}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The sum of the $(2⁰⁸)$ terms of the arithmetic series is $$\begin{cases}5307&\\q^{(2⁰⁸)-1}&\end{cases}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Notice that the left side of the equation is the same as $q$ with $q$ replacing $5307/q$. The $2⁰⁸ + \frac{1}{2} - 1$th term of this arithmetic series is $$\begin{cases}5307&\\q^{(\frac{2⁰⁸ + \frac{1}{2} - 1}{2})-1}&\end{cases}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Hence, the sum of the first $2⁰⁸$ terms of this arithmetic series is $\boxed{5307 q^{2}}$<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m [Ground Truth]
