[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The parabola is of the form $y = ax^2 + bx + c.$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We can find the values of $a$ and $c$ using the coefficients of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $y = -2x^2 + 4x -8$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $a = -2,$ $c = -8$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since $a < 0,$ the parabola opens downwards.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The point of intersection of the $x$- and $y$-axes is $(-\frac{10}{3}, 0)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The $x$-coordinate of the coordinates of the directrix is the negative of this point, so
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $x = -\frac{10}{3}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $q = -\frac{-10}{3}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Divide both sides by $8.$ $d = -\frac{3}{6}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $d = -\frac{1}{2}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The equation of the directrix is $y = -\frac{1}{2}$.
