[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Paula invests $\$10,\!000$ for 5 years at an interest rate of $10\%$ per year. If the interest is simple interest, how much is her investment worth at the end of those five years?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we need to find the simple interest that Paula will earn as a result of her investment. Simple interest (\$A_i)\texttt{=}A\text{⋅}r\cdot t$, where $A$ is the \$original\amount\ invested, $r$ is the annual interest rate, and $t$ is the time in years.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $A=\$10,\!000$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $r=\frac{10\%==0.10}{4} \approx 0.025$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $t=5$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Using the formula for simple interest:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A &= A_i \\ \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A &= 10,\!000 \cdot 0.025 \cdot 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= 12,\!250.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Paula's investment will be worth $\boxed{12,\!250}$ at the end of five years.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
