[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Tyler has entered a buffet line in which he chooses one kind of meat, two different vegetables and one dessert.  If the order of food items is not important, how many different meals might he choose?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\bullet$  Meat: beef, chicken, pork
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\bullet$  Vegetables: baked beans, corn, potatoes, tomatoes
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\bullet$  Dessert: brownies, chocolate cake, chocolate pudding, ice cream
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine the number of different meals Tyler can choose, let's break down the logic step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Step 1: Analyze the variation of service**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Beef: 1 variant (beef)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Chicken: 1 variant (chicken)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Pork: 1 variant (pork)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - All others are the same
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - All can be used in that single selection
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Step 2: Calculate the total number of hamburger combinations from each service**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Beef orders: $1 \times 1 = 1$ combination
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Chicken orders: $1 \times 1 = 1$ combination
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Pork orders: $1 \times 1 = 1$ combination
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - All orders: $1 \times 1 \times 1 = 1$ combination
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Step 3: Multiply the number of combinations from each service**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1 \text{ (chicken)} \times 1 \text{ (pork)} \times 1 \text{ (all other)} = 1 \text{ hamburger}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the total number of different meals Tyler might choose is $\boxed{1}$.<|endoftext|>
