[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Edited for better wording of answer.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In order for two lines to be skew, their direction vectors must be orthogonal (multiplication transformations meet at a right angle).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = 4+6+4=14,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m and
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = 10 + 6 + 4 = 20.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, we need
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 14 \neq 20.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
