[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To parameterize the given line $y = 2x + 7$ using vectors, we need to find two vectors that lie along the line and form the direction vector of the line. These vectors should be pointing in the same direction of the slope of the line. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Exercise and review the graph of the line: Draw the line $y = 2x + 7$. The slope of the line is 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Choose two points on the line: To get four points that lie on the line, pick two points where the line intersects the x and y axes.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Intersection with the x-axis (at y = 0): $0 = 2x + 7 \Rightarrow x = -\frac{7}{2}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Intersection with the y-axis (at x = 0): $y = 9$ (we don't need these points to form the parameterization)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Form the vectors: 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Vector for each endpoint of the x-axis: $\begin{pmatrix} x_1 \\ y_1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{7}{2} \\ 9 \end{pmatrix}$ with the direction vector $\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Vector for each endpoint of the y-axis: $\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ y_2 \end{pmatrix}$ with the direction vector $\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Parameterize the vectors:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    (A) $\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    (B) $\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{7}{2} \\ 9 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Where vector components are found by adding corresponding components from lists (moves right by 2 units, up by 1 unit):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - For (A): $\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2t+0 \\ 2 + 7t \end{pmatrix}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - For (B): $\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{7}{2} \\ 9 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 - t \\ 9 - 2t \end{pmatrix}$
