[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We know that the fractional part of $x$ is $ \left\lfloor x \right\rfloor-\tfrac{1}{2}=x-\tfrac{1}{2}\implies \left\lfloor x \right\rfloor=x-\tfrac{1}{2}$, so we know that $x\cdot(x-\tfrac{1}{2})=27$. Thus, $x\cdot\tfrac{4}{2}=27\implies x=27\cdot \frac{2}{4}=\tfrac{27}{4}=6.75$.
