[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    g(0) = 10^0 - 10^{2 \cdot 0} = 1 - 1 = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. For $x \geq 1$: $g(x) = 10^{x} - 10^{2x} \geq 0$, since $10^{x} > 5$ for all $x$ and $10^{2x} > 0$. Additionally, as $x \rightarrow \infty$: $g(x) = 10^{x} \geq 10^{2x}$, thus the function is monotonic and increasing. Hence, the maximum value occurs at $x=\infty: 0$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. For $x < 0$: $g(x) = 10^{x} - 10^{2x} \uparrow$, because with negative numbers, the more exponent(s) you multiply, the larger the result. Therefore, the maximum value of $g(x)$ is $0$ for $x = 0$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. For $x \in [-1, 1]$: $g(x) = 10^x - 10^{2x}$, and since $10^x$ is maximized when $x = 0$, $g(x) = -5 = 0.001$ for $x = 0$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. For $x \in [0, 1]$: $g(x) = 10^0 - 10^{2x} + 5 \imes 10^{x} - 10^{2x} \times 5 \times 10^x$, subgroupings bear significance, we consider the limit going to 0. This approach shows that the maximum value in $[0, 2]$ is less than $0.4996\approx 0.4996$, and considering the behavior as $x$ approaches infinity it remains as $0.001$, with the preceding proof collaborates rigor to conclude the maximum value is $0$ for $x <-1$ and maximized at $0$.
