[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $x=5+2\sqrt7$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Then, $(5+2\sqrt7)^4=x^4$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we need to calculate $(x^4)^{\frac14}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We know that $(a^b)^{\frac14}=\sqrt{\sqrt{a^b}}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This allows us to calculate $\sqrt{x^4}=|x|=\sqrt{(5+2\sqrt7)^2}=\boxed{5+2\sqrt7}$.
