[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m What is the value of $x$ in the equation $2x + \frac{1}{2}x + 2(1+x) = 29$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Distribute $2$ to $2(1+x)$, and then combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$2x + \frac{1}{2}x + 2(1+x) = 29$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$2x + \frac{1}{2}x + 2 + 2x = 29$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Bringing all the variables to one side:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$2(2x + \frac{1}{2}x) + 2x + 2 - 29 = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$2(2x + \frac{1}{2}x) - 27 = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$(2x + \frac{1}{2}x) = \boxed{\frac{27}{2}}$$
