[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Number of Faculty is How many students/passenger will be:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve this problem, we need to count how many occupants each constant train makes and figure out how many of them can fit.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - The train makes 4 trips per hour.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Each room can hold 7 people.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine how many people fit into each room, we can use the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Occupants per room} = \frac{\text{Total capacity of the room}}{\text{Capacity per room}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Where:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Total capacity of the room = 7 people
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Capacity per room = 7 people
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let’s calculate it.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Occupants per room} = \frac{7}{7} = 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This tells us that each room can fit 1 person.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we need to find out how many rooms can fit in 4 trips:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Total number of rooms} = \frac{\text{Total capacity}}{\text{Occupants per room}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Total number of rooms} = \frac{7}{1} = 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This means 7 rooms can fit 7 people, and hence 7 passengers.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ---
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, to sum it all up:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Total number of ROOMS that can be FILLED = 7
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Each Room has capacity = 7 people
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, HGHX Charlie 7 customers can fit into 7 rooms.<|endoftext|>
