[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Yes, I can help you with that! The number $n = 2^2 \cdot 3^1 \cdot 7^2$ is in the form of $a^x b^y c^z$, where each number is a multiple of prime factors. To find the number of even natural-number factors of $n$, we can use the principle that needlesfactor. even natural-number factors are those that are divisible by 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
