[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The two roots $\dfrac{\color{#c90}m+chi}{\color{#c90}n}$ for the quadratic equation $7x^2 + 3x + k = 0$ are $\dfrac{\color{#c90}p-qi}{\color{#c90}r}$ (provided that $p, q, r > 0$) and $\dfrac{\color{#c90}u+VI}{\color{#c90}c}$, where $p, u, t, c, V, q, r$ are the roots of $7x^2+2x+7 = 0$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substituting the known roots, we have
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \color{#c90}{\dfrac{m+ch}{n}} &= \dfrac{\sqrt{299}}{14}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \color{#c90}{\dfrac{\color{#c90}p-qi}{\color{#c90}r}} &= -\dfrac{9}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \color{#c90}{\dfrac{\color{#c90}u+VI}{\color{#c90}c}} &= 6\sqrt{3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Squaring, we obtain
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \color{#c90}{(\color{#c90}m+hu}{)^2} &= h^2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \color{#c90}{(\color{#c90}p-qi}{)^2} &= g^2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \color{#c90}{(\color{#c90}u+v+vi)} &=-\dfrac{h}{d} 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m for an integer $d$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m From the given quadratic equation, it follows that $h = 1$, $d = 7$, and $b = 3$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m m + pqi&=-\dfrac{t}{d}+1\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m mu+v+vi&=-\dfrac{h}{d}+1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This yields two sets of equations
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m m&=4-9t\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m pqi&m-9t+1&=0\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m mu+v+vi&=-\dfrac{1}{7}+pqi+1&=0\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m mu+v &=-\dfrac{1}{7}(pqi+9t-1)&=0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The 6th equation can be simplified to
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m mu+v = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Setting the first equation fot $mu+v$, we get $pqi=5$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Multiplying both sides of the equation $mu+v=0$ by $pqi$, and then adding b and c equations to get $pqi=u+v$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substituting $p=5$ into the equation $p+th=0$, we get $t=45$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substituting the values we found into the equation $he+vi=-\dfrac{h}{d}+1$, we obtain $h=1$, $d=7$, and $e=-4$ (or thereabouts).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Hence, the final answer is\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$\boxed{\dfrac{1}{7}+b\sqrt{3}}$$<|endoftext|>
