[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Carefully simplify the square root of $25,000$. You can write $25,000$ as the $100^{2}$, since
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 25000 &= 100 \times 250\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &=10^{2}\times 250\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &=10^{2}\times10\times25=(10^{2})\times(10\times25\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= 2000 \times 50\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= 10^{2}\times(10 \times50).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Using the property of $\sqrt{x^{n}}=x^{n}/10^{n}=(10^{n})/10^{n}$, you get
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sqrt{25,000} &=\sqrt{2000 \times 50}\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &=(100^{2})\times(25\times10^{2})\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &=25 \times 10^{2}\times 25\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &=25\times 10^{2} \times25\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &=25 \times 10^{2+2}\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &=10^{2+2}\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &=200.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
