[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve this problem, we first need to determine Kit's moving rate in feet per minute. We are given that Kit moved 60 feet closer to the ticket window in 30 minutes. Therefore, her moving rate is $\frac{60\text{ feet}}{30\text{ minutes}}=2\text{ feet per minute}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now that we know her moving rate, we can calculate how many minutes it would take her to move 70 yards. Since 1 yard is equal to 3 feet, 70 yards is equal to $70 \times 3=210$ feet.The time required to move 210 feet at her rate is $frac{210\text{ feet}}{2\text{ feet per minute}}=105$ minutes. Therefore, it will take Kit 105 minutes to move the remaining 70 yards to the ticket window.
