[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's check each number from 1 to 9 (since 10 is not a prime number because it can be divided by 2 and 5):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 1 is not a prime number (divisors include 1 and 1)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 2 is prime (only divisors include 1 and 2)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 3 is prime (only divisors include 1 and 3)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 4 is not a prime number (divisors include 1 and 2)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 5 is prime (only divisors include 1 and 5)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 6 is not a prime number (divisors include 1, 2, 3, and 6)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 7 is prime (only divisors include 1 and 7)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 8 is not a prime number (divisors include 1, 2, 4, and 8)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 9 is not a prime number (divisors include 1, 3, and 9)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Prime Number List after 10:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
