[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore,  $\begin{eqnarray} \sqrt{(x+y)} &=& 6^{\mp1} \\(x+y) &=& 6 \cdot 6^{\pm 1} = 6 \cdot (-2~ 3\ {*} \frac{^{16}2}1} )=(6+2 3)()^{^{2}} \\(x+y) &=& 40^7=83,\!209 \!332 \& \!3 \end{eqnarray}$$
