[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. **Calculate the area of the original rectangular garden:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Length = 40 feet
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Width = 10 feet
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Area = Length * Width = 40 * 10 = 400 square feet
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. **Calculate the area of the new square garden:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Side length = 30 feet (because the original garden is 4 feet shorter in length and 3 feet taller in width than the new garden)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Area = Side length^2 = 30 * 30
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. **Calculate the difference between the two areas:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Difference = Area1 - Area2 = Area1 - Area2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
