[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If two (positive) prime numbers are roots of the equation $x^2-12x+k=0$, what is the value of $k$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let the two positive prime numbers be $p$ and $q$, then
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$p^2=12p+k~ , q^2=12q+k$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This makes it easy to find prime values for $p$ or $q$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m My thoughts:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m gcd (p,k) = gcd (12,k) = 3 thus p = 4k or 3k or 9k
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For 4, then p = q = 8 which is too small.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, assumng 3, 9 can't be prime, then 8 is a great prime number. 4q = pq or 9q = pq (with distinct denominator)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $n = \gcd(p,k)$. Since the polynomials are tha right when $n$ occur, then
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $k = (kp^n-q)p^{n-2}$ as well as
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $p = \left(\left(k-q\right)^n+{9}q^{2n-1}\right)/k$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m And
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\begin{align*}\left(k-q\right)^n+{9}q^{2n-1} & = {8}+{9}q^2\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}$ and
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $k = 4$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Correct me if was not right, thanks in advance D: ) $\ $ HINT:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $ 12$ is the only digit you need to factorise further (The factorising may take a while)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\ $ Answer $ 1 $:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $(p,q)$ are a pair of distinct positive factors of $ 12 $.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\triangle \text { } q - p = 4$, $\ $ then $ 0.955916... < \lceil 3.141593 \rceil = 2.35 > q \gt p , \\ \triangle \text { } \ \ $ We have $ q=3 $ and $ p=3.6-x=\frac{2}{3} < x < \frac{5}{6} \ . \ $ 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Using $ n^3 - 3n^2 + 2n -12 = 0$ we find the two roots,then prime values. We find the values satisfied by $\ \ $ the root $\mathinf q$ .
