[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - \( 37 \times \) (\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Therefore, the LCM is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    2 \times 3 \times 49 \times 1 \times 37
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - \(
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    49 \times 3 = 147
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Finally:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Multiple:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    2 \times 3 \times 49 \times 1 \times 37
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Thus, the least common multiple of two numbers is mimicking the products of their highest prime exponents (when expanded in exponents).
