[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve the equation, we first distribute the $5$ over the terms in the left side of the equation and on the right side of the equation to eliminate the parentheses by adding $-(1-7x)$. This gives:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5(3x + 2) - 2 = -2(1 - 7x)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5 \cdot 3x + 5 \cdot 2 - 2 = -2 \cdot 1 - 2 \cdot 7x
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we will simplify both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Distribute $5$ over $3x + 2$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 15x + 10 - 2 = -2 - 14x
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Simplify the left side:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 15x + 8 = -2 - 14x
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Add $14x$ to both sides to get all the $x$ terms on one side and the constant terms on the other side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 15x + 14x + 8 = -2 - 14x + 14x
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 29x + 8 = -2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Subtract $8$ from both sides to isolate the $x$ term:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 29x = -2 - 8
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
