[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To express $0.1\overline{7}$ as a common fraction, we first convert the repeating decimal to a fraction using the following steps.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $x = 0.1\overline{7}$. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 100, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$100x = 1.7\overline{7}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we will subtract the original equation from the modified version:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$100x - x = 1.7\overline{7} - 0.1\overline{7}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplifying both sides, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$99x = 1.6$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$x = \dfrac{16}{99}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, $0.1\overline{7}$ is equivalent to the fraction $\boxed{\dfrac{16}{99}}$.(Get rid of your accent marks. You can't end answers with those punctuations because they're part of the punctuation)
