[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m One piece of string is 1.5 inches long and another piece of string is 4.5 inches long. What is the average length, in inches, of these two pieces of string?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's start by converting the measurements from inches to centimeters, as it's recommended before finding the average, since 1 inch is well-defined as $2.54$ centimeters.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 0.5 \, \text{in} = 0.5 \times 2.54 \text{ cm} = 1.27 \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1.5 \, \text{in} = 1.5 \times 2.54 \text{ cm} = 3.81 \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4.5 \, \text{in} = 4.5 \times 2.54 \text{ cm} = 11.15 \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we have the measurements in centimeters, which are \(1.27\), \(3.81\), \(11.15\), and \(1.27\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the average length in centimeters, we can add all these values and divide by the number of values.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Average length in cm} = \frac{1.27 + 3.81 + 11.15 + 1.27}{4} = \frac{26.5}{4} = 6.625 \text{ cm}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the average length of the two pieces of string is \(\boxed{6.625}\) centimeters.<|endoftext|>
