[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the projection of the vector  \vec v_1 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} \text{ onto } \mathbf b = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}, \text{ we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m  - **Step 1: Represent the equation** 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    The given equation is
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{3}{5} \\ \frac{6}{5} \end{pmatrix} = \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf b} \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{3}{5} \\ \frac{6}{5} \end{pmatrix} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Since we know that \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf b} \vec v_1 = \begin{pmatrix} d_1 \\ d_2 \end{pmatrix}, we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ d_1 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} + d_2 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} = -\frac{3}{5} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} + \frac{6}{5} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    This forms a system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ \begin{cases} d_1 + d_2 = -\frac{3}{5} \\ d_1 - d_2 = \frac{6}{5} \end{cases} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m  - **Step 2: Solve the system of equations**  
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    We have four equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ d_1 + d_2 = -\frac{3}{5} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ d_1 - d_2 = \frac{6}{5} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Adding / subtracting these equations, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ 2d_1 = 2 \( \frac{3}{5} \) ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ 2d_2 = 2 \( \frac{6}{5} \) ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    So, the possible pairs \((d_1, d_2)\) are:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ (d_1, d_2) = ( \frac{3}{5}, \frac{6}{5} ) \text{ or } ( -\frac{3}{5}, -\frac{6}{5} ) ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ (d_1, d_2) = (1, -1) \text{ or } (-1, 1) ] ( Not valid because \mathbf b\) is orthogonal)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ (d_1, d_2) = (-1, 1) \text{ or } (1, -1) ] ( Not valid because \mathbf b\) is orthogonal)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    But what we will only need is
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ d_1 - d_2 = \frac{6}{5} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - **Step 3: Solve the system**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    We have 2 such solutions:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ (d_1, d_2) = \left( \frac{3}{5}, \frac{6}{5} \right), \left( -\frac{3}{5}, -\frac{6}{5} \right) ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Using the projection formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ \begin{pmatrix} \frac{3}{5} \\ \frac{6}{5} \end{pmatrix} = \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf b} \begin{pmatrix} \frac{3}{5} \\ \frac{6}{5} \end{pmatrix} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ \begin{pmatrix} d_1 \\ d_2 \end{pmatrix} = \frac{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{3}{5} \\ \frac{6}{5} \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}}{\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Expanding the dot products:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ \begin{pmatrix} d_1 \\ d_2 \end{pmatrix} = \frac{\frac{3}{5} - \frac{6}{5}}{\frac{2}{3} - \frac{1}{2}} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Simplifying the "middle" part:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ \begin{pmatrix} d_1 \\ d_2 \end{pmatrix} = \frac{-\frac{3}{5}}{-\frac{1}{6}} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ \begin{pmatrix} d_1 \\ d_2 \end{pmatrix} = \frac{-\frac{3}{5}}{-\frac{1}{6}} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ \begin{pmatrix} d_1 \\ d_2 \end{pmatrix} = 3 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m        Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m        [ d_1 = 3 \cdot 1 = 3 \text{ and } d_2 = 3 \cdot (-1) = -3 ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Substituting these values back into the projection formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ \begin{pmatrix} \frac{3}{5} \\ \frac{6}{5} \end{pmatrix} = \frac{3}{5} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} - 3 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Simplifying:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ \begin{pmatrix} \frac{3}{5} \\ \frac{6}{5} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{3}{5} - 3 \\ -\frac{3}{5} + 3 \end{pmatrix} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ \begin{pmatrix} \frac{3}{5} \\ \frac{6}{5} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{8}{5} \\ \frac{9}{5} \end{pmatrix} ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Conclusion:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [ \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf b} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{8}{5} \\ \frac{9}{5} \end{pmatrix} ]<|endoftext|>
