[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The units digit of the product of the first 50 natural numbers is the same as the units digit of 50!, because a number ends in the units digit of the factorial. Since $50!$ is divisible by 10 (because $50$ is divisible by 5 and 2), the units digit of $50!$ is 0. Therefore, the units digit of the product of all natural numbers from 1 to 99, inclusive, which is $50!$, is also 0.
