[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m What is the slope of the line containing the midpoint of the segment with endpoints at (0, 0) and (2, 2) and the midpoint of the segment with endpoints at (5, 0) and (6, 2)? Express your answer in simplest form.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the slope of line AB*, we first need to find the midpoint,*, and the slope between points A and B*. The midpoint is the average of the x-coordinates of points A and B*, where A has x-coordinate 0 and B has x-coordinate 6:$$\big((6+0)/2, (2+0)/2\big) = (3, 1).$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The slope is the change in y (which is 2) divided by the change in x (which is 2*difference of x-coordinates:$$\frac{2-(0)}{6-0}=\frac{2}{6}=\frac{1}{3}.$$$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m aveled with the slope. Express your answer as a fraction.
