[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To convert the repeating decimal $0.\overline{73}$ into a fraction, we can multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $100$ to shift the decimal point two places to the right (since the repeating decimal repeats every $2$ digits):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
