[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Among the following propositions:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (1) If two lines are parallel to the same line, then these two lines are parallel.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (2) If two lines are perpendicular to the same line, then these two lines are perpendicular.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (3) If two lines are perpendicular to the same line, then these two lines are parallel.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (4) If a dashed line is perpendicular to a straight line, then this dashed line is perpendicular to the straight line.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Which of these propositions are correct? (注:请一次性填写正确的选项序号)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's analyze each proposition one by one:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (1) If two lines are parallel to the same line, then these two lines are parallel.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This proposition is not necessarily true. Two lines can be parallel to the same line without being parallel to each other. They could be skew lines or intersecting lines. For example, two skew lines can be parallel to the same line.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (2) If two lines are perpendicular to the same line, then these two lines are perpendicular.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This proposition is true. If two lines are perpendicular to the same line, then they are parallel. This is because parallel lines maintain a constant distance from each other while never intersecting.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (3) If two lines are perpendicular to the same line, then these two lines are parallel.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This proposition is true. If two lines are perpendicular to the same line, then they are parallel. This is because both lines are parallel to a line, and if two straight lines are parallel to the same line, they must be parallel to each other.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (4) If a dashed line is perpendicular to a straight line, then this dashed line is perpendicular to the straight line.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This proposition is not necessarily true. A dashed line is not a perpendicular to a straight line. It would not be perpendicular to a line that is not a straight line. However, if we restrict the dashed line to be a straight line, then it is indeed perpendicular to the straight line. But without the restriction, it could be perpendicular to any line.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So the correct propositions are (2) and (3).
