[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To compute $\sin(-60^\circ)$, we need to use the subtraction of angles for the sine function.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since $-60^\circ$ is the same as $-90^\circ+30^\circ$,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\sin(-60^\circ)=\sin(-90^\circ+30^\circ)=-\sin30^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We are given that $\sin30^\circ=\frac{1}{2}$,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m so $\sin(-60^\circ)=-\frac{1}{2}$.
