[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To identify the ordered pair \((b, c)\) that makes \((x - 1)^2\) a factor of \(f(x) = x^3 + bx + c\), we need to substitute \(x = 1\) into \(f(x)\). Given that \((x - 1)^2\) is a factor of \(f(x)\), we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
