[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The values of $a$, $b$, $c$ and $d$ are 1, 2, 3 and 4, but not necessarily in that order. What is the largest possible value of the sum of the four products $ab$, $bc$, $cd$ and $da$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We are trying to maximize the product $(ab)(bc)(cd)(da)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since $d=4$, the largest sum of the pairwise products is $56$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We simply apply case switch and cancel like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (\sqrt{2}(a \sqrt{5} + b \sqrt{10} + c \sqrt{15} + d \sqrt{20})) &\leq 20\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (\sqrt{24}(a \sqrt{2} + b \sqrt{3} + c \sqrt{15} + d \sqrt{4})) &= 12\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \therefore\sqrt{6}(a + b + c + d) &= 4\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m a + b + c + d &= 4
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}<|endoftext|>
