[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m URL: https://www.algebra123.com/process/finding-intersection/
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The point at $(a, b)$ on a Cartesian plane is reflected over the  $y$-axis to the point at $(j, k)$. If $a + j = 0$ and $b + k = 0$, what is the value of $b$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please respond by writing a program in Python.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m from sympy import symbols, Eq, solve
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m a, b, j, k = symbols('a b j k')
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # calculate a, b, j, k
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m eq1 = Eq(a + j, 0)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m eq2 = Eq(b + k, 0)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # find the intersection
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # b + 2j = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m eq3 = Eq(b + 2*j, 0)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m solution = solve((eq1, eq3), (a, b, j, k))
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m a_val = solution[a]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m b_val = solution[b]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # calculate k
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m k_val = solve(eq2.subs({a: b_val, b: b_val}), k)[0]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # find the value of b
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m b_val = b_val + k_val
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m print(b_val)<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
