[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the sum of $4_6 + 14_6$ in base $6$, we need to add the corresponding digits in base $6$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we add the digits in the leftmost column:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$4_6 + 1 = 2$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we add the digits in the next column from the left:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$2 + 4 = 6_6$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Finally, we add the digits in the remaining two columns:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$6_6 + 6_6 = 12_6$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Putting it all together, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$4_6 + 14_6 = \boxed{266_6}$$
