[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\*\\*Step 1: Default Reduced form\\\\*\\*
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m As a fraction is $0.\overline{73}$, we can find a common denominator for $0.73$ and $73$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$0.73 = \frac{73}{100}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{\frac{73}{100}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\*\\*Convert $\\frac{73}{100}$ to a mixed number\\\\*\\*
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The fraction $$\frac{73}{100}$$ means that we need to divide 73 by 100:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$73 / 100 = 0.73$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\*\\*Convert $0.73$ back to a fraction\\\\*\\*
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To convert a decimal or a decimal number back to a fraction, we divide the integer part by the denominator. Here, since there is no integer part, we can simply ignore the decimal and divide the denominator by the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$\frac{73}{100} = \frac{73}{100}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
