[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A regular polygon has an exterior angle that measures $15$ degrees. How many sides does the polygon have?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine the number of sides of the polygon, we can use the fact that the sum of an exterior angle of a polygon is always $360$ degrees. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We are given that one exterior angle is $15$ degrees. We can use the formula to find the number of sides of the polygon:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Exterior angle} = \frac{360^\circ}{\text{number of sides}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let \(\text{number of sides}\) be \(n\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 15 = \frac{360}{n}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Solving for \(n\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m n = \frac{360}{15} = 24
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the polygon has \(24\) sides. Therefore, \boxed{24} is the number of sides of the polygon.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 24
