[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m It is now 12:00:00 midnight, as read on a 12-hour digital clock. In 122 hours, 39 minutes and 44 seconds the time will be $A:B:C$. What is the value of $A + B + C$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the time 122 hours, 39 minutes, and 44 seconds, we can start by breaking down the problem into smaller steps.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we can find the time of the 122nd hour by finding the remainder when 122 is divided by 60:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 122 \mod 60 = 52 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the time 122 hours is actually 32 minutes.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we can find the time of the seconds by finding the remainder when 44 seconds is divided by 60:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 44 \mod 60 = 44 \text{ (since } 44 < 60\text{)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the time started at 18:044.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the whole number part of 122 hours, 39 minutes, and 44 seconds, we add the remainders together:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ (32 + 39 + 44) \mod 60 = 115 \mod 60 = 55 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the time in 122 hours, 39 minutes, and 44 seconds is $55 \text{ hours} + 0 \text{ minutes} + 44 \text{ seconds}$, which is exactly when the digit '0' is replaced by '5', by convention.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So the time is $55:10:44$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Finally, the value of $A + B + C$ is $55 + 10 + 44$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
