[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Find $p+q$, given that $(q+4)(p+3)-(q+2)(p+1)=44$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m When solving this type of problem, we need to rewrite the given equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $(q+4)(p+3)-(q+2)(p+1)=44$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $p^2+3p+4q+12-q^2-7q-q-2=44$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $p^2+q^2+3p+4q-4q-2q+24=44$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $(p^2+p^2)+(q^2+q^2)+(4q-q)+(24-2)+q-1=44$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $2p^2+2q^2+3q+22=44$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $2p^2+2q^2+3q-22=44$(By Subtracting $22$ from both sides of the equation)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $n(p+q)=2(p^2+q^2+3q-q-22)$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $2(p^2+q^2-10q-22)=44$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\mathbf{p=p}+q$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $2p+q-10q-22=11$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $2p-9q-22=11$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $2p=9q+33$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\mathbf{p(p+1)=9(q+1)}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\boxed{q(q+1)=9((p+1)−1)}$
