[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} a_1 \\ a_2 \\ a_3 \end{pmatrix},$ where $a_1^2 + a_2^{\text{2}} + a_3^2 = 1,$ and $\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} b_1 \\ b_2 \\ b_3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a_1 - 1 \\ a_2 - 4 \\ a_3 - 6\end{pmatrix}.$  Note that
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\begin{aligned} \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} &= \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ a_1 & a_2 & a_3 \\ b_1 & b_2 & b_3 \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ a_1 & a_2 & a_3 \\ b_1 & b_2 & b_3 \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} a_2 b_3 - a_3 b_2 \\ a_3 b_1 - a_1 b_3 \\ a_1 b_2 - a_2 b_1 \end{pmatrix} \end{aligned}\]Finally,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\mathbf{c} \cdot (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}) = \begin{vmatrix} 2 & -7 & -10 \\ a_1 - 1 & a_2 - 4 & a_3 - 6 \\ a_1 & a_2 & a_3 \end{vmatrix} = 2(a_2 - 4)(a_3 - 6) - (-7)(a_1 - 1)(a_3 - 6) + (-10)(a_1 - 1)(a_2 - 4)\]
