[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Yes. $g(x)$ can be defined as follows: 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$g(x)= \begin{cases} [f(x)]^2 & \text{if }f(x) \geq 0 \quad \text{and } [f(x)] \leq2 \\ [f(x)]^2 & \text{otherwise}\end{cases}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the range of $g(x),$ we need to consider different cases based on the values of $f(x).$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Case 1: $f(x) \geq 0$ and $[f(x)] \leq 2$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In this case, $g(x)$ is defined as $[f(x)]^2.$ Since $f(x) \geq 0,$ it follows that $[f(x)] \geq 3.$ Thus, $g(x) \geq 9.$ Also, $[f(x)] \leq 2.$ Therefore, $g(x) \leq 4.$ Conclude that $g(x) \in [3,4].$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Case 2: $f(x) \geq 0$ and $f(x) \leq -3$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In this case, since $[f(x)] \geq 0,$ it follows that $[f(x)] \in [0,3].$ Thus, $[f(x)]^2 \in [0,9].$ Here, we have 6 possible values of $g(x),$ which are: 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $g(0) \in [0,4]$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $g(-3) \in [9,16]$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $g(-2) \in [4,9]$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $g(-1) \in [9,16]$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $g(2) \in [9,16]$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $g(3) \in [9,16]$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, consider the case where $[f(x)] = 0.$ Since $[f(x)] \in [0,3],$ it follows that $f(x) = 0.$ Thus, $g(x) = 9.$ 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Case 3: $f(x) < 0$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In this case, since $[f(x)] < 0,$ it follows that $[f(x)]^2 < 0.$ Further, since $f(x) < 0,$ it follows that $[f(x)] \in [-3,5].$ Thus, $g(x) \leq 0.$ So, from this case, we have $g(x) \in [-3,0].$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Combining all the different cases, we notice that there are 6 possible values of $g(x),$ 4 of which are achievable. Furthermore, since $g(x)$ achieves all possible values in $[-3, 6],$ we conclude that the range of $g(x),$ $[-3,6],$ is achieved. $\blacksquare$
