[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m What is the value of $x + y + z$ when $6x + 5y - 2z = -4$ and $4x + 5y + 12z = 54$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the value of $x + y + z$, we can use the method of elimination. We have the following two equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6x + 5y - 2z &= -4 \quad \text{(1)}\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4x + 5y + 12z &= 54 \quad \text{(2)}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we can subtract equation (1) from equation (2) to eliminate the $y$ term:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $(4x + 5y + 12z) - (6x + 5y - 2z) = 54 - (-4)$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4x + 5y + 12z - 6x - 5y + 2z &= 54 + 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m -x + 14z &= 58
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we have a new equation $-x + 14z = 58$. To solve for $x$, we can multiply this equation by -1:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $-x - 14z = -58$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we add this equation to equation (1) to eliminate $x$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $(6x + 5y - 2z) + (-x - 14z) = -4 + (-58)$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6x + 5y - 2z - x - 14z &= -58 - 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5x + 5y - 16z &= -62 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, since we know $-x - 14z = -58$, we can substitute this into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $5x + 5y - 16z = 58$ will cancel out with $-58$, leaving us with an equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $5x + 5y = 76$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Finally, we find the value of $x + y + z$ by solving for $x + y$ where $x + y = 76 - 14z$. Substitute this back into the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $x + y + z = (76 - 14z) + 14z + z$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $x + y + z = 76 + 2z$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we substitute back into our system of equations to find a relationship between $x$ and $z$. We have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $6x + 5y - 2z = -4$ (subtract equation (3) from (2)) or $(6x - (x + 14z)) + 5y - 16z = -4 - 58$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $x - 14z = -62$ (from equation 1)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we substitute $x - 14z = -62$ into the equation for $x + y + z$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $x + y + z = 76 - 14z + 14z + 62 = 76 + 62 = 138$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the value of $x + y + z$ is $\boxed{138}$.<|endoftext|>
