[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the smallest integer $x$ that satisfies the inequality $x < 2x - 7$, let's first rearrange it into a single equation with just one variable:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x < 2x - 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, isolate $x$ on one side of the inequality equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x - 2x < -7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -x < -7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, multiply both sides of this inequality by $-1$ to ensure the direction of the inequality stays the same:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x > 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the smallest integer that makes the inequality true is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x = 8 \]
