[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, let's compute the powers of the matrix $A$. To do this, we need to compute $A^2$, $A^3$, and so on.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A^2 &= A \cdot A \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= \begin{pmatrix}\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}&0&-\frac{1}{2}\\ 0&-1&0\\ \frac{1}{2}&0&\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix}\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}&0&-\frac{1}{2}\\ 0&-1&0\\ \frac{1}{2}&0&\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\end{pmatrix} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= \begin{pmatrix}\frac{3}{4} & \frac{1}{2} & -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}\\ \frac{1}{4} & \frac{1}{2} & -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\\ \frac{1}{4}& \frac{1}{2} & \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}\end{pmatrix}
