[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find $13^{51}$ modulo 5, we can use the pattern of powers of a small prime to simplify the calculation. Since $13^5 \mod 5 = 32 \mod 5 = 2$ (since $13 \equiv 3 \mod 5$), and $13^2 \equiv 49 \mod 5 \equiv 4 \mod 5$ (since $49 \equiv -1 \mod 5$), we see that the powers of 13 repeat every 2. So, $13^{51} \equiv 13^{3 \cdot 17 + 4} \equiv (13+4)^{3 \cdot 17} \equiv 01^{3 \cdot 17} \equiv 4^3 \equiv 64 \mod 5$ (since $01 \equiv 4$). Therefore, the remainder when $13^{51}$ is divided by 5 is $\boxed{4}$.
