[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we'll use the property of the absolute value of a complex number, \(|z| = \frac{\sqrt{z_1^2 + z_2^2}}{z}\) for any complex numbers \(z_1\) and \(z_2\). Here, we calculate \(|\frac{-256 - 448i}{2 - 6i}|\) as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \left|\frac{-256 - 448i}{2 - 6i}\right| = \frac{|-256 - 448i|}{|2 - 6i|} = \sqrt{(-256)^2 + (-448)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we delve into the modulus of the expression \(-256 - 448i\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m |-256 - 448i|^2 = (-256)^2 + (-448)^2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m And the modulus of the complex number \(2 - 6i\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m |2 - 6i| = \sqrt{2^2 + (-6)^2} = \sqrt{4 + 36} = \sqrt{40} = 2\sqrt{10}
