[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m How many four-digit positive integers have at least one digit that is a 2 or a 3?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find how many four-digit positive integers have at least one digit that is either 2 or 3, we can use the principle of inclusion-exclusion. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, let's define:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Let \( A \) be the set of all positive integers where each digit is either 2 or 3. (This means all four-digit numbers can be represented as \( \overline{ABC222} \), or \( \overline{XYZ333} \), or \( \overline{DEFCCCC} \), etc., where \( 0 \leq A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J \leq 9 \). Hence, the total number of elements in \( A \) is \(9 \times 8 \times 8 \times 8\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Let \( B \) be the set of four-digit numbers where at least one digit is a 2 or a 3. ( Then \( B = A + (9 \times 8 \times 8) - 1 \dfrac{3 \times 4}{2 \times 3} ( \sim23 ) \times 8 \times 8 \). Since there are 1000 such numbers (8 digits in each of 23 places), a total of \( 9 \times 8 \times 8 \times 8 \) numbers; hence \( B = 18000 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Let \( C \) be the set of four-digit numbers where at least two digits are a 2 or a 3. (This means \( C = B + (9 \times 8 \times 8) + 9 \times 8 \times 8 + 9 \times 8 \times 8 - 1 \dfrac{3 \times 4}{2 \times 3} ( 23 \times 9 \times 8 )\), \( \sim27 \times 9 \times 8 \), etc.). Hence, \( C = 63000 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Let \( D \) be the set of four-digit numbers where at least three digits are a 2 or a 3. (this means \( D = C + (9 \times 8 \times 8) + 9 \times 8 \times 8 - 1 \dfrac{3 \times 4}{2 \times 3} ( 23 \times 9 \times 8) - 1 \dfrac{3 \times 4}{2 \times 3} ( 23 \times 9 \times 8) \)), \( \( \sim27 \times 9 \times 8 \), etc.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m  Hence, \( D = 42000 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Let \( E \) be the set of four-digit numbers where at least four digits are a 2 or a 3. (This means \( E = D + (9 \times 8 \times 8) + 9 \times 8 \times 8 - 1 \dfrac{3 \times 4}{2 \times 3} ( 23 \times 9 \times 8) - 1 \dfrac{3 \times 4}{2 \times 3} ( 23 \times 9 \times 8) \)). Hence, \( E = 16800 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Then, the number of four-digit positive integers having at least one number that is either 2 or 3 is \( N = 18000 + 63000 - 42000 - 10500 = 48000 - 30000 = 18000 \).<|endoftext|>
