[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let the three consecutive positive prime numbers be denoted as \(a - (a+2) = n\), \(a - (a+4) = m\), and \(a - (a+6) = p\). 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m From the problem statement, we have the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ a - (a+2) + m + p = 3n + m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 2 - a + m + p = 3n + m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 2 - a = 3n \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ a = 3n - 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substitute \(a = 3n - 2\) into the first equation so we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ (3n - 3) + p = 3n + m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ p = 3m - 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since \(n\), \(m\), and \(p\) are all prime numbers, \(3m - 3\) must be a prime number and \(2 - a\), \(m\), and \(p\) can each be multiplied by 2 to get another prime number. Thus, the only prime numbers we can multiply by \(2\) are \(2\) itself or \(4\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ p = 2 \cdot 3m - 6 = 2(3m - 3) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m By checking the first few prime numbers, we find that \(a = 3 \cdot 2 - 2 = 4\) works but \(3m - 3\) must be prime as well. That gives us \(m = 4\) and \(3 \cdot 4 - 3 = 12\) which must be prime, so that \(p = 2 \cdot 4 = 8 = 2^3\), giving \(4 + 8 + 4 = 16\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m By checking further numbers for prime \(a\), we find that \(a = 2 \cdot 3 - 2 = 4\), \(m = 2\), and \(3m - 3 = 9\) which must be prime, so we get \(p = 2^3 = 8\), giving \(4 + 8 + 4 = 22\), which is incorrect, so we need to look at larger pruples. Since we are only interested in the one sequential prime number solution ruled out during checking, letting's just verify by code.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m By checking the first few primes, only one 7 is available primes, such as \(a = 8941\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 2 - a = -608 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 8941 = 2(3 \cdot 3 \cdot 7) - (2 \cdot \sqrt{7} - 1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This matches to being a prime number and satisfies the condition.
