[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine how long it will take Casey's shop to paint 300 dimples, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. **Calculate the total number of dimples needed:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - However, since we are given that it takes 2 seconds to paint one dimple, we need to find out how many seconds are needed to paint 300 dimples.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \text{Total time in seconds} = 300 \text{ dimples} \times 2 \text{ seconds/dimple} = 600 \text{ seconds}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. **Convert the total time from seconds to minutes:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - We know that there are 60 seconds in a minute.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \text{Total time in minutes} = \frac{600 \text{ seconds}}{60 \text{ seconds/minute}} = 10 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, Casey needs \boxed{10} minutes to paint 300 dimples with 2 seconds per dimple.<|endoftext|>
