[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Anna, Beth, and Corey combine all their cars to sell them for breakfast. If Anna has 34 cars, Beth has 5 more than half as many as Anna, and Corey has 16 less than three times as many as Beth, what is the total number of cars they will have to sell?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Anna has 34 cars.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Beth has 5 more than half as many cars as Anna, so Beth has (1/2) * 34 - 5 = 16 cars.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Corey has 16 less than three times as many cars as Beth, so Corey has 3 * 16 - 16 = 48 cars.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The total number of cars they will have to sell is 34 + 16 + 48 = 108 cars.
