[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Find the units digit of $1! + 2! + 3! + 4! + \ldots + 50!$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The units digits that can be obtained by $n!$ are 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 and 11. The units digits of $1!+10! = 9190 + 9199 \ldots + \infty$ become 1, 89, 881, 8881 \ldots. After the first repeating block of 89, all other blocks are 90, 91, 92, ... and 99. Because there are two 8-digit sequences each of 100, there are 200 such blocks. Therefore, the units digit of the sum is $(89+881+90+91+92+ \ldots+99+89) + 2 \times 200$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The sum of the first 100 units digits after 1!+100! is $1+89+881+ \ldots + 100 = (1+99)(1+88+90+\ldots+91+92+93) = 100 \times 8190+91988 \times 2 = 839000+183976 = 1022976$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the units digit of $1!+2!+3!+ \ldots +50!$ is $\boxed{9}$.ozilla@gmail<|endoftext|>
