[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. **Derivative and Sign Change:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Consider how the polynomial \( x^n + x^{n-1} + \dots + x + 1 \) behaves for \( -1 < x < 1 \). These roots are points where the polynomial attains its maximum/(true maximum) value. To find the sign of the function, look at the first and last derivatives or simply examine the polynomial's sign behavior.
