[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the length of \( AB \) in the given isosceles triangle \( \triangle ABC \), we'll reason step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. **Understand the properties of an isosceles triangle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - In an isosceles triangle, the two base angles are equal, and the base angles sum up to \(180^\circ\). Here, \( \angle ABC = \angle ACB \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
