[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, let's observe that \(-3737\) is an odd number because it is negative. We can rewrite our division to be positive:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m -3737 \div 8 \text{ gives}\qquad
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (-3737 + 2614) \div 8 = \frac{-3737}{8} + 363
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we need to determine the remainder when \( -3737 \) (which is \( 36! \)) is divided by \( 8 \). \( 36! \), when divided by \( 8 \), will give a remainder of \( 0 \) (since \( 36 \) is divisible by \( 8 \) and higher powers of \( 8 \) are divisible).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Hence,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (-3737 + 2614) \div 8 = (-1623) \div 8
