[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Certainly, I can help with that.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's start by finding the roots of the polynomial $x^2 + 7x - 2 = 0$. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We can use the quadratic formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m • \begin{equation*}\label{eq:quadratic} \alpha = \,{-b \over a}\,,\qquad \beta = \,{c\over\alpha}\,,\end{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m where $a = 1, b = 7, c = -2$. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Plugging these into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m • \begin{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \alpha = - {\textstyle\frac{7}1} = -7\,,\qquad\quad\beta = {\textstyle\frac{-2}0} = \infty
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, let's find $\alpha^2 + \beta^2$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m • \begin{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \alpha = -7\quad\quad\quad\quad\alpha^2 = (-7)^2 = 49\,,\qquad\quad\quad\quad\quad\end{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m • \begin{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \beta = \infty\,,\qquad\quad\beta^2 = (\infty)^2 = \infty\,.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Combining these results, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m • \begin{equation*}\begin{aligned}\alpha^2 + \beta^2 &= 49 + \infty\,\\ & = \infty\,.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{aligned}\end{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the value of $\alpha^2 + \beta^2$ is $\boxed{\infty}$. Enjoy the problem!
