[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, to find the total number of ways, we multiply the number of ways to go through each step:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4 \text{ ways (select female lead)} \times 4 \text{ ways (select male lead)} \times 1 \text{ (select animal)} = 16
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the number of ways to assign the roles for one female lead, one male lead, and three different objects is \boxed{16}. indebted to the stack platforms for the use of the bot.
