[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Evaluate $$\lfloor\sqrt{1}\rfloor + \lfloor\sqrt{2}\rfloor + \lfloor\sqrt{3}\rfloor + .... + \lfloor\sqrt{19}\rfloor$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To evaluate the provided sum, we need to consider the "floor" function which returns the greatest integer less than or equal to its argument. The problem then becomes related to the properties of the "floor" function.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Firstly, observe the sequence $$\require{stack} \frac{1}{\frak l\sqrt{1}}, \frac{1}{\frak l\sqrt{2}}, ...,\frac{1}{\frak l\sqrt{19}}$$ (denoted as $S$ \[$\]$ later on).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Step 1** : Identify the properties of the "floor" function
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Take an arbitrary number $$x\in\mathbb{R}^+$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m for any real number $$x$$, the value of $$\lfloor x \rfloor$$ is equal to at most the greatest integer less than or equal to $$x$$. For other values of the number $$x$$, the "floor" function can flip.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Examples are:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $$\lfloor x \rfloor \leq x \leq \lfloor x \rfloor + 1$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $$\lfloor x \rfloor \geq x$$ 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $$\lfloor x \rfloor = 0$$ 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $$\lfloor x \rfloor = 1$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In fact, $x = 1$ is the only possible value for the floor function $\lfloor x \rfloor = x$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Step 2** : Consider the sum $S$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Due to the "floor" values flipping action,  
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\begin{eqnarray*} \sum_{k=1}^{11} \lfloor k\sqrt{11} \rfloor &=&\sum_{k=1}^{11} \lfloor \sqrt{11}\rfloor \\ &=& 8 \end{eqnarray*}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m And  
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\begin{eqnarray*} \sum_{k=1}^{10} \lfloor k\sqrt{10} \rfloor &=&\sum_{k=1}^{10} \lfloor \sqrt{10}\rfloor \\ &=& 9 \end{eqnarray*}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Hence, combined,  
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\begin{eqnarray*} S =& 8 + 9 \\ =& 17 \end{eqnarray*}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Wrap this up as: 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\boxed{17}$<|endoftext|>
