[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m After eating lunch together, Jay and Paul start walking in opposite directions. Jay walks 0.75 miles every 15 minutes and Paul power walks 2.5 miles every 30 minutes. In miles, how far apart are they after 1.5 hours?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 1: Determine the number of minutes in half an hour.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1.5 hours = 90 minutes (since 1.5 hours = 3 halves of an hour).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 2: Determine the speed of each person.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Jay walks 0.75 miles every 15 minutes, so his speed is \frac{0.75}{\frac{15}{60}}=0.6 \, \text{miles per minute}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Paul power walks 2.5 miles every 30 minutes, so his speed is \frac{2.5}{\frac{30}{60}}=2.2 \, \text{miles per minute}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 3: Calculate the distance each person covers in half an hour.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Jay's distance: 0.6 \, \text{miles per minute} \times 90 \, \text{minutes} = 54 \, \text{miles}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Paul's distance: 2.2 \, \text{miles per minute} \times 90 \, \text{minutes} = 198 \, \text{miles}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 4: Calculate the net distance between Jay and Paul after half an hour.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m After 1.5 hours, they have each traveled for 90 minutes. So,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Jay's distance after 1.5 hours: 0.6 \, \text{miles per minute} \times 90 \, \text{minutes} = 54 \, \text{miles}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Paul's distance after 1.5 hours: 2.2 \, \text{miles per minute} \times 90 \, \text{minutes} = 210 \, \text{miles}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, the net distance between them:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Net distance = Distance of Jay after 1.5 hours + Distance of Paul after 1.5 hours - Distance not considered by Jay or Paul (i.e., distance between yourselves)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Effortless calculus (since these calculations are just mathematical ratios, and I'll leave it to you to write the rest!) would have been:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Distance separated after 1.5 hours = 54 - 210 - (0.6 + 2.2) = 54 - 210 - 8.8 = -175.8 \, \text{miles}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This indicates they'd be 175.8 miles apart, reversing which half they've been walking with due to their speed difference, reaching out, and perfect for a delta sign summing.
