[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. **Check for corresponding \( \pi(k) - k + 1 \):** We will manually check the value of each \( N \) to see if there are corresponding dominos that contain only the digit 9. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's implement the code to verify the correct answer for \( N = 50 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m import sympy as sp
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m def count_numbers_with_digit_n_in_h(H, digit_n):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     count = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     for i in range(1, H+1):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m         divisors = sp.divisors(i)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m         valid_indices = [d for d in divisors if (i-1) % d == 0]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m         if len(valid_indices) >= digit_n:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m             count += count_numbers_with_digit_n_in_h(i, digit_n - len(valid_indices))
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     return count
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m H = 50
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m count = count_numbers_with_digit_n_in_h(H, 1)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m print("Count of numbers containing only the digit 9:", count)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```
