[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If $4u-5v=23$ and $2u+4v=-8$, find the value of $u+v$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We have $4u-5v=23$ and $2u+4v=-8$. We will use these to find $u+v$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $4u-5v=23$ so $(2u-5v)+(3u-4v)+(u-8v)=23+3u-20-u=23-u$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m And $2u+4v=-8$ so $2u+2-8v=-8-8-u=-8-u-8-u=-16-u$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So we have $23-u=-16-u$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplifying the left-hand side and right-hand side, we get $23-u=-16-u$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Moving $u$ to the left-hand side and $-u$ to the right-hand side, we get $23=16$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now $u=u$ is so $u=3$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substituting $u=3$ into either equation, we have $4(3)-7(5)=23$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplifying, we get $12-35=-23$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Then $-13=-23$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substituting $-13=3$ into our equation, we simplify to $3(3)+4v=-8$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Moving $3$ over to the left-hand side, we get $3+4v=-8$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Moving $-8$ over to the left-hand side, we get $3=4v-8$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Adding $8$ to both sides, we get $11=4v$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Dividing both sides by $4$, we get $4=v$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the solution is $u+v=3+4=\boxed{7}$.Ⴢ
