[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Find the sum of all angles $x \in [0^\circ, 360^\circ]$ that satisfy
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\sin^5 x - \cos^5 x = \frac{1}{\cos x} - \frac{1}{\sin x}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Rewrite the equation as $\sin x - \cos x = \sqrt[4]{3}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Substitute $\cos x$ with $\sqrt[4]{3} - \sin x$ to obtain
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[(\sin x - \cos x)^2 = (\sqrt[4]{3} - \sin x)(\sqrt[4]{3} - \cos x).\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Simplify further to get
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\sin x - \cos x = \sqrt{3} \left(\sqrt[4]{3} - \frac{(\sqrt[4]{3} - \sin x)(\sqrt[4]{3} - \cos x)}{(\sqrt[4]{3} - \sin x)(\sqrt[4]{3} - \cos x)}\right) + \frac{\sin (2k\pi|x|-x )}{(\sqrt[4]{3} - \sin x)(\sqrt[4]{3} - \cos x)}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. As $\sin (n\pi|x| - x ) = 0$, $\sin x$ has only one solution.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. Apply the identity $2k\pi|x| - x = 2k\pi x$ for each $k \in \mathbb{Z}$ to obtain
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\sin x - \cos x = \sqrt{3} \left(\sqrt[4]{3} - \frac{(\sqrt[4]{3} - \sin x)(\sqrt[4]{3} - \cos x)}{(\sqrt[4]{3} - \sin x)(\sqrt[4]{3} - \cos x)}\right).\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6. Simplify the second term to get
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\sin x - \cos x = \sqrt{3} \left(\sqrt[4]{3} - \frac{(\sqrt[4]{3} - \sin x)(\sqrt[4]{3} - \cos x)}{(\sqrt[4]{3} - \sin x)(\sqrt[4]{3} - \cos x)}-\frac{\sin (2x - x )}{(\sqrt[4]{3} - \sin x)(\sqrt[4]{3} - \cos x)}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 7. Finally, use the fact that $\cos (n\pi x - x ) = (\sqrt[4]{3} - \sin x)(\sqrt[4]{3} - \cos x)$ to expand the second term.
