[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m n/2/6 = 4<sup>1/2</sup>, because from any vertex, we can systematically end 4 triangles.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m However, since the dimensions of convex octagons can differ, the greatest number of interior right angles a convex octagon can have is:
