[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. After the goalie is chosen, we need to choose a starting team of 7 players. We can then choose 6 positions out of the remaining 14 players, where each position occupies one position.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. The number of ways to choose positions is given by the number of permutations of 6 out of 14, which is 14! (14 factorial). Evaluating 14!, we get 87,777,576.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Finally, we find the number of ways to choose the remaining 6 players from the 14 players by subtracting the number of ways to choose the goalie and the 6 starting positions from 14!.
