[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given that $k$ is a positive integer less than 6, how many values can $k$ take on such that $3x \equiv k \pmod{6}$ has no solutions in $x$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's consider all possible values of $k$ such that $k$ is a positive integer less than 6. So, $k$ can be 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5. Now we need to find the values that make $3x \equiv k \pmod{6}$ have no solutions in $x$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Any $3x$ that is congruent to $k \pmod{6}$ meaning any number $3x$ that changes $k \pmod{6}$. Let's analyze the cases for $k$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x=k\pmod{6} & \quad \textrm{if}~k \equiv 0~\pmod 6 \noindent\text{(which is impossible)}\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x=6k \pmod{6} &\xrightarrow{x=6y \pmod{6}}\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x=5z-1 \pmod{6} & \quad \textrm{if} -4\leq 6y-1<6-1\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x=5z \pmod{6} & \quad \textrm{if} -4<6y<6\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We shall analyze each case:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x=k \pmod{6} & \quad \textrm{factor way:}~~0-(-1) ~~ 3-0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \quad \textrm{exist for } k=3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x=6k \pmod{6} &\xrightarrow{x=6y \pmod{6}}\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x=0 \pmod{6}~\,\textrm{or}~x=12 \pmod{6}~\,\textrm{which is impossible} \\[5pt]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x=5z-1 \pmod{6} & \quad \textrm{factor way:}~~0-1 \noindent\vspace{3mm}\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x=3z \pmod{6} &\xrightarrow{x=6w \pmod{6}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x\neq 3 \textrm{ and happen -1 whenever $z \\equiv 0~\textrm{or}~z \\equiv -1~\textrm{mod6} }
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If $k=0$, $x=60\equiv 4\pmod{6}$, sary has no solution with $x=6y\pmod{6}$. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If $k=6n+1$, $x=6n+1*1\equiv1\pmod{6}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we multiply them to conclude.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The required values are the ones we get $\{1,5\}$.
