[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The product $(x + i)((x + 1) + i)((x + 2) + i)$ is pure imaginary when the degrees of the three factors are equal (i.e. when $x = -i$, $x = -1 - i$, or $x = -2 - i$).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ▹$-i$ gives $(x + i)((x + 1) + i)((x + 2) + i) = \left(x - i\right) \left(x + 1 + i\right) \left(x + 2 + i\right).$ These factors are even, and have degree 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ▹To simplify, cross out the factors with degree$<2$from the sum.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ▹Since the sum of the cubics has degree $2$, the remaining cubics have degrees $3$ all the same, so they have degree 4.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ▹Thus, the original equation has degree 4, which implies that $x = -i$, $x = -1 - i$, or $x = -2 - i$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ▹$\boxed{{-i}, -1 - i, -2 - i}$
