[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If $f(x)=\frac{x^5-1}3$, find $f^{-1}(-31/96)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Recall that $f(x)$ is an inverse of $y=f^{-1}(x)$ when $$f(f^{-1}(x))=x\\f(f^{-1}(f^{-1}(x))=x$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m so $$f(f^{-1}(x))=f(f^{-1}(f^{-1}(x))$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's start by applying $f(f^{-1}(x))=x$, we can rewrite it to $$f(x)=\frac{x^5-1}3$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplify it, we get $$\frac{\left(\frac{x}{3}\right)^3-1}3$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Then $$\frac{x^3-\left(\frac{x}{3}+1 \right)^3}3$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Distribute and combine. $$\frac{(x^3)-3x^3+3x^3-1}{3}=\frac{x^3-1}{3}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Divide the numerator by the denominator and simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $${1 \over 3}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Divide the numerator by the denominator and simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $${3 \over 1}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. If $${1 \over 3}=3$$, divide the numerator by the denominator and simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$3-1=2=2$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m inx
