[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m What is the tens digit in the sum $7! + 8! + 9! + \cdots + 2006!$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let’s start by expressing each factorial from $n$ to $2006$ as the product of the natural numbers $1$, $2$, ... $n$. This means we can express $n!$ as $n(n-1)(n-2)\cdots 2\cdots 1$. Hence for $n \leq 2006$, 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[7! + 8! + 9! + \cdots + 2006! = \sum_{n=7}^{2006} n! \tag{1}\] 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Taking $e$ as the natural number 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[7! + 8! + 9! + \cdots + 2006! = \sum_{n=1}^{2006} e^n. \tag{2}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The expression 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[e^n = \frac{e^{n \cdot 1!} - 1}{1!}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m for $n \geq 2$ has a well-known closed-form solution for $n \geq 2$, 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[e^n = \frac{1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3\cdots(1+e)-1 \cdot 2\cdots e}{e} = \frac{2 \cdots (1+e)-1 \cdot 1}{e}=\frac{2 \cdots (m \cdot 1-m \cdot 1)+1 \cdot 2-\frac{1 \cdot 1+1}{2}}e = \ldots= \frac{2 \cdots 1999 + 2 \cdots 2005}{e}. \tag{3}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m And further 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[e^2 = \frac{e^4 - 2 e^2 + 1}{e}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Moreover, 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m when $e \geq 5$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[e^4-2 e^2+4 \geq 5^4-2 \cdot 5^2+4 = 1 \geq 5.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, by Cardano inversion formula, 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[e^2 = \sum_{n=1985}^{2006} e^n\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\sum_{n=1}^{2006} e^n = \sum_{n=1985}^{2006} e^n + 1 = e^{2005} + 1,\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m track our solution, and put your answer within \boxed{{}}.accoption, what is the tens digit in the sum $7! + 8! + 9! + \cdots + 2006!?$
