[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve the equation $x(x+10) = 10(-10-x)$, we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Expand the equation. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The given equation is: $x(x+10) = 10(-10-x)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Distribute the multiplication and simplify the equation. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Distribute the $x$ on the left side: $x^2 + 10x = -100 - 10x$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Combine like terms: $x^2 + 10x = -110 - 10x$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Move all terms to one side of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Move all terms to the right side by adding $10x$ to both sides: $x^2 + 20x = -110$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Rewrite the new equation in standard form.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Move the term on the left side to the right by subtracting 20x: $x^2 = 110$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. Solve for $x$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Take the square root of both sides: $x = \pm\sqrt{110}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6. Write the solution in the required format.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
