[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m While watching a parade I saw some clowns and horses. I counted 30 legs and 10 heads. How many horses did I see in the parade?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 1: We know that one animal has one head. Therefore, we can denote the heads of all animals as H = 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 2: We know that one animal has three legs. Therefore, we can denote the legs of all animals as L = 30.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 3: We know there are 10 heads and 30 legs in the parade. We can use the fact that animals on the parade are either horses or clowns, so we can denote the number of horses as H and the number of clowns as C.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 4: There are 10 heads, so we have the equation: H + C = 10 (1)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 5: There are 30 legs, so we have the equation: 3H + C = 30 (2).
