[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m An equilateral triangle and a square are inscribed in a circle as shown. $ABC$ is isosceles. The triangle and square share a common vertex. What is the number of degrees in the measure of the angle indicated by the question mark?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m import markers; defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G;
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m draw(unitcircle);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A=(-1,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m B=(0,-1);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m C=(1,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m D=(0,1);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
