[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, let's rewrite the logarithms by using the change of base formula.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \log_y{x} &= \frac{\log_{10}x}{\log_{10}y} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \log_{x^5}{y^2} &= \frac{\log_5x^2}{\log_5y^2} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \log_{y^4}{x^3} &= \frac{\log_2x^3}{\log_2y^4} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \log_{x^3}{y^4} &= \frac{\log_3x^4}{\log_3y^4} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \log_{y^2}{x^5} &= \frac{\log_2x^5}{\log_2y^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we can rewrite the given expression using the simplification steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m a\cdot\frac{\log_{10}x}{\log_{10}y} \cdot \frac{\log_5x^2}{\log_5y^2} \cdot \frac{\log_2x^3}{\log_2y^4} \cdot \frac{\log_3x^4}{\log_3y^4} \cdot \frac{\log_2x^5}{\log_2y^2} &= a\cdot\frac{\log_10x}{\log_10y} \cdot \frac{\log_5x^5}{\log_5y^5} \cdot \frac{\log_2x^7}{\log_2y^7} \cdot \frac{\log_3x^9}{\log_3y^9} \cdot \frac{\log_2x^{10}}{\log_2y^{10}} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= a\cdot\frac{\log_5x}{\log_5y} \cdot \frac{\log_2x}{\log_2y} \cdot \frac{\log_{10}x}{\log_{10}y} \cdot \frac{\log_3x}{\log_3y} \cdot \frac{\log_{10}x}{\log_{10}y} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= a\log_x{x^{\frac{2}{\log_2y}}}\cdot\frac{\log_{10}x}{\log_{10}y} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= a\cdot\frac{2\log_{10}x}{\log_{10}y}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Comparing this with the expression $a\log_y{x}$, we can see that $a=2\log_{10}x$.
