[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The first link is efficient (fast), because the first node sends data to other nodes without waiting for the communication to complete. The second link is efficient (fast), because the receiving node receives data without waiting for the sending node to send data. The third link is inefficient (slow), because the third node is not sending any data yet. The fourth link is inefficient (slow), because the fourth node is not receiving any data at this moment. The fifth link is efficient (fast), because the fifth node is transferring data as soon as it receives any data. This sequence of attacks form an undirected tree.
