[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $f(m,1) = f(1,n) = 1$ for $m \geq 1, n \geq 1,$ and let $f(m,n) = f(m-1,n) + f(m,n-1) + f(m-1,n-1)$ for $m > 1$ and $n > 1.$  Also, let
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$S(k) = \sum_{a+b=k} f(a,b), \text{ for } a \geq 1, b \geq 1.$$Note: The summation notation means to sum over all positive integers $a,b$ such that $a+b=k.$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given that
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$S(k+2) = pS(k+1) + qS(k) \text{ for all } k \geq 2,$$for some constants $p$ and $q$, find $pq.$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
