[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's solve the system step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Adding all three equations, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}(x+y-z)+(x-y+z)+(x+y-z) &= -8+18+30 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \implies 3(x+y-z) &= 40 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \implies x+y-z &= \frac{40}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we can substitute $x+y-z$ with $\displaystyle \frac{40}{3}$ into one of the original equations.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's use the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}x+y-z &= -8 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \implies x+y &= -8 + z
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substituting this into the third equation, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}-8 + z - z + z - (-8 + z) &= 30 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \implies -8 + z - 8 + z &= 30 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \implies -16 &= 30 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This equation is clearly false, so there must be an error in our assumption. Instead, we should solve for $x, y,$ and $z$ individually.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m From the first and fourth equations, we can easily solve for $x$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}x+y+z &= -8 + 30 = 22 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x &= 7  \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m From the second equation, we can solve for $y$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}x-y+z &= -8 + 18 - (-8 + z) = 18 - (-8 + z)  \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \implies 7 - z &= 26 - z \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \implies -19 &= z \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we can substitute the values of $x,y,$ and $z$ into the equation $x+y-z = \frac{40}{3}$ and solve for $z$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}\frac{40}{3} &= \frac{40}{3} + \frac{40}{3} - \frac{19}{3} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \implies z &= -1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So the values are $x=7,$ $y=-1,$ and $z=-1$. Now we can find $xyz$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}7(-1)(-1)(-1) &= -7 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the final answer is $\boxed{-7}$..FormStartPositionsystem<|endoftext|>
