[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Compute $\tan 75^\circ.$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 1: write down the value of the angle 75 degrees to the nearest tenth
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m degrees.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 2: recall that the tangent of an angle is equal to the ratio of the opposite side of the angle to the adjacent side.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 3: write down the formula for the tangent of an angle:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}\tan \theta &= \frac{\sin \theta}{\cos \theta} = \frac{\frac{costheta}{\sin noise}}{\frac{\sin theta}{\sin theta}} \\ &= \frac{\frac{costheta}{\sin theta}}{\frac{cotheta}{\sin noise}}\end{align*},
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m where cosh(theta) is equal to the hyperbolic cosine of theta, and sinh(theta) is equal to the hyperbolic sine of theta.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 4: recall the trigonometric identity that states that the square of the tangent of an angle plus the square of the cosine of the angle is equal to one:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}\tan ^{2} \theta + \cos ^{2} \theta &= 1\\[1ex] &= 1\end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 5: recall the trigonometry formula for the square of a difference:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}\cos (a \minus{} b) &= \cos a \cos b \plus{} \sin a \sin b\end{align*},
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m where a and b are side lengths of a triangle.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 6: now substitute a = 75 degrees and b = 75 degrees into the formula and use the trigonometry identity for cos(a - b) to simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}\cos (75 \minus{} 75) &= \cos 0 \cos \frac{\pi}{2} \plus{} \sin 75 \sin \frac{\pi}{2} \\ &= \frac{1 \plus{} 0}{1 \plus{} 0}\\ &= 1\end{align*}\boxed{\textbf{answer}}$.
