[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A wooden model of a square pyramid has a base edge of 12 cm and an altitude of 8 cm. A cut is made parallel to the base of the pyramid that separates it into two pieces: a smaller pyramid and a frustum. Each base edge of the smaller pyramid is 6 cm and its altitude is 4 cm. How many cubic centimeters are in the volume of the frustum?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 1: Determine the volume of the whole pyramid
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the volume of the whole pyramid, we can use the formula for the volume of a pyramid: \(\frac{1}{3} \times \text{base area} \times \text{height}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The base area of the pyramid is \(12 \times 12 = 144 \text{ cm}^2\), and the height is 8 cm.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the volume of the whole pyramid is \(\frac{1}{3} \times 144 \text{ cm}^2 \times 8 \text{ cm} = 384 \text{ cm}^3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 2: Determine the volume of a smaller pyramid
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We know that the smaller pyramid has a base area of 6 cm \(\times 6 = 36 \text{ cm}^2\) and the same height of 4 cm.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the volume of the smaller pyramid is \(\frac{1}{3} \times 36 \text{ cm}^2 \times 4 \text{ cm} = 48 \text{ cm}^3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 3: Determine the volume of the frustum
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we subtract the volume of the smaller pyramid from the volume of the whole pyramid to determine the volume of the frustum.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The volume of the frustum is \(384 \text{ cm}^3 - 48 \text{ cm}^3 = 336 \text{ cm}^3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the volume of the frustum is \(\boxed{336}\) cubic centimeters.rparr<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 336
