[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 8:  $$\frac{1}{5\times6} = \frac{1}{5\times6} = \frac{1\times7}{5\times6\times7} = \frac{7}{210}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 9:  Now we can sum up the fractions:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$\left(\frac{2}{4} + \frac{4}{24} + \frac{5}{60} + \frac{6}{120} + \frac{7}{210}\right) = \left(\frac{60}{24} + \frac{20}{24} + \frac{20}{24} + \frac{12}{24} + \frac{7}{24}\right) = \frac{60 + 20 + 20 + 12 + 7}{24} = \frac{119}{24}.$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 10:  Therefore, the sum can be expressed as a simple fraction in lowest terms as $$\boxed{\frac{119}{24}}$$.
