[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars (N$) to Chinese yuan (CNY), we need to first determine the value of the painting in currency based on the exchange rate provided, and then translate that value into Chinese yuan.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. First, calculate the total number of Namibian dollars given to the painting:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 105 \text{ N$} \times 7 \text{ USD/N$} = 735 \text{ USD}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Next, convert this total exchange to Chinese yuan using the given exchange rate:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 735 \text{ USD} \times 6 \text{ CNY/USD} = 4410 \text{ CNY}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the painting costs \(\boxed{4410}\) Chinese yuan.<|endoftext|>
