[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ✅ The value of $\lfloor\sqrt{63}\rfloor$ is $6$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 蹾h> Because $6^2=36<63$ and $7^2=49>63$. So, we know that $\sqrt{63} < 7$, and the greatest integer less than or equal to $\sqrt{63}$ is $6$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 蹾h> We can also easily calculate $\lfloor\sqrt{63}\rfloor$. Let $n$ be the largest possible integer that satisfies $n^2<63$, which is $n=\lceil\sqrt{6}\rceil=4$, since $4^2=16<63<16^2=256$. But $\sqrt{63}$ is the largest possible integer such that $n^2<63$ is $5$, since $5^2=25<63<25^2=625$. So, $\sqrt{63}\approx 7.889\ldots$; therefore, $\lfloor\sqrt{63}\rfloor=6$.
