[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6. $y$: The three numbers $189$, $311$, or $234 + y$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We will check each pair to see if there exist sums $x, y$ that satisfy the given conditions:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Checking Pair #1 (189, 311)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - The only number $x$ that can be formed by three numbers from the set $189$, $311$, $287$, $234$ is $287$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Therefore, $x = 287$ and $y = 189$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Checking Pair #2 (320, 461)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - The only number $x$ that can be formed by three numbers from the set $320$, $461$, $287$ is $287$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Therefore, $x = 287$ and $y = 320$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Checking Pair #3 (234, 277)
