[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m What is the least common multiple of 72 and 96?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the least common multiple (LCM) of two numbers, we need to find the highest power of each prime factor that appears in both numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Group the prime factors of the numbers and multiply the highest power of each factor:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Grouping the prime factors: } \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 72 & \text{> } 96 \implies \text{72 > } 96 \Rightarrow 72 &> 96 &\text{(no prime factors left not greater than both numbers)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Groups of prime factors} &>\text{96 &> \cancel{96}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = \text{72 &> \cancel{72}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \implies \text{LCM} = 72
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m  democratic convince,national healthcare._\boxed{{72}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m  democratic convince, democratic
