[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Square $ ABCD $ has side length $10$. Point $E$ is on $\overline{BC}$, and the area of $ \triangle ABE $ is $40$. What is $ BE $? [asy]size(4cm);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m pair A,B,C,D,E;
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A=(0,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m B=(0,50);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m C=(50,50);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m D=(50,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m E = (30,50);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m draw(A--B);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m draw(B--E);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m draw(E--C);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m draw(C--D);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m draw(D--A);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m draw(A--E);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m dot(A);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m dot(B);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m dot(C);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m dot(D);
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m dot(E);
