[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The volume of a frustum of a pyramid is maximized when the height of the frustum is equal to the slant height of the pyramid. For this particular problem, we have a pyramid with legs $AB=3$ cm and $CB=4$ cm, so the slant height $l$ is given by
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m l = \sqrt{l^2 + h^2} = \sqrt{25 + 16} = \sqrt{41} \approx 6.4.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So the volume of the frustum is given by
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
