[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In rectangle $ABCD$, let's consider the coordinates of the points without any changes.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $(0,0)$ corresponds to point $A$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $(0,3)$ corresponds to point $C$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $B$ is at $(0,0)$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $D$ is at $(9,0)$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $B$ is at $(7.6,0)$ because $9-0 = 7.6$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $D$ is at $(9,3)$ because $9-0 = 9$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $E$ is at $(9,3)$ because $D$ is $(9,3)$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $F$ is at $(16+3.2,-2.4)$ because $16 = 17-3, \quad -2.4 = B-C$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Since we fold the rectangle so that point $A$ coincides with point $C$, $C$ is now at $(11.6, 3)$ because $A$ is at $(9,0)$ and $C$ is at $(17,3)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we need to find the distance $EF$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $F$ is at $(16, 0)$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - $E$ is at $(9, 3)$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The distance formula for horizontal distances is $d = \text{difference}$ in the y-coordinate, and for vertical distances is $d = \sqrt{(\text{difference})^2 + (\text{difference})^2}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m d_E = 16 - 3 = 13
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m d_F = 9 - 3 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the length of segment $EF$ is the square root of $d_E^2 + d_F^2$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m EF = \sqrt{13^2 + 6^2} = \sqrt{169 + 36} = \sqrt{205}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So the length of segment $EF$ is $\sqrt{205}$.<|endoftext|>
