[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Consider the following quantities.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$3x+5y\quad \text{and}\quad 2(x+2y)+y^2$$ 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The function $f(x,y) = 3x+5y-\left(2(x+2y)+y^2\right)$ can be simplified by observing that a key factor is rearranging terms. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align}&3x+5y-\left(2x+4y+2y^2\right)\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &=3x+5y-2x-4y-2y^2\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &=(x-2y)+3y-(4y^2)\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &=x-3y-y^2\\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &=[x+(1-y)]-(y+1)^2\end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Indeed, by rearranging the factors, $f(x,y)=a(x+b)^2+c$ 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m where $a=b=1$, and $c=-y^2$.
