[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Each prime is a natural number greater than 1 and when divided by 2 (such as 2, 3, 5, 7 and so on) leaves the remainder of 1. In this case, the prime 11 is divided by 6. The interger division of this number by 6 leaves a remainder of 1. Hence the remainder thus obtained, when you add the first ten consecutive primes (13, 17, 19, 23, 29, 31, 37, 41... , the last prime is 59) is 1 The seventh prime number is 59.<|endoftext|>
