[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given \( r \) and \( d \) as outlined previously:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Radius \( r = 10 \) inches
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Length of the diameter \( d = 10 \) inches
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - diameter formula read: if random radius, means unequal circle and diameter never to direct apply,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - area will choose formulas normally applied 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Areas based on circumference or diameter directly proportional will be near complete confirmed center from.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Final Answer: 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m def area_calc( radius ):
