[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we will distribute the coefficients:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ (5-4i) - 2(3+6i) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we will perform the multiplications for each term:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 5 - 4i - (6 + 12i) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This transforms into:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 5 - 4i - 6 - 12i \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we will combine the real parts and the imaginary parts:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ (5 - 6) + (-4i - 12i) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -1 - 16i \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the result of the expression $(5-4i)-2(3+6i)$ as a complex number can be expressed as:
