[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. **Calculate the lengths of the other two sides:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     - The sum of the angles in a triangle is always \(180\) degrees.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     - A triangle is divided into two right triangles by the sides meeting at its vertices.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     - The included angle in the right triangle will reduce the length of the sides in half.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     - The included angle for the 45-degree angle must be complementary, meaning \(45^\circ + 45^\circ = 90^\circ\). Therefore, left and right angles in any triangle are equal, making in triangles has bisectors.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     - The side of opposite 45-degree angle in right triangle O is 6 / \sqrt{2}.
