[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m There are real numbers $A$ and $B$ such that
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\frac{5x-16}{x^2-7x+10}=\frac{A}{x-2}+\frac{B}{x-5}.\]Find $A+B$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve for $A+B$, we start by eliminating the denominators using the common denominator $(x-2)(x-5)$. Thus, we must manipulate the given equation to cross-multiply:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{eqnarray*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{5(x-2)}{(x-2)(x-5)} + \frac{B(x-5)}{(x-2)(x-5)} &= \frac{5x-16}{x-2}(x+5) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{5(x-2) + B(x-5)}{(x-2)(x-5)} &= \frac{5x-16}{x-2}(x + 5).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{eqnarray*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We then multiply both sides by $(x-2)(x-5)$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{eqnarray*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5(x-2) + B(x-5) &= \frac{(5x-16)(x+5)}{(x-2)(x-5)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5x - 10 + Bx - 5B &= \frac{5x^2 + 25x - 16x - 80}{(x-2)(x-5)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5x - 10 + Bx - 5B &= \frac{5x^2 + x - 80}{(x-2)(x-5)}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{eqnarray*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since the polynomials on the left side have the form $A(x)$, we may equate coefficients:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{eqnarray*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5x - 10 &= \frac{A(x)}{(x-2)(x-5)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Bx - 5B &= \frac{-16(x - 2)(x - 5)}{(x-2)(x-5)}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{eqnarray*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We isolate $A$, $B$, and move everything else to the right side:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{eqnarray*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A &= \frac{5x - 10}{x-2} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m B &= \frac{-16(x^2 - 7x + 10)}{x(x-2)(x-5)}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{eqnarray*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{eqnarray*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A &= \frac{5x - 10}{x-2} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m B &= \frac{-16(x-2)(x-5)}{x(x-2)(x-5)}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{eqnarray*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m From this, we see that $A = 5$ and $B = \frac{-16}{x-2}$. Therefore, our expression for $A+B$ is $5 + \frac{-16}{x-2}$. The value to be boxed is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{5-\frac{16}{x-2}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed endforeach互动。 NOI 2018 SUMS 中习作审核阶段 对于一次性指定的和参与动手参与测评的论文，至少需要（）名参加测评的学生。
