[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the number of non-congruent figures that can be constructed by attaching two equilateral triangles to the regular pentagon \(ABCDE\) in two of the five positions shown, we need to calculate the number of distinct ways to position two equilateral triangles along the edges of the pentagon.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. **Determine all possible crossings along the edges of the pentagon:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - The pentagon has 5 vertices, and two equilateral triangles can be placed at any of its 5 edges, but we must select 2 out of these 5 edges to place the triangles.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - The calculation involves choosing 2 edges from 5, which simplifies to finding the combinations of these 5 edges.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. **List the combinations of edges:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - \(AB, AD, BA, BD, DC, ED\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - \(AC, AD, AC, AD, BD, BC,...\) is similar for other edges.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. **Calculate the possible placements of the triangles:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - We need to count the distinct combinations where two triangles are placed on the same edge. For example, each edge in the configuration is one combination.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Apply these rules to find each type of combination:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      - \(AB\) (no constraint) -> 2 ways (Check any 2 edges of 1 edge)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      - \(AC\) (no constraint) -> 2 ways (Check any 2 edges of 1 edge)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      - \(AD\) (no constraint) -> 2 ways (Check any 2 edges of 1 edge)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      - Similarly for \(BD, CD, DE, EA, EB...\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Eventually, every edge is possible to have two triangles placed on it, leading to a count of 2 years of combinations for each pair of the edges.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. **Sum all valid combinations:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - For each combination of 2 vertices (representing 2 edges), the number of valid configurations is simply 2:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \text{Total combinations} = \left\lfloor \frac{5!}{2! \cdot 2!} \right\rfloor = 10
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Applying this method to specific cases:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      - $CE, EC, KE, KE$ for a total of 10 configurations.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the number of non-congruent figures that can be constructed by attaching two equilateral triangles to the regular pentagon in two of the five positions shown is \(\boxed{10}\).<|endoftext|>
