[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we need to find \(9^6 \pmod{13}\). This can be simplified using Fermat's Little Theorem, which states that for a prime \(p\) and an integer \(a\) not divisible by \(p\), \(a^{p-1} \equiv 1 \pmod{p}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In our case, \(p = 13\) and \(a = 9\). So, we need to find \(9^6 \pmod{13}\). We can compute this step-by-step:
