[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the volume of the space inside the cylinder but outside the cone, we'll first calculate the volume of the cylinder and then subtract the volume of the cone.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. **Calculate the volume of the cylinder:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    The formula for the volume \( V \) of a cylinder is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    V_{text{cylinder}} = pi r_{text{cylinder}}^2 h_{text{cylinder}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    where:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - ( r_{text{cylinder}} = 1 )
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - ( h_{text{cylinder}} = 3 )
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Substituting these values:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    V_{text{cylinder}} = pi cdot 1^2 cdot 3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. **Calculate the volume of the cone:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    The formula for the volume \( V \) of a cone is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    V_{text{cone}} = frac{1}{3} pi r_{text{cone}}^2 h_{text{cone}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    ]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    where:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - ( r_{text{cone}} = 1 )
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - ( h_{text{cone}} = 1 )
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Substituting these values:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    [
