[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m .PositionSummaryThe Office of the Responsible Officer has developed this Web page to provide information and support about how to review and control the access of third-party system administrator(s) to confidential, privileged information regarding the Health Clearinghouse Program. The information presented on this Web page is intended to give You an idea of what the ultimate responsible officer (RO) is expected to do in the event that a request for an access request is made after the information is stored in the system. Our primary responsibility is to help the system administrator ensure that the competing program requirements are not put to a noncompliance situation. The final RO is the individual company in charge of the project responsible for reviewing, approving and changing access to this information. If You suspect that there is a significant possibility that unreviewed requests are making it into the program's system, You should be aware that the final RO in this process is the one person in charge.
