[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{x^3}{x^2 + 5x + 1}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Notice that (x^3) appears inside the divisor but doesn't directly divide such terms. Instead, we choose a term lower down, here just falling values for simplicity: ($x^3$, $2x^2$, $4x$), and focus effort:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m & \frac{x^3}{x^2 + 5x + 1} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = & \quad \frac{f_4}{x^2 + 5x + 1}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m However, this should read just $f_4$ in this case, trying to stick with as it is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m & \quad \frac{x^3}{x^2 + 5x + 1} = x^2 + \frac{x^3 - 5x^2 - 1}{x^2 + 5x + 1}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, we rewrite it as:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m & \quad x^2 + \frac{x^3 - 5x^2 - 1}{x^2 + 5x + 1} = x^2 + \frac{5x^2 + x + 1}{x + 1}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since we have successively divided terms by their respective highest degree factors $x^2$ and $x + 1$. Therefore, the remainder when $a(b - c)$ is made up of sums of unilateral factors, the degree and exponent minus one, multiplied by $b - c$.
