[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the fractional part of the wall that Heidi can paint in 9 minutes, we need to determine how much of the wall is painted in the second situation.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We know that Heidi paints a full wall (ignoring the fact that 1 wall = 1 m²). So, the first situation, involving painting a wall, can be measured in "full walls". The answer to what fraction of the wall she painted in 45 minutes is $45$. The second situation, involving painting of walls in 9 minutes, can be measured in "how many full walls in 9 minutes". So, the answer to what fraction of the wall she can paint in 9 minutes is $\frac{45}{9}$. Thus, the answer is $\boxed{\frac{5}{1}}$.
