[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let the endpoint be $(x, y)$ and the midpoint be $(h, k)$. Then,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$\begin{align*} x &= 6 + h \\\\ y &= 8 + k \end{align*}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m where $h$ and $k$ are the coordinates of the midpoint.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We are given that $\frac{x-6}{4} = \frac{y-8}{3}$, which comes from converting the midpoint formula from the 2-D point to the 3-D Cartesian cooridnates.
