[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let \[f(x) = \left\{
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{array}{cl}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x^2+1 &\text{ if }x>5, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2x-3 &\text{ if } -5 \le x \le 5, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3 &\text{ if } x <-5.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \right.\]Find $f(-7)+f(0)+f(7)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find $f(-7)+f(0)+f(7)$, we need to evaluate the function $f(x)$ at $x = -7$, $x = 0$, and $x = 7$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We have two cases to consider: $x>5$ and $-5 \le x \le 5$, and $x< -5$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For $x>5$, we use the first case of the function definition: $f(x) = x^2+1$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For $-5 \le x \le 5$, we use the second case of the function definition: $f(x) = 2x-3$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For $x<-5$, we use the third case of the function definition: $f(x) = 3$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Plugging these cases into the function definition, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $f(-7) = (-7)^2 + 1 = 49 + 1 = 50$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $f(0) = 2(0) - 3 = -3$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $f(7) = 3$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, $f(-7)+f(0)+f(7) = 50 + (-3) + 3 = \boxed{40}$.####
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{40}<|endoftext|>
