[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In writing the integers from 10 through 99 inclusive, how many times is the digit 6 written?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This question asks us to count the number of occurrences of the digit 6 present in all numbers from 10 to 99 inclusive. A more systematic way to solve this would be considering how the digit '6' appears in each value, and then summing these counts.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 1: Identify the place values in the range 10 to 99. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - One is in the hundreds place (80-89)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Two are in the tens place (10-19)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Two are in the units place (10-19)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 2: Determine the occurrences of the digit '6' in the hundreds place.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - In each '8' (80, 81, 82, 83, 84, 85, 86), there is an occurrence of the digit '6'.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - The same scenario occurs in the rest of the numbers in the range left over, totaling 7 occurrences.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 3: Determine the occurrences of the digit '6' in the tens and units place.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - In the hundreds place, after 80 we count no more '6's
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - In the tens place, for numbers 101, 102, 103, 104, 105, 106, 107, 108, 109, the digit '6' occurs once.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - In the units place, for numbers 101-109 the digit '6' occurs two times.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 4: Sum up the occurrences from step 2 and step 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Number of multiples of 6 in the '10s' place = 7
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Number of numbers containing the digit '6' in the hundreds, tens, and units place = Number of multiples of 6 in the '10s' - 7 + 2 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, there are 13 occurrences of the digit '6' in the number from 10 to 99 inclusive.
