[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $S_n$ denote the sum of the first $n$ terms of an arithmetic sequence with common difference 3.  If $\frac{S_{3n}}{S_n}$ is a constant that does not depend on $n,$ for all positive integers $n,$ then find the first term.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $S_{3n}$ = $a_n + $ ( $(3n - 2) + $ (3n - 1 + $ 3(n-1))$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m =$a_n + $ (3n)$+2a_1+3n\times 3-1$ + 9n - 3n + 3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = $3a_1 + $ (15n - i)$=$3a_1 + 15(n-1) + n\times 3-1$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m =$n\times 3a_1 + 13n + 2$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $S_n$ = $a_1$ +,$ 10 n$ + $3(n-1)$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m =$a_1 + 10n + 3n - 3$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m =$a_1 + 13n - 3$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\therefore \frac{S_{3n}}{S_n}=\frac{n\times 3a_1 + 13n + 2}{a_1 + 13n - 3}$=$3a_1 +$\frac{2}{a_1 + 13n - 3}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\therefore \frac{2}{a_1 + 13n - 3}$ is a constant that doesn't depend on n; 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since only the constant term $2/a_1 + 13n\times 3-3$ is independent on n:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\therefore 2/a_1$ = constants for all n
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This constant is associated with the first term.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $m$ be this constant: $\implies 2/\times1 = m$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\therefore 5 = a_1$
