[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the product of \(0.\overline{6}\) and 6, let's first convert \(0.\overline{6}\) into a fraction to make the calculation easier.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \(0.\overline{6}\) is equal to \(6/9\) because \(0.\overline{6} = 0.666... \Rightarrow 0 + 0.666... = 0.666...\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, to find the product of \(6/9\) and 6:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \left( \frac{6}{9} \right) \times 6
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Focusing on the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{6}{1} \times 6 = 6 \times 6 = 36
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now focusing on the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Notice that \(9\) and \(6\) have a common factor of \(3\). So, \(9 = 3^2\) and \(6 = 2 \times 3\), hence we can factor out a \(3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 36 = 3 \times 36 \times 3 = 3 \times 3 \times 3 \times 12 = 3 \times 3 \times 3 \times 3 \times 4 = 3^3 \times 4
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m But we can recompute:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{6}{9} \times 6 = \frac{6 \times 6}{9} = \frac{36}{9} = 4
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the product is \(4\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
