[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To convert 225 to base prime representation, we need to process each digit of the number through the exponentiation of each prime factor.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we need to find the prime factors of 225. From here, we work in base 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 225 factors are $ {3 * 7 * 5} $, because
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2  chunks = 3 ∗ 7
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 7 chunks = 3 ∗ 7
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5 chunks = 3 ∗ 7
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m so 2  * 5 = 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3  * 7 = 12.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2 chunks = 3 ∗ 2 = 12
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 7 chunks = 3 ∗ 2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m so 2 * 7 = 14.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2 * 5 = 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1 chunk = 3. Hence 1  * 5 = 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Hence 1 chunk * 7, 1 chunk * 5, and 1 chunk * 3. Thus, the number 225 can be written in base 3 as 1101211111.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, base 3 converts many numbers into their base 2 representations and eventually to the base prime. Let's calculate Cbs.
