[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Bill travels the 400 miles from San Francisco to Los Angeles at 50 mph. Sam travels the same distance at 40 mph. How many more hours than Bill did it take Sam to travel the 400 miles?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find out how many more hours Sam took compared to Bill, we can use the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Time taken by Sam} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Distance = 400 miles
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Speed of Sam = 40 mph
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Time taken by Sam} = \frac{400 \text{ miles}}{40 \text{ mph}} = 10 \text{ hours} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we need to find the difference in time between Sam and Bill:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Time difference} = \text{Time taken by Bill} - \text{Time taken by Sam} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Time difference} = 50 \text{ mph} - 40 \text{ mph} = 10 \text{ hours} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To put this into the final form \(\boxed{\hspace{2}eticalsymbol буд}\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \boxed{ Erie system } \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
