[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A particular triangle has sides of length 14 cm, 8 cm and 9 cm. In centimeters, what is the perimeter of the triangle?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the perimeter of the triangle, we need to add up the lengths of all its sides. Therefore, we add up the lengths 14 cm, 8 cm, and 9 cm.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Perimeter} = 14 \, \text{cm} + 8 \, \text{cm} + 9 \, \text{cm}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's add these numbers step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 14 + 8 = 22
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 22 + 9 = 31
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the perimeter of the triangle is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{31}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
