[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To evaluate the given summation, first we need to recognize its structure:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sum_{m = 1}^\infty \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{1}{mn(m + n + 1)}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We can rewrite the inner sum by letting \( k = m+n+1 \) (note that this transformation should be consistent). Thus, the inner sum becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sum_{k = 2}^\infty \sum_{n = 1}^k \frac{1}{kn(k + n)}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m With \( k = m+n+1 \) and \( n \) from 1 to \( k \), this becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{1}{nk(k + n)}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, to simplify the inner sum, we use partial fraction decomposition. Notice that:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{1}{nk(k + n)} = \frac{1}{k} \left( \frac{1}{n} - \frac{1}{k + n} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, reiterate this decomposition with \( n \) replaced by \( n-1 \) to ensure mutual consistency and proceed with ultimate summation techniques. Therefore, we find:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{1}{nk(k + n)} = \sum_{n=1}^\infty \frac{1}{k} \left( \frac{1}{n} - \frac{1}{(n+1)k} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Integrate this expression term by term from 1 to \(\infty\). The additive property of integration will yield:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sum_{n=1}^\infty \frac{1}{k} \left( \frac{1}{n} - \frac{1}{(n+1)k} \right) = \frac{1}{k} \sum_{n=1}^\infty \left( \frac{1}{n} - \frac{1}{(n+1)k} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplify the resulting summation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{1}{k} \sum_{n=1}^\infty \left( \frac{1}{n} - \frac{1}{(n+1)k} \right) = \frac{1}{k} \left( \sum_{n=1}^\infty \frac{1}{n} - \sum_{n=1}^\infty \frac{1}{(n+1)k} \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The original summation now becomes simplified effectively as seen:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sum_{n=1}^\infty \frac{1}{nk(k + n)}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m As you've shown in reverse logic with power and series, seemingly presents a fine happenstance.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the summation leans towards:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
