[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The sum of the 2009 fractions, each of the form $\frac{2}{n(n+2)}$ for the positive integers from 1 to 2009, can be expressed as:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{2}{1} \left( 1 + x + 2x + 3x^2 + 4x^2 + 5x^3 + \cdots \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This can be simplified using the formula for the sum of an infinite geometric series:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{2}{1} \left( 1 + 3x + 5x^2 + 7x^3 + 9x^4 + \cdots \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This represents a geometric series with the first term $a = 1$ and the common ratio $r = 3x$. The sum of an infinite geometric series $\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} ar^{n-1} / (1 - r)$ can be found using the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m S = \frac{a}{1 - r}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Here, $a = 1$ and $r = 3x$. Thus:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{2 \cdot 3x^n}{1-x}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Breaking it down into simplified terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = 2 \cdot 3x \left( \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} x^n \right)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We recognize the sum of the infinite geometric series:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} x^n = \frac{x}{1-x}, \quad \text{for} \quad 0 < x < 1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = 2 \cdot 3x \left( \frac{x}{1-x} \right) = \frac{6x^2}{1-x}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Combining this with the original term, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{2}{1} \left( \frac{6x^2}{1-x} \right) = \frac{12x^2}{1-x}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
