[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. **Find the Area of the Smaller Square**: The area \(A_{\text{small}}\) of a square is given by \( \text{side}^2 \). Here, the side is 2 inches. So, \( A_{\text{small}} = 2^2 = 4 \) square inches.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. **Calculate the Shaded Region**: The shaded region is the area of the original square minus the area of the smaller square. So, the area \(A_{\text{shaded}}\) is the original square minus the smaller square. This gives \( A_{\text{shaded}} = 4 - 4 = 0 \) square inches.
