[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The shape of the sign outside Bob's Burger Barn is a regular octagon. How many degrees are in the measure of an interior angle of this sign?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the measure of an interior angle in a regular octagon, you can use the formula for the sum of the interior angles of any polygon:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Sum of interior angles} = (n - 2) \times 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m where \( n \) represents the number of sides (or angles) in the polygon.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For an octagon:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - \( n = 8 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - The sum of the interior angles is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m   \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m   (8 - 2) \times 180^\circ = 6 \times 180^\circ = 1080^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m   \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now that we have the sum of the interior angles, we can find the measure of any one interior angle by dividing the total sum by the number of angles (which is \( 8 \) in this case):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Measure of an interior angle} = \frac{1080^\circ}{8} = 135^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the measure of an interior angle of this sign is \(\boxed{135^\circ}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
