[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Find the integer $n$, $0 \le n \le 5$, such that \[n \equiv -3736 \pmod{6}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find an integer \( n \) such that \( 0 \le n \le 5 \) and \( n \equiv -3736 \pmod{6} \), we need to determine what remainder \( n \) has when divided by 6. This can be done by taking the negative of \(-3736\) and then finding the modulo 6 of this result.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Calculate the negative of \(-3736\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    -3736 \equiv 6 - 3736 = 6 - 3736 = 6 - 3 \cdot 656 = 6 - 1968 = -1962 \equiv 6 - 6 \cdot 336 = 6 - 1968 = 6 - 0808 = 6 - 808 = 6 - 0808 = -1002 \equiv 6 + 636 = 636 \pmod{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Find the remainder when \(-1002\) is divided by 6:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    -1002 \div 6 = -167.0 \quad \text{(integer part)} \quad \text{so} \quad -1002 = 6 \cdot (-167) + r \quad \text{(remainder)}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    -1002 = 6 \cdot -167 + 0 \quad \text{i.e., } 0 \quad \text{so} \quad r = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Thus, the smallest positive integer \( n \) that satisfies the condition is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \boxed{636}<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
