[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Find the number of positive integers $n$ for which the graph of
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[y = \frac{(x + 3)(x - 7)^5}{(x - 1)(x - 7)^n}\]has a hole at $x = 7.$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve this problem, let's break it down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we need to identify the value of \( n \) that makes the graph of the function \( y = \frac{(x + 3)(x - 7)^5}{(x - 1)(x - 7)^n} \) a horizontal asymptote at \( x = 7 \). A horizontal asymptote at \( x = 7 \) implies that the degree of the polynomial in the denominator must be less than or equal to the degree of the polynomial in the numerator.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The numerator of the function is \( (x + 3)(x - 7)^5 \), which has a degree of 6. The denominator of the function is \( (x - 1)(x - 7)^n \). The power of \( (x - 1) \) in the denominator should be less than or equal to 6. Therefore, we set up the inequality:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ n \leq 6. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This means \( n \) can be any positive integer less than or equal to 6.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we will check each of these values of \( n \) to see if it makes the function a horizontal asymptote at \( x = 7 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. If \( n = 1 \), the denominator becomes \( 6^1 = 6 \). The function becomes \( y = \frac{(x + 3)(x - 7)^5}{3(x - 7)^1} = \frac{(x + 3)(x - 7)^4}{x - 7} \). When \( x = 7 \), \( y = \frac{(7 + 3)(7 - 7)^4}{7 - 7} = \frac{10 \cdot 0}{0} \). The function has a horizontal asymptote at \( y = 0 \), not at \( x = 7 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. If \( n = 2 \), the denominator becomes \( 6^2 = 36 \). The function becomes \( y = \frac{(x + 3)(x - 7)^4}{(x - 1)(x - 7)^2} = \frac{(x + 3)(x - 7)^2}{x - 1} \). When \( x = 7 \), \( y = \frac{(7 + 3)(7 - 7)^2}{7 - 1} = \frac{10 \cdot 0}{6} = 0 \). The function has a horizontal asymptote at \( y = 0 \), not at \( x = 7 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. If \( n = 3 \), the denominator becomes \( 6^3 = 216 \). The function becomes \( y = \frac{(x + 3)(x - 7)^4}{7(x - 1)^3} \). When \( x = 7 \), \( y = \frac{(7 + 3)(7 - 7)^4}{7(7 - 1)^3} = \frac{10 \cdot 0}{50^3} = 0 \). The function has a horizontal asymptote at \( y = 0 \), not at \( x = 7 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. If \( n = 4 \), the denominator becomes \( 6^4 = 1296 \). The function becomes \( y = \frac{(x + 3)(x - 7)^4}{(x - 1)(x - 7)^4} = \frac{x + 3}{x - 1} \). When \( x = 7 \), \( y = \frac{7 + 3}{7 - 1} = \frac{10}{6} = \frac{5}{3} \). The function does not have a horizontal asymptote at \( x = 7 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. If \( n = 5 \), the denominator becomes \( 6^5 = 7776 \). The function becomes \( y = \frac{(x + 3)(x - 7)^5}{(x - 1)(x - 7)^5} = \frac{(x + 3)(x - 7)}{x - 1} \). When \( x = 7 \), \( y = \frac{10 \cdot 4}{7 - 1} = \frac{40}{6} = \frac{20}{3} \). The function does not have a horizontal asymptote at \( x = 7 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6. If \( n = 6 \), the denominator becomes \( 6^6 = 46656 \). The function becomes \( y = \frac{(x + 3)(x - 7)^5}{(x - 1)(x - 7)^6} = \frac{(x + 3)(x - 7)}{2(x - 1)} \). When \( x = 7 \), \( y = \frac{(7 + 3)(7 - 7)}{2(7 - 1)} = \frac{10 \cdot 0}{14} = 0 \). The function has a horizontal asymptote at \( y = 0 \), not at \( x = 7 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, there are no positive integers \( n \leq 6 \) that make the function a horizontal asymptote at \( x = 7 \). The number of such \( n \) is \boxed{0}.<|endoftext|>
