[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We have to find $x$ such that $\log_{12} \bigg(3x\bigg) = 2$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve for $x$, we can use logarithmic properties and the properties of logarithms.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m L'Hopital's Rule says that if $\lim\limits_{a \to c} f\bigg|_{a^-}$ and $\lim\limits_{a \to c} g\bigg|_{a^-} = \infty$,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We will proceed with the conversion to a standard form.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Then we can cancel out the common factor $\log _{12} x$,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m and we will get that $x \equal{} 3 \cdot 12 ^ {\minus{} 2}$ </embed><\/strong I">
