[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the expression Z using the formula for a geometric sum, we need to consider the radius \( r \) and the angle \( \theta \) separately.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The sum of an infinite geometric series reaches its maximum value when the ratio \(\frac{a}{r}\) exists within the range \( -1 < r < 1 \). In this case, the series starts clear horizontally (83 degrees), and its maximum is 1 (the imaginary part is 1) when:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    (
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    theta = cis(75)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    )
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The formula for the sum of the series \( Z \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Z = theta * r
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m           
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For our series, we can substitute \( r = 1 \) into the formula. This gives us Z in terms of \(\theta\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Z = theta 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So $\theta = 147^\circ$.<|endoftext|>
