[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We are given the recursive sequence $a_n=a_{n-1}a_{n-2}^2$, where $a_0=1$, $a_1=\sqrt[19]{2}$, and $a_n=a_{n-1}a_{n-2}^2$. I would like to find the smallest positive integer $k$ such that the product $a_1a_2\cdots a_k$ is an integer.The base cases are present, $a_0=1$ and $a_1=\sqrt[19]{2}$. Now, $a_2=a_1^2=\left( \sqrt[19]{2} \right)^2=\frac{2}{19}.$ And $a_3=a_2^2=\left(\frac{2}{19}\right)^2=\frac{4}{361}$. Finally, $a_4=a_3^2=\left( \frac{4}{361} \right)^2=\left( \frac{4}{19^2}\right).$It is clear that $a_1a_2a_3a_4=\frac{4^4}{361^3}=1$ is an integer.  $\blacksquare$<|endoftext|>
