[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve this problem, let us first understand the binomial coefficient mind carefully. The binomial coefficient $\binom{n}{k}$ represents the number of ways to choose $k$ items out of $n$ items, and it is defined as $\binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}$, where $n!$ denotes the factorial of $n$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given our infinite sum, the term $\frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}}$ simplifies to $\frac{\frac{n!}{15!12!}}{\frac{n!}{17!10!}}$ using the properties of binomial coefficients.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplifying further, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}} = \frac{\frac{n!}{15!12!}}{\frac{n!}{17!10!}} = \frac{17!10!}{15!12!}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Notice that $15!$ and $17!$ recursively cancel out, leaving us with:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{17!10!}{15!} = \frac{17 \cdot 16 \cdot 15 \cdot 14 \cdot 13 \cdot 12 \cdot 11 \cdot 10!}{15 \cdot 14 \cdot 13 \cdot 12 \cdot 11 \cdot 10!} = 17 \cdot 16 = 272.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the infinite sum is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sum_{n=17}^{\infty} \frac{\binom{n}{15}}{\binom{n}{17}} = 272.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
