[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Yes. To solve the problem with Python, let's calculate the factorial values and then find the factorial of $14-5 = 9$. Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 9 = \frac{9!}{8!} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 14! = \frac{14!}{9!} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 9 = \frac{9!}{8!}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substituting the previous values:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{14!}{5! \times 9!} = \frac{\frac{14!}{5!}}{9!} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = \frac{7 \times 2 \times 11 \times 10 \times 9!}{8 \times 7 \times 6 \times 5!} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = \frac{7 \times 2 \times 11 \times 10}{8 \times 6 \times 5!}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
