[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If $(x - 1) + (x - 2) + (x - 3) + (x - 4) = x$, then what is $x$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 1: Analyze the given equation
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We are given the equation $(x - 1) + (x - 2) + (x - 3) + (x - 4) = x$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 2: Sum all the terms on the left side
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $(x - 1) + (x - 2) + (x - 3) + (x - 4) = x$ can be simplified by adding all the terms together.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $3x - 10 = x$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 3: Solve for $x$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve for $x$, rearrange the equation to isolate $x$ on one side.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $3x - x = 10$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $2x = 10$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 4: Divide both sides by 2
