[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The matrix
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} \frac{4}{29} & -\frac{10}{29} \\ -\frac{10}{29} & \frac{25}{29} \end{pmatrix}\]corresponds to projecting onto a certain vector $\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix}.$  Find $\frac{y}{x}.$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If the matrix is the projection matrix, then each row of the matrix gives the current position in some basis. We can write $\textbf{X}$ as a linear combination of $\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix}$. So we can write it as
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} x^{2} & x y \\ y x & y^{2} \\ z & w \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} x & y \\ z & w \end{pmatrix}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $\begin{pmatrix} \frac{x_{2}}{x_{1}} \\ \frac{y_{2}}{y_{1}}\end{pmatrix}$ be the eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\lambda$. Then
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} \frac{x_{1} y_{1} z^{2} + x_{1} w & \frac{w x_{2} z^{2} + x y_{1} z^{2}}{y_{1}^{2} w} \\ \frac{x_{1} y_{2} w + x_{2} y_{1} w & \frac{z y_{1} x_{2} w}{y_{1}^{2} w^{2}} \\ w^{2} & 0\end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix},\   \begin{pmatrix} x & y \\ \frac{w^{2}}{y_{1}} & 0 \end{pmatrix}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Then $\frac{w^{2}}{y_{1}} = -\frac{x_{1} z^{2} + x_{1} w}{y_{1}^{2} w}$, and we have $\frac{1}{y_{1}} = \frac{x_{1} z^{2} + x_{1} w}{y_{1}^{2} w + x_{2} y_{1} z^{2} + x_{2} w}$. Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\frac{y_{1}}{x_{1}} = \frac{x_{1} z^{2} + x_{1} w}{y_{1}^{2} w + x_{2} y_{1} z^{2} + x_{2} w}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Similarly, $\frac{x_{2}}{y_{2}} = \frac{y_{2} x_{1} - y_{1} x_{2}}{y_{1}^{2} w^{2} - y_{2} z^{2} + x_{2} w}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Finally, $\frac{y_{1} + y_{2}}{x_{1} + x_{2}} = \frac{x_{1} z^{2} + x_{1} w + y_{1} x_{2} - y_{1} x_{2}}{y_{1}^{2} w + x_{2} y_{1} z^{2} + x_{2} w}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, $\frac{y_{2} + y_{1}}{x_{2} + x_{1}} = \frac{y_{1} x_{2} + y_{2} x_{1}^{2} - y_{1}^{2} + x_{1} y_{2}}{y_{1}^{2} w + x_{2} y_{1} z^{2} + x_{2} w}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Putting things together, we find that
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{y_{1}} & \frac{0}{x_{1}} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} x_{1} z^{2} + x_{1} w & \frac{w x_{2} z^{2} + x y_{1} z^{2}}{y_{1}^{2} w} \\ \frac{y_{2} x_{1} - y_{1} x_{2}}{y_{1}^{2} w^{2} - y_{2} z^{2} + x_{2} w} & \frac{z y_{1} x_{2} w}{y_{1}^{2} w^{2} - y_{2} z^{2} + x_{2} w}\end{pmatrix},\   \begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{y_{2}} & \frac{0}{x_{2}} \end{pmatrix}.\]<|endoftext|>
