[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For the polynomial to be divisible by $x-4$, the remainder must be $0$. We can use the Remainder Theorem (also known as the Factor Theorem) to evaluate the polynomial at $x=4$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
