[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The amount of money a certain company has can be modeled with the line $y=-265x+2800$, where $x$ is the number of workers the company decides to hire. What is the maximum number of workers the company can hire before the company has no money left and goes bankrupt?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m From the given equation $y=-265x+2800$ , the maximum number of workers the business has before going bankrupt would be achieved when $y$ is maximized. Since $y$ represents the earnings before paying any expenses, let's find out $y>0$ first.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m y>0 \Rightarrow -265x+2800>0.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m As $x$ represents the number of workers, taking the absolute value of both sides and forming an absolute value fraction, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \left | y \right | > \left | 2800 \right | \Rightarrow \left | -x \right |+2800>\left | -265 \right | \Rightarrow \left | x+2802 \right |>\left | -265 \right | \Rightarrow (x+2802) > 265.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Solving the inequality $(x+2802) > 265$ for $x$, we find two potential values approaching a limiting value. One endpoint of the interval approach $x = \boxed{{1006/265}}$, and the other endpoint approaches $x = \boxed{{\infty}}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since the formula represents an absolute value, our conditions yield an inequality $1006/265-1< x < \infty$, which is actually taking the endpoints of an interval where $x$ corresponds to:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x \in \left [\frac{\left ( 1006/265 \right ) -1}{2},+\infty \right ).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the maximum number of workers the company can hire before the company runs out of money and has to decide to shut down is $\boxed{{\left [ 1 +\frac{1}{2}} \right ]}$.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
