[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Captain Rusczyk tracked down a pirate who had stolen $2345_{6}$ dollars worth of goods from his ship. After winning an epic duel, the Captain demands that the pirate return $41324_{5}$ dollars. How much has the pirate gone in debt due to his two encounters with Rusczyk? Express your answer in base 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Yes, properly converted to the leftmost six digits follows:  $2345_{6}$ becomes $2345_{10}$, while $2345_{10}$ becomes $1240016_{10}$. Here's the conversion: 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$2345_{10} =1\times10^{4}+2\times10^{3}+4\times10^{2}+5\times10^{1}+6\times10^{0}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Side note: You may find it helpful to remember that a 6 in the six's place and a 1 in the one's place leads to a $1 x 10^6$, a $2 x 10^3$, etc, leading to the above necessary calculation.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$1240016_{10} =$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$ 2\times 10^5+3\times10^4+4\times 10^3+5\times 10^2+16\times 10 ^1+16\times 10 ^0 \;.$$ 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now the two pirates are useless when it comes to converting those.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$2345_{10} + 41324_{10} = 64779_{10} \;.$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Lastly, $$64779_{10} =$$ $5100100_6 \;.$ So the Captain is owe a total of 5100100 dollars when converted.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m From here we can simplify using the order of operations. When we convert the mix down 510016_{10} also, it becomes just $5100100_6{}$. Now the other problems were 30000_{10} left, we follow the same formula. So $64779 + 1666665 = 1766443$<|endoftext|>
