[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $p(x) = x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7$. We want to find $p(r) + p(s) + p(t)$, which expands to $r^3 - 20r^2 + 18r - 7 + s^3 - 20s^2 + 18s - 7 + t^3 - 20t^2 + 18t - 7$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Notice that $s^3 - 20s^2 + 18s - 7$ appears in both the expression for $p(r)$ and the expression for $p(s)$. Similarly, we have $t^3 - 20t^2 + 18t - 7$ in both $p(t)$ and $p(s)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
