[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 这么久不写作业了回复你的公共投稿提示没错。gunta system 要计算 \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{2 + 6}{4^{100}} + \frac{2 + 2 \cdot 6}{4^{99}} + \frac{2 + 3 \cdot 6}{4^{98}} + \dots + \frac{2 + 98 \cdot 6}{4^3} + \frac{2 + 99 \cdot 6}{4^2} + \frac{2 + 100 \cdot 6}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This series is telescoping. For each term \( n \cdot 6 \), the term before it is \( \frac{2 + 6}{4^n} \), which is not equal to \( \frac{2 + n \cdot 6}{4^n} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For \( n = 1, 2, 3, \ldots, 100 \), we have \( 6 \cdot n \), so the numerators of the terms become \( 2 + 6n \), which are all equal, while the denominators \( 4^n \) become \( 6^n \), which are all equal to \( 2^n \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the final sum reduces to:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6 \cdot \left( \frac{2}{4} + \frac{6}{4^2} + \cdots + \frac{98 \cdot 6}{4^{100}} \right) + 6
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6 \left( \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{2} \left( \frac{6}{4^2} + \frac{6}{4^3} + \cdots + \frac{6}{4^{99}} \right) \right) + 6 = 6 \left( \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{4} + \cdots + \frac{1}{4} \right) + 6 = 6 \cdot \frac{100}{4} + 6 = 300 + 6 = 306
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the final answer is \( \boxed{306} \).<|endoftext|>
