[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. The coordinates of the angle $\theta$ relative to the $$x$$-axis are $${x}_{1} = \frac{5 \pi}{12}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. The coordinate of the radial distance $$(x_r, y_r, z_r) = (3 r \sin \theta, 3 r \cos \theta ,3)$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Rearrange the equation of the $$x$$-axis to get $z = -\sqrt {|\phi|^2 +\phi ^2} r \simeq -\sqrt {75} r$. (The cause of this image being $2 \times r \sin \theta$ appears to be a screen captured of a screen of $2 \times r$ with a dotted line $z = 0$).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m  理由:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. We start by identifying the $x$, $y$, and $z$ coordinates in the given spherical coordinates. The coordinates provided are $\left( \rho, \theta, \phi \right) = \left( 3, \frac{5 \pi}{12}, 0 \right)$. Here, $\rho$ represents the radial distance, $\theta$ is the angle from the $x$-axis, and $\phi$ is the angle in the $xy$-plane from the positive $z$-axis.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Since $\phi = 0$, the angle $\phi$ is zero. The radial distance $r$ in spherical coordinates is simply $\rho = 3$. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Our task is to convert this spherical coordinate system to rectangular coordinates (xyz coordinates). This conversion involves using the relationship $x_r = \rho \sin \theta \cos \phi$, $y_r = \rho \sin \theta \sin \phi$, and $z_r = \rho \cos \phi$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. For the given spherical coordinates, we substitute the values in the $x_r$, $y_r$, and $z_r$ equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    x_r &= \rho \sin \theta \cos \phi \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    y_r &= \rho \sin \theta \sin \phi \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    z_r &= \rho \cos \phi
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. Substituting the values from spherical coordinates $(\rho = 3)$, $\theta = \frac{5 \pi}{12}$, and $\phi = 0$, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    x_r &= 3 \sin \left( \frac{5 \pi}{12} \right) \cos (0) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    &= 3 \sin \left( \frac{5 \pi}{12} \right) \times 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    &= 3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    y_r &= 3 \sin \left( \frac{5 \pi}{12} \right) \sin (0) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    &= 3 \sin \left( \frac{5 \pi}{12} \right) \times 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    &= 0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    z_r &= 3 \cos (0) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    &= 3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6. Therefore, the rectangular coordinates will be $(x_r, y_r, z_r) = (3, 0, 3)$.
