[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $p(x)$ be a polynomial with integer coefficients. By the division algorithm, we have: $$ 4=x(1+x+\cdots+x+1) + (x+\cdots+x)(x^{n-1}+x^{n-2}+ \cdots + x +1) + 136 x, $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m where $n$ is the height, $x$ is the length of the infinitely long effectoring chain~1, and~2 is the factorization. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Then,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m   \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m p(x) &= (x+x^{n-1}+\cdots + x +1) \cdot (1+x+\cdots + x +1) +2(x+x^{n-1}+ \cdots + x +1)  \\ \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= (1+x^{n-1}+\cdots + x +1)\left(x +1 +x^{n-2}+\cdots +x^{n-1} +1\right) +2 \left(x +1 +x^{n-2}+\cdots + x +1\right). 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m  \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, by the identity $\overline{xA+c} = \dfrac{a+c}{\Vert a\Vert}\overline x,$ $p(x)$ satisfies the polynomial $q(x)$: 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m q(x)-1 &= (1+x^{n-1}+\cdots + x +1)\overline x^{n-1} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m q(x)+(1+x^{n-1}+\cdots + x +1)\overline x^{n-1} &= 2\overline x^{n-2} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m q(x)+2\overline x^{n-2} &= 2\overline x^{n-1}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m  \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Replacing $x \mapsto x-1,$ $(q(x)+2\overline(x^{n-1}+x^{n-2} +\cdots + x +1)= 2\overline(x^{n-1})$, and by repeatedly using the inequality $5^k> k x^{k/2}$ for any $x \geq 1$ and suitable integers, we get $ 3\cdot 11x^7+7\cdot 11^2x^3+ 5\cdot 11^3x= 2\cdot 11^5x-2\cdot 11^7.$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Rewriting all three $32^3x^3=1$, $32^5$ and $32^7$ factors of $3$ out from right to left, and substituting for $x$, we find that $q(x)$ = $-3^{5}3^{5}1^2-x^{6}[1+ 3]$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Rewriting $q(x)$ into a slightly simpler form yields $p(x) = r(x) \cdot 3^53^4$,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m which can be similarly divided out of $32^3x^3$ and $32^53^{3}3$, and substituting for $x$ to obtain: $p(2)=3^53^43=3^{9}=27 \cdot 3^2=7 \cdot 9$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So $p(6) = 7(9)=63$.
