[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We need to find the number of different ways to arrange the letters U, C, O, N, and T around a circle. Let's denote the positions of the letters as a, b, c, d, e, and f respectively.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since each position has a unique letter, we can use a permutation of these five letters. The number of permutations of five items is given by \(5!\) (5 factorial).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[5! = 5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1 = 120\]
