[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Joyce has found that (n + 1)/5 + 1 ≡ 0 (mod 3) means that (n + 1) is a multiple of 3. Afterwards, she finds that (n + 2)/5 - 2 ≡ 0 (mod 3) means that n + 2 is a multiple of 15. Thus n is a multiple of 15. The so-called "minimum number of \"hands\" needed to open a card's secret" and(payment) is therefore approximately equal to the least common multiple of (a + 1); this turns out to be, roughly, 52.\boxed{52}
