[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The equation 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$\lfloor r \rfloor + r = 12.2$$ 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m can be expressed as 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $r - \lfloor r\rfloor = 10.8$. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$r = \left\lfloor r \right\rfloor + 10.8.$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m As we know 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $12 \approx 12$, 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m and thus 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $r\leq 11$. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Also, since 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\lfloor r \rfloor \leq r \leq \left \lfloor r \right \rfloor + 1$, 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m clearly 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $r \ge 12$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Adding the two inequalities will yield the result:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$r = 12 \leq \left \lfloor r \right \rfloor + 10.8 \leq 11 \implies r \leq 19.8.$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Hence 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $r = 10$ or 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $r = 19.8$.<|endoftext|>
