[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve the problem, we need to determine how many integer values of \( x \) satisfy both sets of inequalities:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. \( |x| + 5 < 7 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. \( |x - 3| > 2 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Step 1: Solve the first inequality \( |x| + 5 < 7 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The absolute value inequality \( |x| + 5 < 7 \) can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
