[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine the length of the intercepted arc $\widehat{BC}$, we can start with the given circumference of the circle $A$: $60$ feet. According to a standard knowledge point in circles, we know that the circumference of a circle is $2 \pi r$, where $r$ is the radius of the circle. Given that the circumference is $60$ feet, we can set up the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 2 \pi r = 60 \]
