[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m  razón solution
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In base 2, each digit represents the number of times a certain bit is set (1), as opposed to a certain bit being set (1:0). 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So to find the sum, you would look at the sum of the digits at different bases. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So in base 2, 1011 is the same as 3 + 2 + 1 = 6 in base 10, 3 + 2 + 1 = 6 in base 2 as well. Heights
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Compute $1001_2 \times 101_2$ and put your answer in base 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Express your answer as a hexadecimal or binary number in base10.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m eous solution
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's break down $1001_2 \times 101_2$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (1) We start with multiplying:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     $$ 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     1 \times 101_{10} \leftarrow 101
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To align the decimal part, we shift it to the left (find the length of the shorter string + 1).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Fixing the decimal multiplication, we calculate:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1 \times 10 + 0 \times 1 = 10. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Taking the result modulo $2^{n}$, we determine:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$ 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 10 \mod 161 = 4 \quad \Rightarrow \quad -10+21 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 5.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Reversing the steps by shifting $5$ on the left gives $514_{10}$ in base 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In hexadecimal, this number becomes $93_9$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In binary, this means $1111010_2$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Hence, our satisfactory answer is $\boxed{1111010_2}$.
