[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Angle \( \angle AOD \) is given as \( 54^\circ \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Both \( \angle AOB \) and \( \angle BOC \) are diameters of the circle.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. The sum of a pair of equal angles within any circle is \( 180^\circ \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Analysis
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given that \( \angle AOD = 54^\circ \), we know that \( \angle AOB + \angle BOC = 168^\circ \) because \( \angle AOD, \angle BOC \) are diameters and form a circle. However, since each reflex angle in a circle measures \( 54^\circ \), we can also calculate an angle of \( 180^\circ - 54^\circ = 126^\circ \) corresponding to \( \angle BOC \). But using the angle measure of the diameters, we can cover the full circle.
