[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve this system of inequalities, we will solve each inequality separately and then find the overlapping solutions.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For inequality (1):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -3y \geq y + 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We add \(y\) to both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -3y + y \geq y + 7 + y \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -2y \geq 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Then, divide both sides by \(-2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ y \leq -\frac{7}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For inequality (2):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -2y \leq 12 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Divide both sides by \(-2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ y \geq -6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since both inequalities are inclusive, the overlapping solution is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -6 \leq y \leq -\frac{7}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For inequality (3):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -4y \geq 2y + 17 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Subtract \(-2y\) from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -4y + 2y \geq 2y + 17 - 2y \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -2y \geq 17 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Then, divide both sides by \(-2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ y \leq -\frac{17}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Combining the solutions from the inequalities:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -6 \leq y \leq -\frac{7}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
