[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Find
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{n^2 + n - 1}{(n + 2)!}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the sum of the series, recall
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{n^2 + n - 1}{(n + 2)!}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We will factor the numerator
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\frac{n^2 + n - 1}{(n + 2)!} = \frac{(n - 1) + 2}{(n + 2)!} = \frac{2 - 1}{(n + 2)!} = \frac{1}{(n + 2)!}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the series becomes
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{1}{(n + 2)!}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we test the partial sum for large values of \( n \) (using Knuth's upshift lemma)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\sum_{n = 1}^{100} \frac{1}{(n + 2)!} = 1 + \frac{1}{6!} + \frac{1}{5!} + \frac{1}{4!} + \dots\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We have
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\frac{1}{6!} + \frac{1}{5!} + \frac{1}{4!} + \dots = \frac{1}{6!} \left[ \frac{1}{135} + \frac{1}{165} \right] = 0.0001.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Also,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\frac{1}{6!} + \frac{1}{7!} + \frac{1}{8!} + \dots = \frac{1}{6!} \times E = 0.0001.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\sum_{n = 1}^{100} \frac{1}{(n + 2)!} = 0.0001.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Continuing to the limit as \( n \to \infty \),
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\lim_{n \to \infty} \sum_{n = 1}^{100} \frac{1}{(n + 2)!} = 0.0001.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, our sum is
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\boxed{0.0001}.\]<|endoftext|>
