[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m I want to read 4 books over the next month.  My bookshelf has 12 different books.  In how many ways can I choose which books to read over the next month, without regard to the order that I read them?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This is a combinatorics problem. There are 12 possible books to choose from. We want to find the number of ways to choose 4 books to read. This can be visualized as a combination problem, and the answer can be calculated using the formula.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We use the formula 𝑦 choose \( n \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \binom {12}{4} ={991}{=}\boxed{18 {,}7{,}3} \]<|endoftext|>
