[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - When \(\lfloor x \rfloor = 0\), \(\lfloor x \rfloor = 0\), so the equation simplifies to \( x^2 = 75\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Solving \( x^2 = 75 \), we get \( x = \pm \sqrt{75} = \pm 5\sqrt{3} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Case 2: \(\lfloor x \rfloor = 1\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - When \(\lfloor x \rfloor = 1\), \(\lfloor x \rfloor - 1 = 0\), so the equation simplifies to \( x^2 - 1 = 75 \), which means \( x = \pm \sqrt{76} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Case 3: \(\lfloor x \rfloor = 2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - When \(\lfloor x \rfloor = 2\), \(\lfloor x \rfloor - 2 = 0\), so the equation simplifies to \( x^2 - 4 = 75 \), which means \( x = \pm \sqrt{79} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Case 4: \(\lfloor x \rfloor = 3\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - When \(\lfloor x \rfloor = 3\), \(\lfloor x \rfloor - 3 = 0\), so the equation simplifies to \( x^2 - 9 = 75 \), which means \( x = \pm \sqrt{84} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Case 5: \(\lfloor x \rfloor \geq 4\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - When \(\lfloor x \rfloor > 4\), \(\lfloor x \rfloor - 4 = -3\) (a negative number), so the equation \( x^2 - 3 = 75 \) has no solutions because \(-3\) is not a perfect square.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the possible solutions are \( x = \pm 5\sqrt{3} \), \( x = \pm \sqrt{76} \), \( x = \pm \sqrt{79} \), \( x = \pm \sqrt{84} \), and \( x = \pm 5\sqrt{3} \). So, the final answer is:
