[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ f(x) = 3x + 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ f(2) = 3(2) + 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ f(2) = 6 + 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ f(2) = 9 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we use the result from \( f(2) \) to evaluate \( g(f(2)) \), which is \( g(9) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ g(x) = 4x + 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ g(9) = 4(9) + 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ g(9) = 36 + 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ g(9) = 39 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Finally, we use the result from \( g(9) \) to evaluate \( f(g(f(2))) \), which is \( f(39) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ f(x) = 3x + 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ f(39) = 3(39) + 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ f(39) = 117 + 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ f(39) = 120 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
