[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Start by calculating $g(2)$ using the function $g(x)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    g(2) = f(2 \cdot 2) - 3 = f(4) - 3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Next, we use the function $g(x)$ to find the value of $f(4)$. Since $f(x) = 2x + 1$, substitute $x = 4$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    f(4) = 2 \cdot 4 + 1 = 8 + 1 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    So,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    g(2) = 9 - 3 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Now that we know $g(2) = 6$, we need to find $g(g(2)) = g(6)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Substituting $x = 6$ into the function $g(x)$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    g(6) = f(2 \cdot 6) - 3 = f(12) - 3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. Next, we use the function $g(x)$ to find the value of $f(12)$. Since $f(x) = 2x + 1$, substitute $x = 12$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    f(12) = 2 \cdot 12 + 1 = 24 + 1 = 25
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    So,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    g(6) = 25 - 3 = 22
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the final answer is $\boxed{22}$.<|endoftext|>
