[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the number of paths from $C$ to $D$ on the grid, where every step must be down or to the right, we need to consider the path from $C$ (which we will label as $-1$) to $D$ (which we will label as $1$). We need to navigate through the towers of three towers, which are all identical cells.
