[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m By how many degrees does the measure of an interior angle of a regular octagon exceed the measure of an interior angle of a regular hexagon?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine the difference in the measure of an interior angle of a regular octagon compared to a regular hexagon, we can use the fact that the sum of an interior angle of a regular polygon is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Sum of interior angles} = (n-2) \times 180^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m where \( n \) is the number of sides of the polygon.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For an octagon (\( n = 8 \)):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Sum of interior angles of octagon} = (8-2) \times 180^\circ = 6 \times 180^\circ = 1080^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For a hexagon (\( n = 6 \)):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Sum of interior angles of hexagon} = (6-2) \times 180^\circ = 4 \times 180^\circ = 720^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The difference in the measure of an interior angle between a regular octagon and a regular hexagon is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Difference} = 1080^\circ - 720^\circ = 360^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the measure of an interior angle of a regular octagon exceeds the measure of an interior angle of a regular hexagon by \boxed{360^\circ}.<|endoftext|>
