[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, let's analyze the given information:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - The dimensions of the rectangular box are 8 cm thick, so the length of the box is twice the height (32 cm), and the width is also twice the height (32 cm).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - The top base of the box is a square with side length 32 cm.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - There are two edges for the box's height, and each edge is equal to the height since the height is 32 cm.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We can determine the coordinates of the center point \(P\) of one base and the coordinates of the corner \(Q\) of the opposite base.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For an edge of 32 cm:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Center of the edge} = \left( \frac{32}{2}, \frac{32}{2}, 0 \right) = (16, 16, 0) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This corresponds to vertex \(C\) at \((16, 16, 0)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For the opposite base, it is a square of side length 32 cm, so the center of this base \(Q\) is 16 cm away from each of its opposite corners. Since any point on the square will be the same distance from both corners, the coordinates for center \(Q\) would be:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Center of the base} = (16-8, 16, 0), (16+8, 16, 0) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's compute these coordinates:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ (16-8, 16, 0) = (8, 16, 0) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ (16+8, 16, 0) = (24, 16, 0) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, since \(P\) is at (16, 16) and the center \(Q\) of the opposite base is at (24, 16, 0), the distance \(p\) from \(P\) to \(Q\) can be found using the distance formula in 3D:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ p = \sqrt{(24-16)^2 + (16-16)^2 + (0-0)^2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ p = \sqrt{2^2 + 0 + 0} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ p = \sqrt{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ p = 2 \text{ cm} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the distance from the center point \(P\) of one square base to the corner \(Q\) of the opposite base is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\boxed{2}\]<|endoftext|>
