[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let \[a = 5b \] and \[b = 23 \cdot 2 \cdot b = 46b\], so
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\begin{aligned} 5 &= 5b \cdot 2 = 2 \cdot 5b,\\ 23 &= 23b \cdot 2 = 9 \cdot 2 \cdot 23b,\\ \therefore 46 &= 5b \cdot 23b \cdot 2 = b \cdot (9 \cdot 2 \cdot 23b) \cdot 2 = 3 \cdot 5 = 15 \cdot b \cdot 46b \cdot 2.\end{aligned}\] Since the base $b$ must be greater than 8, $b = 15$. The answer is 15.
