[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For $\bold{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ -4 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\bold{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix},$ compute $\text{proj}_{\bold{w}} \bold{v}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find $\text{proj}_{\bold{w}} \bold{v}$, we first need to compute the projection matrix $\text{proj}_{\bold{w}} \bold{v}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Textbook solver:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{proj}_{\bold{w}} \bold{v} = \frac{\bold{v} \cdot \bold{w}}{\bold{w} \cdot \bold{w}} \bold{w}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Multiplying $\bold{v}$ and $\bold{w}$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 0 \cdot 2 + (-4) \cdot 2 + 1 \cdot (-1) = -9
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Computing $\bold{w} \cdot \bold{w}$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2 \cdot 2 + 2 \cdot 2 + (-1) \cdot (-1) = 9
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{proj}_{\bold{w}} \bold{v} = \frac{-9}{9} \bold{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ -1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
