[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the maximum value of $y$ for the equation $y = -x^2 + 5$, we need to analyze the quadratic function.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$y = -x^2 + 5$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Was perfect for use of graphing calculator in finding the maximum or minimum. It is a parabola as it opens downwards because of the negative sign outside the equation. The highest point/rail on the graph gives us the maximum point.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\begin{vmatrix} -1 & 0 & 5 \end{vmatrix}=\frac{(5)^{2}-(-1)}{2}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\displaystyle \frac{24}{2}=-12$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore $y$ reaches its maximum point at $12$ on the graph.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\boxed{y=12}$<|endoftext|>
