[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If $x \diamondsuit y = 3x + 5y$ for all $x$ and $y$, then what is the value of $2 \diamondsuit 7$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$2\,\diamondsuit\, 7 = (2x)_\Diamond_ (7y)...eq. 1$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This means the value of $y$ must be 6. If we use 6 in the above equation, we find $$2, 7= 3(2) + 5(6).$$ The value of $x$ is $13$ since, using the $x \diamondsuit$ operation, we find $$13 = 3(13) + 5(1) = 41$$ by orignally calculating. We therefore find $2 \Diamondsuit 7 = 41.$
