[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve this problem, you first list the first eight prime numbers. These are 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, and 19. Note that the first prime number is 2 and the last is 19. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, you draw two numbers without replacement from the list, 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, and 19. The sum of these digits is 2+3+5+7+11+13+17+19 = 71. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m You need to check if 71 is a prime number. A prime number has only two positive divisors (1 and itself), so any number greater than one is not prime.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
