[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Chris and Nathan order a giant cookie together. If Chris eats $\frac{2}{7}$ of the cookie and Nathan eats $\frac{3}{5}$ of the cookie, what fraction of the original cookie is left?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\begin{aligned} &\text {original \ cookie } = \frac{2 \times 5}{7} + \frac{3 \times 7}{5} \\\\ &\text{Since}\ 7\ &\text{and}\ 5\text{ are relatively prime}\ \text{'s}\ \text{product in both numerator and denominator}; \\\\ &\frac{2}{7} + \frac{3}{5} = \frac{2 \times 5 + 7 \times 3}{5 \times 7} = \frac{1}{1} \end{aligned}$<|endoftext|>
