[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given $\delta(x) = 3x + 8$ and $\phi(x) = 8x + 7$, what is $x$ if $\delta(\phi(x)) = 7$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Start by substituting $\phi(x)$ into the first function, $\delta$, to arrive at the equation $\delta(8x + 7) = 7$. Next, use the definition of the $\delta$-function \begin{equation*} \delta(m) = \frac{1}{\text{val}(m-E)} \end{equation*} to see the ratio $7 \div (\text{val}(E) - 8)$. As $x$ varies, $\text{val}(E)$ stays constant, so we only need to solve \begin{equation*} 7 = \frac{1}{\text{val}(E) - 8} \end{equation*} for $\text{val}(E)$, which looks like: \begin{align*} 7 (\text{val}(E)-8)&=1 \\ 7 \cdot 1-\text{val}(E)&=1 \\ 7- \text{val}(E)&=1 \\ \text{val}(E)&=6 \end{align*} Now, $x$ is a function of $\text{val}(E)$, so we must look up $\text{val}(E)$ in this formula at $\delta(6)$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \delta(6)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m &= \frac{1}{4} \\ &\end{align*} Therefore, $\delta(6.25)$ refers to the third decimal place in 6.25, so the middle three digits are $\text{val}(E)$. So $\delta(6.25)$ is $7$.
