[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the matrix that corresponds to projecting onto the vector \(\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\), we need to use the formula for the projection of a vector \(\mathbf{v}\) onto another vector \(\mathbf{w} \neq \mathbf{0}\). The projection matrix \(P\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ P = \frac{\mathbf{w} \mathbf{w}^T}{\mathbf{w}^T \mathbf{w}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Here, the vector \(\mathbf{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\). Let's find the transpose of \(\mathbf{w}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \mathbf{w}^T = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we compute the dot product \(\mathbf{w}^T \mathbf{w}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \mathbf{w}^T \mathbf{w} = 2^2 + (-3)^2 = 4 + 9 = 13
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the projection matrix \(P\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P = \frac{\mathbf{w} \mathbf{w}^T}{\mathbf{w}^T \mathbf{w}} = \frac{1}{13} \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -3 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \frac{1}{13} \begin{pmatrix} 4 & -6 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{4}{13} & -\frac{6}{13} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the matrix that corresponds to projecting onto the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{4}{13} & -\frac{6}{13} \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
