[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - The GCF of $(3x^2 - 5x + 4)$ and $(7 \_ 2x)$ can be found by focusing on their common factors. The coefficient of the GCF is 7, while the constant terms have the relationship $3 - 7 = -4$. Identifying the GCF thus is $7 \_ 4 \cdot $x \_ (-)1 \_4 \_(-1 \_ − \_1}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Hence, '-The greatest common factor is GCF: 7', indicating that considering the difference of their weights (work), it takes into account the largest factor common to both.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - For the numerical part, $7 \cdot 4 = 28$ and $-1 \cdot 4 = -4$, then $GCF: 28 \_ (-)\_4 \cdot $=—1' or $24$.
