[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The probability that the sum of the results of rolling a standard six-sided die six times is a prime number is \(\left( \frac{6 - 1}{6 - 1} \right)^6 \times \text{probability of rolling a 2-6 from die 1-6}\). This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \left( \frac{5}{5} \right)^6 \times \left( \frac{1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 1^5}{8} \right) = 1 \times \left( \frac{5}{8} \right)^6
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The value \(\left( \frac{5}{8} \right)^6\) is approximately \(0.06871875\), so the final probability is approximately \(0.069\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the probability that the sum of all the results is a prime number is \(\boxed{\frac{1}{13}}\).
