[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine how many minutes it will take my friend to read the same novella, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. **Understand the given information:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Friend reads three times as fast as I do.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - It takes me 2 hours to read a novella.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - We need to convert my reading speed (speed for another person) to minutes per hour and then convert the time required for my friend to read the same novella to minutes.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. **Calculate my reading speed in minutes per hour:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Given that the friend reads three times as fast as I do, my reading speed is \(\frac{3}{1} \text{ times}\) my speed per hour.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Linear speed: \(\frac{3}{1}\) times faster per hour.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. **Convert the friend's reading time to hours and then convert the author's reading time to hours:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - The author takes 2 hours to read the novella.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Since I read 1 hour (1.00) per friend, our friend takes \(\frac{2}{1}\) hours to read the same novella.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. **Calculate the friends reading time in minutes:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - \(\frac{2}{1}\) hours is 2 hours.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Since the friend reads 1 hour per friend, it will take my friend 2 hours to read the novella.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. **Convert my friend's reading time from hours to minutes:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - 2 hours \(\times 60\) minutes per hour = \boxed{120} minutes.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, it will take my friend 120 minutes to read the same novella.<|endoftext|>
