[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the value of \( x \), we need to use the fact that the sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always \( 180^\circ \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \angle A = x^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \angle B = 2x^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \angle C = 5x^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we substitute the given values into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x + 2x + 5x = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 8x = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find \( x \), we divide both sides of the equation by 8:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x = \frac{180^\circ}{8}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Perform the division:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x = 22.5^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
