[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A box contains 4 white balls and 4 black balls.  I draw them out of the box, one at a time.  What is the probability that all of my draws alternate colors?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ↵ easify the choices.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ↵ We have 4 white balls and 4 black balls, total of 8 balls.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ↵ What are the possible outcomes? I'll draw the first ball and record my choice. Then, since I want them to alternate colors, the next ball would be black, thus eliminating the second white ball. We have now drawn two white balls and two black balls. The third ball can either be white or black, but since we already have two of the colors, the third ball will be black.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ↵ A total of 3 events.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ↵ There are 2 ways to get it: white, black are black, white are black.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ↵ Thus, the probability that all the arrangements alternate colors is the number of favorable events divided by the total number of events.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ↵ The probability is 5/8 or 0.625
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ↵ Therefore, the answer is: ↷
