[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Convert the fraction to a decimal (if needed for percentage):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    0.025
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the estimated tax rate for an assessed house at $160,000 is $0.025 or 2.5%.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. **Calculate the tax for a house assessed at $\$160,000$:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \text{Tax} = \text{Assessed property} \times \text{Estimated rate} = \$160,000 \times 0.025 = \$4,000
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the tax for a house assessed at \$160,000 is \(\boxed{4000}\) dollars.
