[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The total number of outcomes is $25 \choose 3$, and there must be $2$ones in any group of $3$ ($25 = 4 \cdot 21$) to be able to defend them. Therefore, $A_3(25) = \frac{(4 \cdot 21)!}{2!22!} = \frac{25 \times 24 \times 23 \times 22!}{2!22!} = \frac{25 \times 24 \times 23}{2}$.
