[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m What is half of the absolute value of the difference of the squares of 18 and 16?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Sure. Let's solve the problem step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Find the squares of 16 and 18:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    16 = 16
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    18 = 18
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Find the absolute value of the difference between the squares of 16 and 18:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    18^2 - 16^2 = 324 - 256 = 68
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Find the absolute value of the square root of 68:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    sqrt(68) = 2\sqrt{17}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Now, we need the absolute value of the difference between the squares of 16 and 18:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    sqrt(68) - 16 = 2\sqrt{17} - 16
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. Finally, divide the absolute value of the difference of the squares by 1.5 to get half:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    (2\sqrt{17} - 16) ÷ 1.5 = (2\sqrt{17} - 16) - 1 = 2\sqrt{17} - 17
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, half of the absolute value of the difference of the squares of 18 and 16 is 2\sqrt{17} - 17.
