[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We first isolate \( x^2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x^2 + 9 = 10 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x^2 = 10 - 9 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x^2 = 1. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, take the square roots of both sides to solve for \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x = \pm \sqrt{1}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x = \pm 1. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The sum of all possible values of \( x \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 1 + (-1) = 0. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
