[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. $\angle GEL = 80^\circ$ (given).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since points $B$, $I$, and $L$ are collinear, we can find $\angle BILL$ by considering the sum of the angles in triangle $BILL$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
