[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve the problem, you need to compute $\dfrac{9!}{6!3!}$, which is the same as $\dfrac{(9)(8)(7)(6)!}{(6)(5)(4)(3)!}$. This simplifies to $\dfrac{9 \times 8 \times 7}{1 \times 2 \times 3} \times \dfrac{1 \times 2 \times 3!}{1 \times 2} = \dfrac{9 \times 8 \times 7}{2 \times 3} \times \dfrac{6 \times 5!}{1} = 10 \times 7 = 70$. The answer is 70. admirable
