[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In how many ways can 5 different keys be placed on a keychain?  (Two arrangements are considered the same if one can be rotated or flipped to be identical to the other.)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the number of ways to arrange 5 different keys on a keychain, we need to calculate the number of unique permutations. We can think of this as selecting an order for 5 keys, and then fixing the positions of all other keys.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The formula for the number of permutations of n distinct objects taken r at a time, where order matters, is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\#P(r)\ = \frac{n!}{(n-r)!} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Where n is the total number of items to choose from and r is the number of items to place.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In this case, we are choosing 5 keys from a set of 5 keys, so n = 5. So the calculation would be:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ r! = 5! \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\#P(r) = \frac{5!}{(5-5)!} = \frac{5!}{0!}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To calculate the factorial of zero, which is also zero, we calculate 5!. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\#P(1)=5!\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = 120
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the number of permutations of choosing 5 keys from 5 different keys without any restrictions is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\boxed{120} \]
