[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Question 1: Applying the Simple Regression Model to the Tag Info Company
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m GoldenGate (GSFT) has acquired BatteryInsight Solutions in a broad array of business verticals. The relationship between the Tag Info Company's stock price ($x$) and the average monthly mortality rate ($y$), given by the simple regression model:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x = 0.016y\,\, \text{(Note: $x$ is the annual number of earthquake disasters, $y$ is the annual number of earthquake disasters in every 100 sq km.)}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We need to find the point estimate of $y$ given that an average earthquake is occurring every 18th day and the standard deviation is 3 days.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Steps to solve:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Use the binomial distribution to model yearly occurrences: 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    X \sim Poisson(\lambda = \frac{\text{average deaths per year}}{\text{sqrt(count days per 100 sq km)}}) = x\,\, \text{(average deaths per year)}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Calculate the mean and variance of a single occurrence:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \mu = \text{average deaths per year} \times \frac{18}{\sqrt{100}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \sigma^2 = \text{standard deviation}^2 \times \frac{\text{mean}}{100^2} = 3^2 \times \frac{\text{average deaths per year}}{100^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Then, for the mean, use it to find the estimate of y.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Question 2: Finding the P-value in the Multiple Comparisons ANOVA Technique
