[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Question 3: Shooting and Haircut Accuracy Pairs
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In a simple random sample of 100 men with a male haircut consent rate of 20% out of a total of 1000 officers, the safety complaint ratio is 12.31. We assume the number of men from each subgroup (male and female) may significantly influence this ratio.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Cases to Match:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Case: Gender (Male, Female)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Match: \(\text{Ratio} = 2\%\frac{male}\text{ to }female\frac{whole\ text{ male}}{male\ \text{and\ \female}}\text{ as a simple as possible.}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Steps to find the Observed Ratio:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Given task: for officers who meet Condition 1 (Male), the ratio is 12.31.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Use the condition to derive the ratio of male-friendly officers: 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \text{conditioned\ ratio} = \frac{12.31}{12.31 + 0.2*0.2*0.8}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Further calculate:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \text{male\ ratio} = 1000*0.991*0.993*0.65
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Then, calculate the actual ratio using the actual condition numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{actual\ ratio} = \frac{12.31*1000*0.991*0.993*0.65}{\text{conditioned ratio}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **P-val calculation:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Observed Ratio} = 12.31*2.6*x*\frac{male}{female}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{MyPVal} = (12.31 - 12.30)ed Var(X) + (12.30 - 12.30)ed Var(X)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Summary
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For the p-values in Question 1, they are independence relationships within the adjustment model.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
