[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Compute $\tan 30^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To compute $\tan 30^\circ$, we will use the relationship between the tangent function and the sine and cosine functions. The tangent of an angle is defined as the ratio of the sine of the angle to the cosine of the angle.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \tan 30^\circ = \frac{\sin 30^\circ}{\cos 30^\circ}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We know the values of $\sin 30^\circ$ and $\cos 30^\circ$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sin 30^\circ = \frac{1}{2} \quad \text{and} \quad \cos 30^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substituting these values into the tangent formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \tan 30^\circ = \frac{\frac{1}{2}}{\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To simplify the fraction $\frac{\frac{1}{2}}{\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}}$, we multiply by the reciprocal of the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \tan 30^\circ = \frac{1}{2} \times \frac{2}{\sqrt{3}} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To rationalize the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by $\sqrt{3}$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \tan 30^\circ = \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} \times \frac{\sqrt{3}}{\sqrt{3}} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the value of $\tan 30^\circ$ is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{\frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
