[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m raising a polynomial to the power, simply means raising each term inside the polynomial to the power, so √(9 3) can be expressed as 9^1/2 * 9^3/2. Applying the exponent property of multiplication, 9^1/2 * 9^3/2 can simplify to (9^1/2)^3. This completely equals 9^3/2.
