[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The points $(x, y)$ represented in this table lie on a straight line. The point $(28, t)$ lies on the same line. What is the value of $t?$ \begin{tabular}{c|c}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $x$ & $y$ \\ \hline
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1 & 7 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3 & 13 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5 & 19 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{tabular}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the value of \(t\), we need to identify the equation of the line that passes through the points \((1, 7)\) and \((3, 13)\). The general form of a linear equation is \(y = mx + b\), where \(m\) is the slope and \(b\) is the y-intercept.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we calculate the slope \(m\) using the slope formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m m = \frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Here, \((x_1, y_1) = (1, 7)\) and \((x_2, y_2) = (3, 13)\). Plugging in these values, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m m = \frac{13 - 7}{3 - 1} = \frac{6}{2} = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the slope \(m\) is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we use the point-slope form of the equation of a line, which is \(y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)\), and substitute the slope \(m = 3\) and one of the points, say \((1, 7)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m y - 7 = 3(x - 1)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We also know that one of the points is \((3, 13)\), and we can substitute this point into the equation to solve for \(b\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 13 - 7 = 3(3 - 1)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplify both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6 = 3 \cdot 2 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This confirms that \(b = 6\). Therefore, the equation of the line is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m y - 7 = 3(x - 1)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We can now convert this into the slope-intercept form \(y = mx + b\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m y - 7 = 3x - 3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Add 7 to both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m y = 3x - 3 + 7
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m y = 3x + 4
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the point-slope form of the equation is \(y = 3x + 4\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find \(t\), we need to substitute the coordinates \((28, t)\) into the equation of the line:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m t = 3(28) + 4
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Calculate the value:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m t = 84 + 4 = 88
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the value of \(t\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{88}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
