[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m What is the greatest multiple of 3 that is less than 500 and is also a multiple of 4?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the greatest multiple of 3, 4 less than 500, we should find a multiple of 12 (the least common multiple that is both 3 and 4) and 500 if necessary.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We have 500/3 = 166... remainder 2. This means the greatest multiple of 3 less than 500 but with no multiples of 12 will be 3162, because we are adding 6 more zeros, not allowing us to add multiples of 12 that would exceed 500.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we go to the multiples of 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2, 6, 10, 14, 18, 22, 26, 30, 34, 38, 42, 46, 50, 54, 58,...
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This sequence is just skipping ones. In fact, it is equivalent to writing out the familiar prefixes.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So the required multiple of 3 and 4 that is less than 500 is 3162 - 2162 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ionalesim}
