[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $n$ be a primitve non-integer, i.e. negative.  Let each $0 < x_{i} < 1$ for every $i$ algebraics $\alpha _{i}, \dots , \beta _{n}$.  Without loss of generality, we can assume that $\alpha _{1}\leq \alpha _{2}$(since otherwise, we just multiply by $1/n$).  Change $x_{1}$ to $\ln n$ for non-integer $x$ and we get:  $$\text{ROOTED binary tree with }n \text{ nodes and }n \text{ leaves}$$ $$\text{Let nodes have a single leaf, call that their ulder leaf}$$ $$\text{Same as, rooted binary tree with sub-tablet over the leaves with same leaf order}$$ $$\text{Same as, star tree which has different leaf order}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\text{Sum: 4log(n)}$  $$\text{And you add four zeros to get } \frac{1}{2} n^4 \implies \frac{1}{4} \iff n^4$$
