[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the positive base \( b \) that satisfies the equation \( 5_b \cdot 23_b = 151_b \), we will convert the numbers from base \( b \) to base 10, perform the multiplication, and then convert the result back to base \( b \). The equation then becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5b \cdot 2b + 23b + 28b = 151b
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 111b = 151b
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m By subtracting \( 111b \) from both sides, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 0 = 40b
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This tells us that \( b \) must be 5. Let's verify this by substituting \( b = 5 \) back into the original equation to ensure it holds true.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, calculate \( 5_5 \cdot 23_5 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5_5 = 5 \\ 23_5 = 2 \cdot 5^1 + 3 \cdot 5^0 = 10 + 3 = 13; \\ 5_5 \cdot 23_5 = 15 \text{ in base 10}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This is evident because \( 40b = 40 \cdot 5 = 200_{10}. \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since \( 151_5 = 11 \cdot 5^2 + 1 \cdot 5^1 + 1 \cdot 5^0 = 205 \text{ in base 10}, \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 151_5 = 1015_5
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This confirms that our solution is correct.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The positive base \( b \) is \boxed{5}.<|endoftext|>
