[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the range of the function \( h(x) = 2f(x) - 7 \), we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. **Determine the range of \( f(x) \) given that the range of \( f(x) \) is \([-3, 5]\).**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Since \( f(x) \) is a continuous function and its range is \([-3, 5]\), and it is defined for all real numbers \( x \), we can describe the range of \( f(x) \) as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    -5 \leq f(x) \leq 5
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    This means that the values of \( f(x) \) are in the range \([-5, 5]\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. **Determine the range of \( h(x) = 2f(x) - 7 \).**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Since \( f(x) \) has the range \([5, 5]\), we can calculate \( 2f(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    2f(x) \geq 2 \cdot 5 = 10
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    This means that \( 2f(x) \) ranges from \([5, 10]\). Next, we need to subtract 7 from \( 2f(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    h(x) = 2f(x) - 7 \leq 10 - 7 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Therefore, the range of \( h(x) \) is \([3, 10]\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. **Translate the range back to the original domain of \( h(x) \).**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Since the range of \( h(x) \) is the same as the range of \( f(x) \) because \( h(x) = 2f(x) - 7 \) maps values within the range of \( f(x) \) to values within \( h(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    h(x) = 2f(x) - 7
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    The range of \( h(x) \) will be the same as the range of \( f(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    h(x) = 2f(x) - 7 \subseteq [-3, 5]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the range of the function \( h(x) \) is:
