[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We should analyze the value. First, we need to know that a prime number has only 2 distinct divisors. To get a prime number, we can give it more than one divisors. Having one or some divisors is a practical scenario when combining a number without other as its factors, such as in the equation (10 = 33 × 3).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, the expression $7 + (30 \times N)$ simplifies becoming $33 + (72 N)$.
