[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m we need to solve the equations formed by equating the vector values at their respective points.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. **Equating the vector values:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -7 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 3 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -5 \\ 4/3 \end{pmatrix} + u \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 4 \\ 1/3 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. **Separating variables and collecting coefficients:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    4 - 7t + tu = -2 + 2u - 5t + tu
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Simplify by removing \( tu \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    4 - 7t = -2 + 2u - 5t
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    4 + 2 = 2u + 7t
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    6 = 2u + 7t
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    3 = u + 3.5t
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. **Solving for \( t \) in terms of \( u \):**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    t = \frac{3 - 3u}{3.5}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    t = \frac{6}{7} - \frac{6u}{7}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
