[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find $\csc 330^\circ$, first recall that $\csc\theta = \frac{1}{\sin\theta}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In this case, we have $\theta = 330^\circ$. So, to find $\csc 330^\circ$, we need to calculate $\sin 330^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $330^\circ$ is in the fourth quadrant, where the sine function is negative. Therefore, we'll use the property that $\sin(\pi - \theta) = \sin \theta$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, $\sin 330^\circ = \sin (360^\circ - 30^\circ) = \sin 30^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since $\sin 30^\circ = \frac{1}{2}$, we find that $\csc 330^\circ$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\csc 330^\circ = \frac{1}{\sin 330^\circ} = \frac{1}{\frac{1}{2}} = 2$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
