[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the value of \( n \) such that \( t_n = \frac{19}{87} \) for the given sequence defined by \( t_1 = 1 \) and for \( n > 1 \) by \( t_n = 1 + t_{n/2} \) when \( n \) is even, and by \( t_n = \frac{1}{t_{n-1}} \) when \( n \) is odd, we will simulate the sequence until we reach \( t_n = \frac{19}{87} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Start with \( n_1 = 1 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Compute \( t_2 \) using the recursive formula for even \( n > 1 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Compute \( t_3 \) using the recursive formula for odd \( n > 2 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Continue this process until \( t_n = \frac{19}{87} \).
