[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In how many ways can four people sit in a row of five chairs?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To calculate the number of ways four people can sit in a row of five chairs, we will use the concept of permutations. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The number of permutations of r items is given by the formula: P_r(n, k) = n! / (n-k)!, where n is the total number of items, and k is the number of items we want to arrange (which is less than n).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In this case, we have four people (n = 4), and we want to arrange them in five rows (which means we have 5 - 4 = 1 chair left to leave). So, k must be 1.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Using the formula, we get the total number of permutations of five chairs with four people:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P_5(4, 1) = 4! / (4-1)!
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m             = 4! / 3!
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m             = (4 × 3 × 2 × 1) / (3 × 2 × 1)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m             = 4
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, there are 4 ways for four people to sit in a row of five chairs.
