[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve this problem, we need to find all real numbers \( x \) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \left\lfloor x \lfloor x \rfloor \right\rfloor = 29
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, let's denote \( \lfloor x \rfloor \) as \( n \). This means that the floor function \( \lfloor x \rfloor \) provides the greatest integer less than or equal to \( x \), and \( \lfloor x \rfloor = n \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \left\lfloor x \cdot n \right\rfloor = 29
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For this to be true, \( 29 \) must be between \( x \cdot n \) and \( x \cdot (n+1) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 29 \leq x \cdot n < 30
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we solve this inequality for \( x \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Divide both sides by \( n \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 29 \leq x \cdot \frac{n}{n} < 30
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 29 \leq x < 30
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Since \( \lfloor x \rfloor = n \), we need \( n \leq x < n+1 \). 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Combining these two inequalities, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m n \leq x < 30
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, \( x \) must be in this interval:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x = n \quad \text{or} \quad x = n+1, \quad \text{where } n \in \mathbb{N}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find specific values of \( x \) that satisfy \( \left\lfloor x \lfloor x \rfloor \right\rfloor = 29 \), we consider possible values for \( n \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - If \( n = 10 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x \leq 10 \quad \text{and} \quad x < 30
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
