[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Finally we try values for \(x\) and verify for \(y\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{gathered}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x = 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m y = 3 \Rightarrow 10(4)(3) + 14(4) + 15(3) = 120 + 56 + 45 = 221 \neq 166 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{gathered}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{gathered}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x = 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m y = 4 \Rightarrow 10(4)(4) + 14(4) + 15(4) = 160 + 56 + 60 = 276 \neq 166 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{gathered}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Here's the key, trying each possible value for \(x\) and verifying if there's an corresponding \(y\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{gathered}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x = 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m y = 12 \Rightarrow 10(1)(12) + 14(1) + 15(12) = 120 + 14 + 180 = 314 \neq 166 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{gathered}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, we might try a value for \(x\) that needs to satisfy it under another equation, and then return to \(x, y\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{gathered}
