[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A church, also known as a basilica, is a monumental church in the Roman Catholic and Oriental Catholic belief group, which stands as the most Holy of worship and prayer places. Its primary purpose is for religious purposes, which also have some prestige and commercial importance. Within the Roman Catholic set theory, they are renowned for a profound doctrine known as papal infallibility. As part of the Roman Catholic faith, the pope is, by definition, the sole infallible authority on matters of belief, and they maintain a binding obligation to confess and absolve error. They can send cardinals and the pope even send himself, in the sacrament of an indulgence, to appear before the bishop of Rome, and can bring them on a trip to Rome themselves, or appoint them special commissions; all such actions are accompanied by absolution from sin.
