[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Sure, let's solve the inequality \( |x - 1| + |x + 2| < 5 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 1: Understand the absolute value functions. The expression \( |x - 1| \) represents the distance between \( x \) and 1 on the number line, and \( |x + 2| \) represents the distance between \( x \) and -2 on the number line. These distances are all non-negative.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 2: Break it down into different cases based on their relative positions:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Case 1: \( x \geq 1 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ |x - 1| = x - 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      So, the inequality becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ x - 1 + x + 2 < 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ 2x + 1 < 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ 2x < 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ x < 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      Combining with \( x \geq 1 \), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ 1 \leq x < 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Case 2: \( x < 1 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ |x - 1| = 1 - x \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      So, the inequality becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ 1 - x + x + 2 < 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ 3 < 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      This is always true for any \( x < 1 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Case 3: \( x = 1 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ |x - 1| = 1 - 1 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ |x + 2| = 1 + 2 = 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      So, the inequality becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ 0 + 3 < 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[ 3 < 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      This is false, so there are no values of \( x \) in this case.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Combining all the cases, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 1 \leq x < 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the solution to the inequality is \( \boxed{1 \leq x < 2} \).<|endoftext|>
