[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve the equation \(-9x^2 - 3x + 2 = 0\), we will use the quadratic formula, which is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In this equation, the coefficients are:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - \( a = -9 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - \( b = -3 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - \( c = 2 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's substitute these values into the quadratic formula.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Calculate the discriminant (\( \Delta \)):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \Delta = b^2 - 4ac \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \Delta = (-3)^2 - 4(-9)(2) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \Delta = 9 + 72 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \Delta = 81 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Substitute the values of \( a, b, \) and \( \Delta \) into the quadratic formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x = \frac{-(-3) \pm \sqrt{81}}{2(-9)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x = \frac{3 \pm 9}{-18} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Solve for \( x \) in two possible cases:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x_1 = \frac{3 + 9}{-18} = \frac{12}{-18} = -\frac{2}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x_2 = \frac{3 - 9}{-18} = \frac{-6}{-18} = \frac{1}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since \( x > 0 \), we select the solution \( x = \frac{1}{3} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \boxed{\text{The solution is } \frac{1}{3}} \]<|endoftext|>
