[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m And shall put in front that expression in the equation above.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve the given equation, we start with the original logarithmic equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 16 \log_{5} \frac{5}{3} + \log_{5} 9 = \log_{5}(5 \sqrt{3}) + \log_{5} 10
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we can combine the logarithms on the right-hand side using the properties of logarithms. Recall that \(\log_{a} b + \log_{a} c = \log_{a} (b \cdot c)\). Thus:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \log_{5}(5 \sqrt{3}) + \log_{5} 10 = \log_{5} (5 \sqrt{3} \cdot 10) = \log_{5} (50 \sqrt{3})
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So the equation becomes:
