[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 16 \log_{5} \frac{5}{3} + \log_{5} 9 = 16 \log_{5} \frac{5}{3} + \log_{5} (50 \sqrt{3})
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, observe that the term \(\log_{5} (50 \sqrt{3})\) can be rewritten using the property of logarithms \(\log_{a} x + \log_{a} y = \log_{a} (xy)\). Here, \(x = 50\sqrt{3}\) and \(y = \sqrt{3}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \log_{5} (50 \sqrt{3}) = \log_{5} (50 \cdot (\sqrt{3})^2) = \log_{5} (50 \cdot 3) = \log_{5} 150
