[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      HN = 12.67
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. **Determine $\tan G$:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - The tangent of an angle in a right triangle is defined as the ratio of the length of the opposite side to the length of the adjacent side.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - In this case, $H$ is the opposite side with length 15, and $N$ is the adjacent side with length 8.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. **Calculate $\tan G$:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \tan G = \frac{H}{N}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \tan G = \frac{15}{8}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Conclusion: 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{\frac{15}{8}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
