[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we need to convert this decimal number to base-7.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To convert a decimal number to base-7, we repeatedly divide the number by 7 and keep track of the remainders. We then read the remainders from bottom to top.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, let's do the conversion from decimal to base-7:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. 1 ÷ 7 gives a remainder of 1. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. 1 ÷ 7 gives a remainder of 1.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we divide 1 by 7: quotient is 0, remainder is 1. 
