[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine the value of \( n \) in the equation \( 11^5 \equiv n \pmod{9} \), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. **Simplify \( 11 \mod 9 \):**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    11 \equiv 2 \pmod{9}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    This is because \( 11 \) and \( 9 \) have a common factor of \( 1 \) (since \( 9 = 9 \cdot 1 \) and \( 11 = 9 \cdot 1 + 2 \)).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. **Raise 11 to the power of 5 and then take modulo 9:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    11^5 \equiv 2^5 \pmod{9}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. **Calculate \( 2^5 \):**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    2^5 = 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 = 64
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. **Reduce the result modulo 9:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    64 \div 9 = 7 \text{ remainder } 1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    64 \equiv 1 \pmod{9}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the value of \( n \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{1}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
