[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Hamburgers consumption as a percentage} = \left(\frac{1}{3}\right) \times 100 \approx 33.333\%
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given that the budget is $30, we need to calculate the number of hamburgers that can be purchased with these funds. Using the percentage, we can compute:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Hamburgers purchase} = \frac{30 \times 33.333}{100} \approx 10 \text{ hamburgers}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, Urs maintains memory on hamburgers for \boxed{10} dollars.
