[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If March 1 is a Monday, what day of the week will it be 270 days later?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine the day of the week two weeks after March 1, a Monday, we first need to understand that there are 7 days in a week. Therefore, 270 days would be two times twelve weeks, i.e., \(2 \times 12 = 24 \text{ weeks}\) before Sunday on the original date.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since March 1 is a Monday, we can count backwards from Monday in 24 weeks:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Mon} - \text{Tues} - \text{Wed} - \text{Thu} - \text{Fri} - \text{SAT} - \text{Sun} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 24 weeks is a substantial number of weeks, so counting backward from Monday would result in us revisiting the same date, but in reverse. Therefore, the date where it would once again be Monday is after two weeks past. Therefore, the day of the week will be Saturday.
