[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Ryosuke is picking up his friend from work. The odometer reads 74,568 when he picks his friend up, and it reads 74,592 when he drops his friend off at his house. Ryosuke's car gets 28 miles per gallon and the price of one gallon of gas is $\$4.05$. What was the cost of the gas that was used for Ryosuke to drive his friend back home from work? (Express your answer in dollars and round to the nearest cent.)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the cost of the gas used, we'll follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Calculate the total distance driven:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We'll subtract the odometer reading when the car was dropped from when the car was picked up:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \Markdown
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```
