[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Simplify the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \sin 18^\circ \cos 12^\circ + \cos 162^\circ \cos 102^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Using the cosines and sine functions in supplementary angles,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \cos 162^\circ = -\cos 8^\circ \quad \text{and} \quad \cos 102^\circ = -\cos 8^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    So,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \cos 162^\circ \cos 102^\circ = (-\cos 8^\circ)(-\cos 8^\circ) = \cos^2 8^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \sin 18^\circ \cos 12^\circ + \cos 162^\circ \cos 102^\circ = \sin 18^\circ \cos 12^\circ + \cos^2 8^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Using the identity:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \sin 18^\circ = 2 \sin 9^\circ \cos 9^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    And
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \cos 12^\circ = 2 \cos 6^\circ \sin 6^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    So our expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    2 \sin 9^\circ \cos 9^\circ \cdot 2 \cos 6^\circ \sin 6^\circ + \cos^2 8^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Simplify the term involving 12 in the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \sin 18^\circ \cos 12^\circ + \cos^2 12^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    We observe that the denominator of the original fraction is:
