[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve this math problem, we need to evaluate the expression $99^3 + 3(99^2) + 3(99) + 1$. Let's break down each part step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Evaluate $99^3$: 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - $99 \times 99 \times 99 = 970299$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Evaluate $3(99^2)$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - $3 \times (99)^2 = 3 \times 9801 = 29403$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Evaluate $3(99) + 1$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - $3 \times 99 + 1 = 297 + 1 = 298$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we can sum all these parts together:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
