[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Do you know that $z^3$ can be written in the form $k+ia$, where $k$ and $a$ are real numbers?  This is from the power series for this function,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{align*} z^3 & = \sum_{n=0}^\infty C_n z^n\\ = C_0 z^0 + C_1 z^1 + C_2 z^2 + C_3 z^3 + \cdots \end{align*}So $C_3=100$ and $C_1 = 75,$ as well as $a=75$ Hence $z = 5$, and we have $|z| = \boxed{\sqrt{75+100}}= 2\sqrt{15}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Explanation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To begin answering, we should study $z^3 = 100+75i$, which means that $z^3 = 100+75i$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $z\cdot z\cdot z = 100+75i$, which means $z$ must also be a 3-dimensional complex number (real and imaginary part read as $z\cdot z\cdot z$).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Begin by also considering complex conjugates: if $w\neq z, zw\cdot zw = 100+75i$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For example, if we replace $z$ with $-z$, then we can place another 3-dimensional complex number aswell, $-z,\ 0+i.\ldots$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m All three numbers' 3-dimensional product will simplify to $0,\underbrace{75}_{\text{real inside }i3}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The first equation $z^3 = 100+75i$ therefore tells us that $\displaystyle (z-i)^3 = 100$ i.e. by substituting that in place of $z$ we eventually find that $\displaystyle z+i=100^{1/3},-\sqrt{75}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This finally confirms that $z=100^{1/3}+i=5+7i$. .
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Subtracting $z$ from $z^3, z^3-z=100$ shows that $|z|=2\sqrt{15}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m I think this raises the interesting point of... how is that possible other than \displaystyle \break $|z| = \sqrt{\Big( a_1 + a_2 + a_3\Big)^2 + \Big( b_1 + b_2 + b_3 \Big)^2} =$ \Big( $|a_1|^2+\ldots$ ... ...
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\displaystyle{=(a_1+0)^2+ \:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (a_2-i)^2 + (b_2+i)^2+ (b_3+i)^2}=$...
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m NOTE: You correctly continue the investigation! :)<|endoftext|>
