[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $p$ and $q$ satisfy $pq=9$ and $p+q=6$. What is the value of $p^2 + q^2$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the value of \( p^2 + q^2 \), we can use the given equations \( pq = 9 \) and \( p + q = 6 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we will square the sum of \( p \) and \( q \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (p + q)^2 = 6^2 = 36
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we will square the product \( pq \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (pq)^2 = 9^2 = 81
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we can use the identity for the square of a binomial to find \( p^2 + q^2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (p + q)^2 = p^2 + q^2 + 2pq
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substitute the known values:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 36 = p^2 + q^2 + 2pq
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We already know \( pq = 9 \), so we substitute \( 2pq \) with \( 2 \cdot 9 = 18 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 36 = p^2 + q^2 + 18
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Then, solve for \( p^2 + q^2 \) by isolating it on one side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m p^2 + q^2 = 36 - 18
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
