[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For how many values of the digit $A$ is it true that $63$ is divisible by $A$ and $273{,}1A2$ is divisible by $4$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m There are $9$ values of the digit $A$ that satisfy the given condition.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The required digit $+A$ such that the number $273A{,}1AB$ is divisible by $4$:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{split}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2\cdot3A{,}1\cdotA + 1 + 2\cdot1A{,}B\cdotA & = (3A+1)2\cdot1A{,}B + 5\cdot1A{,}B \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m & = 3A\cdot2A{,}B + A{,}B + 2\cdot1B{,}9 + A{,}B \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m & = 3A\cdot2A{,}B + 2\cdot1B{,}9 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m & \text{When }A = 9,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m & = 5\cdot2{,}B + B = 8B \\ & \text{When }A = 2,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m & = 5\cdot2{,}B + 2B + B = 10B \neq 0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m & \text{When }A = 8,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m & = 5\cdot2{,}B + 2B = 7B = 0 \neq 0 \hfill
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{split}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, $A = \boxed{9} $. deport explanation
