[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m odies were odd, or multiple of 3 if it was 12. So, include_kernelsize=off tells the ConvolutionKNN argument to indicate the output is a multiple of the kernel size, but arguments like demo [12, 30, 61, 140] specify the kernel size only to be a multiple of the arguement's size, then project filter(s) right out. The so-called flag for the CV transform utility library may mean different things depending on whether the ConvolutionKNN argument is a Convolution argument or a CV utility. Convolution arguments are arguements to the Convolution. For OpenCV2, CV utility arguments do not correspond to a Convolution flag: the CV utility functions are called KERNEx_Norm, which but not KERNEx_Kern2d. The only inbuilt utility with this extra and deprecated kern2dim value is KERNEx_HistogramAvg, for which the kernel is a 3x3 HAMMING window of width and height 2. Let's just for fun switch back to using the C library arguments:
