[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Solve the inequality
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[|x - 1| + |x + 2| < 5.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve the inequality \[|x - 1| + |x + 2| < 5,\] we need to consider the different cases based on the critical points where the expressions inside the absolute values change sign. These points are \(x = 1\) and \(x = -2\). Therefore, we will break the inequality into three separate inequalities and solve each one.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. \(x - 1 + x + 2 < 5\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. \(x - 1 + -(x + 2) < 5\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. \(-(x - 1) + -(x + 2) < 5\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's solve each inequality separately.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x - 1 + x + 2 < 5 \implies 2x + 1 < 5 \implies 2x < 4 \implies x < 2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x - 1 + -(x + 2) < 5 \implies x - 1 - x - 2 < 5 \implies -3 < 5 \quad \text{(always true, so this part doesn't provide new information)}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m -(x - 1) + -(x + 2) < 5 \implies -x + 1 - x - 2 < 5 \implies -2x - 1 < 5 \implies -2x < 6 \implies x > -3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So the final solution to the inequality is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m -3 < x < 2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's use Python to verify this solution.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m import numpy as np
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # Define the inequality function
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m def inequality_invariant(x):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     return abs(x-1) + abs(x+2) < 5 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # Test the left and right solutions
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m print("(1) -3 < 2:", inequality_invariant(1))
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m print("(2) -3 < -4:", inequality_invariant(-4))
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m print("(2) -2 < 2:", inequality_invariant(-2))
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```<|endoftext|>
