[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the number of positive 3-digit numbers that are divisible by 7, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 1: Find the largest 3-digit number that is divisible by 7.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The largest 3-digit number is 999. We can check if 999 is divisible by 7 by performing the division (999 / 7) = 142.3571. Since 142.3571 is not an integer, 999 is not divisible by 7. We continue to the next largest 3-digit number, which is 998. We can check if 998 is divisible by 7 by performing the division (998 / 7) = 142.5714. Since 142.5714 is not an integer, 998 is not divisible by 7.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 2: Find the smallest 3-digit number that is divisible by 7.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the smallest 3-digit number divisible by 7, we can start from 100 and keep subtracting 7 until we get a 3-digit number.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 100 - 7 = 93
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 93 - 7 = 86
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 86 - 7 = 79
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 79 - 7 = 72
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 72 - 7 = 65
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 65 - 7 = 58
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 58 - 7 = 51
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 51 - 7 = 44
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 44 - 7 = 37
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 37 - 7 = 30
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 30 - 7 = 23
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 23 - 7 = 16
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 16 - 7 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 9 - 7 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2 - 7 = -5
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since the smallest 3-digit number that is divisible by 7 is 2, the answer is the positive value less than 2. Therefore, there are 1 positive 3-digit numbers that are divisible by 7: 2, 10, 18, 26, 34, 42, 50.
