[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To convert $54321_6$ from base 6 to base 10, we first need to understand the value of each digit in base 6 and how to add them starting from the rightmost digit.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In base 6, the digits are represented as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The given number is $54321_6$. The leftmost digit is $5$, which is in base 10. The number 4 in base 6 is $4 \times 6^0 = 4_{\text{base}}$ as decimal.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To convert the remaining digits, move the decimal point 5 places to the left, indicating multiplication by 6. So, 3 becomes $3_6 \times 6^1 = 18_{\text{base}}$,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2 becomes $2 \times 6^2 = 72_{\text{base}}$,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1 becomes $1 \times 6^3 = 216_{\text{base}}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, adding these base 10 values together:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $5$, $18$, $72$, $216$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Adding these together:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $5 + 18 + 72 + 216 = 311$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the base 10 equivalent of $54321_6$ is $311$.<|endoftext|>
