[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the length of the diagonal connecting point \( A \) and point \( B \) in a rectangular prism where \( A \) is at \((0, 2)\) and \( B \) is at \((2, 0)\) with dimensions 10 inches by 20 inches by 10 inches, we use the 3-dimensional version of the Pythagorean theorem.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The formula for the diagonal \( C \) of a rectangular prism with given dimensions \( a \), \( b \), and \( c \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m C = \sqrt{a^2 + b^2 + c^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Here, the dimensions of the rectangular prism are:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - \( a = 10 \) inches
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - \( b = 20 \) inches
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - \( c = 10 \) inches
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substitute these values into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m C = \sqrt{10^2 + 20^2 + 10^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, calculate the squares of each dimension:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 10^2 = 100
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 20^2 = 400
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 10^2 = 100
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Add these squares together:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 100 + 400 + 100 = 600
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Finally, take the square root of the sum to find the length of the diagonal:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m C = \sqrt{600} = \sqrt{100 \times 6} = \sqrt{100} \times \sqrt{6} = 10 \sqrt{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the length of the diagonal connecting point \( A \) and point \( B \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{10 \sqrt{6}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
