[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A line is described by the equation $y-4=4(x-8)$. What is the sum of its $x$-intercept and $y$-intercept?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine the sum of the x-intercept and y-intercept of the given line, we need to first extract the intercepts from the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given equation: \( y - 4 = 4(x - 8) \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We will solve for the x-intercept by setting \( y = 0 \) and solving for \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 0 - 4 = 4(x - 8) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -4 = 4(x - 8) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ -1 = x - 8 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x - 8 = -1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x = -1 + 8 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x = 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the x-intercept is at \( (7, 0) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we will solve for the y-intercept by setting \( x = 0 \) and solving for \( y \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ y - 4 = 4(0 - 8) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ y - 4 = 4(-8) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ y - 4 = -32 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ y = -32 + 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ y = -28 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the y-intercept is at \( (0, -28) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Finally, we sum the x-intercept and y-intercept:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{x-intercept} = 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{y-intercept} = -28 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Sum} = 7 + (-28) = -21 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the sum of the x-intercept and y-intercept is \(\boxed{-21}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
