[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the maximum value of the expression \(\sqrt{x + 27} + \sqrt{13 - x} + \sqrt{x}\) for \(0 \le x \le 13\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. **Understand the Objective**: We want to maximize the function \(f(x) = \sqrt{x + 27} + \sqrt{13 - x} + \sqrt{x}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. **Evaluate at Boundary Points**: First, evaluate the function at the boundary points where all three terms are clear. These points are \(x = 0\), \(x = 13\), and \(x = 12\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. **Evaluating at Boundary Points**:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - For \(x = 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      f(0) = \sqrt{0 + 27} + \sqrt{13 - 0} + \sqrt{0} = \sqrt{27} + \sqrt{13} + 0 = 3\sqrt{3} + \sqrt{13}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - For \(x = 13\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      f(13) = \sqrt{13 + 27} + \sqrt{13 - 13} + \sqrt{13} = \sqrt{40} + 0 + \sqrt{13} = 2\sqrt{10} + \sqrt{13}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - For \(x = 12\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      f(12) = \sqrt{12 + 27} + \sqrt{13 - 12} + \sqrt{12} = \sqrt{39} + \sqrt{1} + \sqrt{12} = \sqrt{39} + 1 + 2\sqrt{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. **Compare Values**: Compare the values \(3\sqrt{3} + \sqrt{13}\), \(2\sqrt{10} + \sqrt{13}\), and \(\sqrt{39} + 1 + 2\sqrt{3}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - First comparison:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      3\sqrt{3} + \sqrt{13} \approx 3 \times 1.732 + 3.606 = 5.196 + 3.606 = 8.802 \quad (\text{Value})
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      2\sqrt{10} + \sqrt{13} \approx 2 \times 3.162 + 3.606 = 6.324 + 3.606 = 9.93 \quad (\text{Value})
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \sqrt{39} + 1 + 2\sqrt{3} \approx 1.979 + 1 + 2 \times 1.732 = 1.979 + 1 + 3.464 = 6.443 \quad (\text{Value})
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    3\sqrt{3} + \sqrt{13} \quad \text{is less than} \quad 2\sqrt{10} + \sqrt{13}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    3\sqrt{3} + \sqrt{13} \quad \text{is less than} \quad \sqrt{39} + 1 + 2\sqrt{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. **Conclusion**: The maximum value occurs at \(x = 0\), where the value is \(3\sqrt{3} + \sqrt{13}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
