[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 9^2 = 81
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 10^2 = 100
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 11^2 = 121
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 12^2 = 144
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 13^2 = 169
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 14^2 = 196
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 15^2 = 225
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 16^2 = 256
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 17^2 = 289
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 18^2 = 324
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 19^2 = 361
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 20^2 = 400
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We see that the perfect squares between 200 and 300 are 4, 16, 25, 29, 36, 49, 324 (200^2-169), 49, 36.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, there are 8 perfect squares between 200 and 300.
