[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To compute $\dbinom{7}{4}$, we can use the formula for combinations, which is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\dbinom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For $\dbinom{7}{4}$, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\dbinom{7}{4} = \frac{7!}{4!(7-4)!}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = $\frac{7!}{4!3!}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = $\frac{7 \times 6 \times 5 \times 4!}{4! \times 3!}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = $\frac{7 \times 6 \times 5}{3!}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = $\frac{5 \times 6 \times 5}{3 \times 2 \times 1}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = $\frac{5 \times 6}{2 \times 1}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = $\frac{30}{2}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = 15
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, $\dbinom{7}{4} = 15$.
