[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 1: Since we will be using the property of the inverse matrices, we can write the product \(\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B}\) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \mathbf{A}\mathbf{B} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 1 & -2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 2: Now, we need to find the inverse of this product, which is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 1 & -2 \end{pmatrix}^{-1}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 3: If we denote the inverse by \(\mathbf{A}^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 1 \\ 0 & -3 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\mathbf{B}^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 5 \\ -1 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\), then the inverse of their product is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 1 & -2 \end{pmatrix}^{-1} = \frac{1}{0 \times (-3) - 1 \times 1} \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -2 \\ -1 & 1 \end{pmatrix} = -\frac{1}{-3} \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -2 \\ -1 & 1 \end{pmatrix} = \frac{1}{3} \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -2 \\ -1 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{3} & \frac{2}{3} \\ -\frac{1}{3} & \frac{1}{3} \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
