[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Three faces of a right rectangular prism have areas of 48, 49 and 50 square units. What is the volume of the prism, in cubic units? Express your answer to the nearest whole number.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 1: Identify the three given lengths of the prism's faces.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - The area of one face is 48 square units.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - The area of the other face is 49 square units.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - The area of the third face is 50 square units.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 2: Calculate the area of the unknown face.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We know the sum of the areas of the three given faces is equal to the area of the unknown face. Let's denote the area of this unknown face as \( A \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 48 + 49 + 50 = A
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Adding the areas of the three given faces:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 147 = A
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 3: Calculate the volume of the prism.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The volume \( V \) of a rectangular prism is found by multiplying the area of one face by the length of the prism.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m V = \text{Area of the unknown face} \times \text{length of the prism}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since \( A = 147 \) square units, and the prism has three faces:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m V = 147 \times \text{length}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 4: Substitute the known values.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m V = 147 \times 32.46831448210493
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 5: Calculate the volume.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m V \approx 4763.404093359337 \text{ cubic units}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 6: Round to the nearest whole number.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m V \approx 4763
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the volume of the prism is \boxed{4763} cubic units.<|endoftext|>
