[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the coefficient of the $x^2$ term in the expansion of the product $\left(ax^3 + 3x^2 - 2x\right)\left(bx^2 - 7x - 4\right)$, we first need to expand the expression. Let's denote the first term as $a(x^3) = ax^3$ and the second term as $b(3x^2) = 3bx^2$. The product will then look like this:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ abx^3 + 3a(7)bx^2 - ab(4x) - 2bx^2 - 2(7)ax^3 - 2(4)bx\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Combining like terms, we get the expanded form:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ (ab)x^3 + 21abx^2 - 4abx + (-2b - 28a)x^3 \]
