[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let x be the number of points Hadley must score on the final test.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The mean is the sum of the points divided by the number of tests.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \( \frac{92 + 73 + 79 + 87 + x}{5} = 80 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Multiplying both sides by 5, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \( 92 + 73 + 79 + 87 + x = 400 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Adding the numbers on the left side, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \( 341 + x = 400 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Subtracting 341 from both sides, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \( x = 59 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, Hadley must score at least \boxed{59} points on the final test.
