[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Yes, I am happy to help. To find the length of the diagonal connecting point A and point B in a rectangular prism, we can use the formula for the distance between two points in three-dimensional space when the points are right angles (i.e., the diagonal of the rectangle). The formula is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[d = \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2 + (z_2 - z_1)^2}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m where \((x_1, y_1, z_1)\) and \((x_2, y_2, z_2)\) are the coordinates of points A and B, respectively. For the rectangular prism, the coordinates of point A are \((0, 0, 0)\) and the coordinates of point B are \((2, 2, 10)\). Substituting these coordinates into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[d = \sqrt{(2 - 0)^2 + (2 - 0)^2 + (10 - 0)^2}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[d = \sqrt{2^2 + 2^2 + 10^2}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[d = \sqrt{4 + 4 + 100}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[d = \sqrt{108}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplifying further:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[d = \sqrt{36 \cdot 3} = 6\sqrt{3}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the length of the diagonal connecting point A and point B is \(6\sqrt{3}\) inches.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
