[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In the $19^\text{th}$ century, Britain used a money system which included pence, farthings, shillings and pounds. The following conversions were used:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\bullet$ $4 \text{ farthings} = 1 \text{ pence},$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\bullet$ $12 \text{ pence} = 1 \text{ shilling},$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\bullet$ $20 \text{ shillings} = 1 \text{ pound}.$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m How many total farthings were equivalent to $1$ pound and $5$ pence?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find out how many farthings are equivalent to 1 pound and 5 pence, we need to follow the given conversions step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1 \text{ pound} = 24 \text{ pence} \quad \text{(1 pound is equal to 24 farthings)}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5 \text{ pence} \div 1 \text{ shilling} = 5 \text{ pence} = 5 \text{ shillings} = 24 \text{ pence} = 24 \text{ farthings}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, 5 pence is equivalent to 24 farthings:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5 \text{ pence} = 24 \text{ farthings}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, let's add this in the context of the given steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1 \text{ pound} = 24 \text{ farthings}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1 \text{ pounds and 5 pence} = 1 \text{ pound} + 5 \text{ pence} = 24 \text{ farthings}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
