[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m  Josh purchased 15 packs of candy necklaces from Store Y. There are 15 candy necklaces in each pack. Joshua gives away 170 candy necklaces to kids at Shelterhouse School. Joshua also decides to keep 20% of the candy necklaces he purchased for himself. How many candy necklaces does he have left? To determine the number of candy necklaces Josh has left, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of candy necklaces inside the 15 packs.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Determine how many candy necklaces Joshua keeps for himself.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Subtract the remaining candy necklaces from the total to get the number of candy necklaces he has left.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Step 1: Calculate the total number of candy necklaces.**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Josh purchased 15 packs, with each pack containing 15 candy necklaces.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 15 \text{ packs} \times 15 \text{ candy necklaces per pack} = 225 \text{ candy necklaces}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Step 2: Determine how many candy necklaces Joshua keeps for himself.**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Joshua decides to keep 20% of the candy necklaces he purchased for himself.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 20\% \text{ of } 225 \text{ candy necklaces} = 0.20 \times 225 = 45 \text{ candy necklaces}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Step 3: Subtract the remaining candy necklaces from the total to find out how many he has left.**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The number of candy necklacesJosh provides away is 170.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 225 \text{ candy necklaces} - 170 \text{ candy necklaces} = 55 \text{ candy necklaces}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the number of candy necklaces Josh has left is \boxed{55}.
