[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the sum of the first 10 odd positive integers, we need to first identify these numbers. The first 10 odd positive integers can be represented as follows: 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, and 19.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we need to find the sum of these numbers. We can do this by adding them together step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 1 + 3 = 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 4 + 5 = 9 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 9 + 7 = 16 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 16 + 9 = 25 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 25 + 11 = 36 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 36 + 13 = 49 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 49 + 15 = 64 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 64 + 17 = 81 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 81 + 19 = 100 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
