[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Ivan rents a car for $\$$25 a day and $\$$0.20 a mile. If he rents it for 4 days and drives it 400 miles, how many dollars does he pay?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To compute how much Ivan pays be 4 times his rented car using 25, 0.02 for every mile:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. First, calculate the cost for the miles:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4 \times 400 \text{ miles} = 1600 \text{ miles}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Since 0.02 cents per mile is typically used per mile, multiply:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 0.02 \text{ cents} \times 1600 \text{ miles} = 32 \text{ cents}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Add the cost per day to the miles cost to get the total expense:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 25 \text{ dollars/day} + 32 \text{ cents} = 25 \text{ dollars/day} + \frac{32}{100} \text{ dollars} = 25 \text{ dollars/day} + 0.32 \text{ dollars/day}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Add the rental cost which is $\$$25:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 25 + 0.32 = 25.32 \text{ dollars}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, Ivan pays $\$$25.32.
