[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A deli sandwich consists of one type of bread, one type of meat, and one type of sauce. The deli offers wheat, rye, and white bread; ham, turkey, roast beef, and tuna; ranch and southwest chipotle sauce. Javier is allergic to rye bread, tuna, and southwest chipotle sauce. He tells the server to assemble a random deli sandwich. What is the probability that Javier will suffer an allergic reaction?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine the probability that Javier will suffer an allergic reaction, we need to consider the total number of possible deli sandwiches he can choose from and the number of sandwiches that include rye, tuna, and southwest chipotle sauce.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, let's list the ingredients available at the shop:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Bread (wheat, rye, white)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Meats (ham, turkey, roast beef, tuna)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Sauces (ranch, southwest chipotle)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Javier is allergic to:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - rye bread
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - tuna
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - southwest chipotle sauce
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We will consider each possible combination of ingredients and calculate the probability for each scenario.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Scenario 1: All meats (ham, turkey, roast beef, tuna)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Options: wheat, rye, white
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of bread is wheat: \(\frac{1}{3}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of meat is ham, turkey, roast beef, tuna: \(\frac{1}{2}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of sauce is ranch: \(\frac{1}{2}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(\text{all meats}) = \left( \frac{1}{3} \right) \times \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \times \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) = \frac{1}{12}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Scenario 2: All bread (white, rye, wheat)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Options: ham, turkey, roast beef, tuna
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of meat is ham, turkey, roast beef, tuna: \(\frac{1}{2}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of bread is wheat: \(\frac{1}{3}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of sauce is ranch: \(\frac{1}{2}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(\text{all bread}) = \left( \frac{1}{3} \right) \times \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \times \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) = \frac{1}{12}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Scenario 3: All meat h/t tuna (tuna)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Options: rye, white, rye (all wheat)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of bread is wheat: \(\frac{1}{4}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of meat is ham, turkey, roast beef, tuna: \(\frac{1}{2}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of sauce is ranch: \(\frac{1}{2}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(\text{all meat, north}) = \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) \times \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \times \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) = \frac{1}{16}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Scenario 4: All bread (white, rye, wheat, ham, turkey, roast beef, tuna)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of bread is wheat: \(\frac{1}{4}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of meat is ham, turkey, roast beef, tuna: \(\frac{2}{2} = 1\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of sauce is ranch: \(\frac{1}{2}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(\text{all bread}) = \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) \times 1 \times \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) = \frac{1}{8}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Scenario 5: All meat h/t north chips (tuna)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Options: wheat, rye, wheat
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of bread is wheat: \(\frac{1}{4}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of meat is ham, turkey, roast beef, tuna: \(\frac{2}{2} = 1\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of sauce is ranch: \(\frac{1}{2}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(\text{all meat, north}) = \left( \frac{1}{4} \right) \times \left( 1 \right) \times \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) = \frac{1}{8}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Scenario 6: All meat h/t all rye nuggets (white)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Options: wheat, white, wheat
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of bread is wheat: \(\frac{1}{3}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of meat is ham, turkey, roast beef, tuna: \(\frac{3}{2}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - Probability of sauce is ranch: \(\frac{1}{2}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(\text{all meat, all rye}) = \left( \frac{1}{3} \right) \times \left( \frac{3}{2} \right) \times \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) = \frac{1}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, let's find the probability that Javier will suffer an allergic reaction by considering the possible scenarios:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. \(\frac{1}{12}\) for all meats (including tuna).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. \(\frac{1}{12}\) for all bread (including wheat).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. \(\frac{1}{8}\) as per Scenario 1.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. \(\frac{1}{8}\) as per Scenario 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. \(\frac{1}{4}\) as per Scenario 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6. \(\frac{1}{4}\) as per Scenario 4.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The total probability is the sum of the individual probabilities:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(\text{all meats}) = \frac{1}{12} + \frac{1}{12} + \frac{1}{8} + \frac{1}{8} + \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's calculate the sum:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{1}{12} + \frac{1}{12} = \frac{2}{12} = \frac{1}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{1}{8} + \frac{1}{8} = \frac{2}{8} = \frac{1}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{4} = \frac{2}{4} = \frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Final Calculation
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Sum of all individual probabilities:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{1}{12} + \frac{1}{12} + \frac{1}{8} + \frac{1}{8} + \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{4} = \frac{1}{6} + \frac{1}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Converting \(\frac{1}{4}\) to a common denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{1}{4} = \frac{2}{8}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{1}{6} + \frac{2}{8} = \frac{4}{24} + \frac{6}{24} = \frac{10}{24} = \frac{5}{12}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Probability of allergic reaction
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since probability of not suffering allergic reaction is the complement of above event:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(\text{all non-allergic}) = 1 - P(\text{all allergic})
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(\text{all non-allergic}) = 1 - \frac{5}{12}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(\text{all non-allergic}) = \frac{7}{12}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Final Answer
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{\frac{7}{12}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
