[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's define \( x \) as the total number of football cards Max has at the beginning. According to the problem, after deleting 3 cards, Max is left with 3 cards. Therefore, we can express this relationship with the following equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x - 3 = 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we solve for \( x \) by isolating it on one side of the equation. To do this, we add 3 to both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x - 3 + 3 = 3 + 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ x = 6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, Max initially has \(\boxed{6}\) football cards.
