[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    To find the largest multiple of 3 in this range, divide 99 by 3:  
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \(\frac{99}{3} = 33\). So, the largest multiple of 3 must be \(33 \times 3 = 99\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Therefore, the multiples of 3 are: \(3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, 21, 24, 27, 30, 33, 36, 39, 42, 45, 48, 51, 54, 57, 60, 63, 66, 69, 72, 75, 78, 81, 84, 87, 90, 93, 96, 99\).
