[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we substitute \( g(-3) \) into \( f(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ f(g(-3)) = f(-3) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we use the definition of \( f(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ f(-3) = 2(-3) + 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's calculate this step-by-step:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Calculate \( 2(-3) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[ 2(-3) = -6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Add 1 to the result:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[ -6 + 1 = -5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the value of \( f(g(x)) \) is:
