[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\sqrt[3]{12} \times \sqrt[3]{20} \times \sqrt[3]{15} \times \sqrt[3]{60} = \sqrt[3]{12 \times a \times b \times c \times d} = \sqrt[3]{12 \times a \times b \times 20 \times d} = \sqrt[3]{12\sqrt[3]{12 \times a^2 \times b \times d \times 20}} = \sqrt[3]{12\sqrt[3]{12}\times \sqrt[3]{\frac{a^2\times b \times 20}{d}}}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 1: Identify the factors under the cube root.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 2: Separate the factors under the cube root with the variable 'a', 'b', 'c', and 'd'.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step 3: Combine the cube roots of the individual factors plus the constant 'a', 'b', 'c', and 'd'.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\sqrt[3]{12} \times \sqrt[3]{20} \times \sqrt[3]{15} \times \sqrt[3]{60}$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = $\sqrt[3]{12 \times \sqrt[3]{a^2 \times b \times d}}$
