[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the polynomials whose roots are \(2r_1\), \(2r_2\), and \(2r_3\), we first need to recall that the polynomial whose roots are the roots of the given cubic polynomial \(x^3 - 3x^2 + 8 = 0\) will have roots \(r_1, r_2,\) and \(r_3\). Therefore, we seek to find polynomials whose roots are \(2r_1, 2r_2,\) and \(2r_3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we note how scale and shifting transformations affect the roots of the polynomials:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Consider the polynomial \(x^3 - 3x^2 + 8 = 0\). The roots of this polynomial are \(r_1, r_2,\) and \(r_3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. We want to form a polynomial with roots \(2r_1, 2r_2,\) and \(2r_3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Notice the relationship between the scaled and shifted versions. If a polynomial \(P(x) = a_3 x^3 + a_2 x^2 + a_1 x + a_0\) has roots \(a, b, c\), then a new polynomial with roots \(a_1, b_1, c_1\) can be obtained by scaling and shifting the polynomial by a constant factor:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     - **Scaling:** The polynomial becomes \(aP\left(\frac{x - b}{a}\right)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     - **Shifting:** The polynomial becomes \(aP(x) - aP(b)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Hence, our new polynomial for \(2r_1\), \(2r_2\), and \(2r_3\) will be:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[P(x) = a (x - 2r_1) (x - 2r_2) (x - 2r_3)\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Here \(a\) is a scaling constant.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Expanding this expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(x) = a \left[\left(x - 2r_1\right)\left(x - 2r_2\right)\left(x - 2r_3\right)\right]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = a \left[x^3 - (2r_1+2r_2+2r_3)x^2 + (2r_1 \cdot 2r_2 + 2r_1 \cdot 2r_3 + 2r_2 \cdot 2r_3)x - 2r_1 \cdot 2r_2 \cdot 2r_3\right]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we need to combine the constants inside the polynomial. Note that the constant term \(a \cdot 2r_1 \cdot 2r_2 \cdot 2r_3\) can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2r_1 \cdot 2r_2 \cdot 2r_3 = 16r_1r_2r_3 = a \cdot 2r_1 \cdot 2r_2 \cdot 2r_3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m -2r_1 \cdot 2r_2 \cdot 2r_3 = -a \cdot 2r_1 \cdot 2r_2 \cdot 2r_3 = -16a r_1r_2r_3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Combining all this, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(x) = a \left[x^3 - (2r_1+2r_2+2r_3)x^2 + (7r_1r_2r_3)x - 16(r_1r_2 + r_2r_3 + r_1r_3) \right]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve this, we determine the specific value of \(a\) needed for a polynomial with roots \(r_1, r_2,\) and \(r_3\). We verify that this general form allows for polynomial roots \(2r_1, 2r_2,\) and \(2r_3\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(1) = a \left[1^3 - (2+2+2)x^2 + (7r_1r_2r_3)x - 16r_1r_2 + 7r_1r_2r_3 - 16r_2r_2\right]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = a \left[1 - 6x^2 + (7r_1r_2r_3 - 7r_1r_2)x - 16r_1r_2 + 7r_1r_2r_3 - 16r_2r_3\right]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = a \left[1 - 6x^2 + (7r_1r_2r_3 - 7r_1r_2 - 16r_1r_2 + 7r_1r_2 - 16r_2r_3)\right]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This matches the polynomial derived from the conditions \(2r_1, 2r_2,\) and \(2r_3\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(x) = 0x^3 + 7r_1r_2r_3 - 7r_1r_2 - 16r_1r_2 + 7r_1r_2 - 16r_2r_3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplifying further:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m P(x) = 7r_1r_2r_3 - 16r_1r_2 + 7r_1r_2 - 16r_2r_3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = 7r_1r_2r_3 - 16r_1r_2 - 16r_2r_3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Hence, the polynomial is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{x^3 - 3x^2 + 8}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This polynomial has roots \(2r_1,\) \(2r_2,\) and \(2r_3\) because the constant term \(7r_1r_2r_3 = 8\) is consistent with the conditions of the problem.
