[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m How many different two-person sub-committees can be selected from a committee of six people (the order of choosing the people does not matter)?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To calculate the number of different two-person sub-committees that can be selected from a committee of six people, we start by noting that the order of choosing the two people does not matter. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we calculate the number of ways to choose two people from six. This is given by the combination formula \( \binom{6}{2} \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \binom{6}{2} = \frac{6!}{2!(6-2)!} = \frac{6 \times 5}{2 \times 1} = 15
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, there are 15 different two-person sub-committees that can be selected from a committee of six people.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Each of these two-person sub-committees can then be further divided into three possible assignments of the two people to two different sub-committees.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The number of ways to assign each of these two-person sub-committees to two different sub-committees is \( 2^3 \) because each of the 15 two-person sub-committees can be assigned to any one of the two machines.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the total number of different two-person sub-committees that can be selected is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 15 \times 2^3 = 15 \times 8 = 120
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{120}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 15
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
