[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the remainder when \(8735 + 8736 + 8737 + 8738\) is divided by 11, we can use modular arithmetic. We start by finding the remainder of each number when divided by 11, and then sum those remainders. Finally, we divide the sum of the remainders by 11 to find the remainder of the original addition.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, let's find the remainders of \(8735\), \(8736\), \(8737\), and \(8738\) when divided by 11:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. \(8735 \div 11\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    8735 = 8 \times 1125 + 5
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    8735 \equiv 5 \pmod{11}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. \(8736 \div 11\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    8736 = 8 \times 1082 + 4
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    8736 \equiv 4 \pmod{11}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. \(8737 \div 11\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    8737 = 8 \times 1080 + 1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    8737 \equiv 1 \pmod{11}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. \(8738 \div 11\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    8738 = 7 \times 1292 + 3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    8738 \equiv 3 \pmod{11}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we sum the remainders:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5 + 4 + 1 + 3 = 13
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Finally, we find the remainder when 13 is divided by 11:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 13 \div 11 = 1 \text{ remainder } 2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 13 \equiv 2 \pmod{11}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the remainder when \(8735 + 8736 + 8737 + 8738\) is divided by 11 is \(\boxed{2}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Compute: 123 × 7 + 45 × 8.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To compute \(123 \times 7 + 45 \times 8\), we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. First, compute \(123 \times 7\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    123 \times 7 = 861
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Next, compute \(45 \times 8\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    45 \times 8 = 360
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Now, add the results from the two multiplications.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    861 + 360 = 1221
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the final answer is:
