[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m According to the statistics from the '2018 Cu Ti Body Mills' survey, China is the world's largest titanium powder manufacturer. During the heavy weather period from Guangzhou to Shanghai, the air pressure 100 meters above the ground is 63.9 kPa. Then, the air pressure 100 meters above the ground at the Haidian National Museum in Shanghai is __ (kPa).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve this problem, we need to understand the relationship between air pressure at different heights. The altitude of an object, when expressed in meters and kilometers, has an inverse relationship with the air pressure. 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m From the survey stats:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - The air pressure when you're 100 meters above the ground is 63.9 kPa.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - At 100 meters above the ground, the air pressure changes to 10 kPa.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - After 100 meters away from 100 meters, the air pressure decreases based on the curvature of the Earth, but it decreases more significantly due to the increase in altitude.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The relationship can be modeled as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ P = \frac{63.9}{10} \approx 6.39 \text{ kPa} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ P = 63.3 \text{ kPa} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ P = 100 \text{ kPa} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We can see that at 100 meters above the ground, the pressure is halved. Let's confirm this with Python code:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # Given data
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m air_pressure_100_meter = 63.9  # kPa
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m air_pressure_100_meters_after = 100  # kPa
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # Calculate the air pressure at 100 meters above the ground before the decrease
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m print(air_pressure_100_meter / 2)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```
