[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To convert $2 \frac{1}{6}$ yards to inches, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Convert the mixed number $2 \frac{1}{6}$ yards into an improper fraction: $2 \frac{1}{6} = \frac{12}{6} + \frac{1}{6} = \frac{13}{6}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Convert the improper fraction $\frac{13}{6}$ to a decimal: $\frac{13}{6} \approx 2.1667$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Convert the decimal to inches. Since there are 12 inches in a foot, we can multiply 2.1667 inches by 12 to get the total number of inches. $2.1667 \times 12 \approx 26.16$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, $2 \frac{1}{6}$ yards is approximately \boxed{26.16} inches.<|endoftext|>
