[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m er, to solve this problem, we first simplify the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $ n + (n + 1) + (n + 2) = 9 \Rightarrow 3n + 3 = 9 \Rightarrow 3n = 6$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, $n = \frac{6}{3} = 2$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m zeichsystem
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the value of n in the equation n + (n + 1) + (n + 2) = 9, we set up the following equation: 3n + 3 = 9. To find n, we need to isolate it on one side of the equation. We do this by subtracting 3 from both sides: 3n = 6. Next, we divide both sides by 3: n = 2. So, the value of n that satisfies the equation is n = 2.<|endoftext|>
