[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m :^ To find the measure of the smallest interior angle of the triangle, we start by letting the measures of the angles be \(5x\), \(6x\), and \(7x\) where \(x\) is the common factor. The smallest angle is \(5x\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We know the sum of the interior angles of a triangle is \(180^\circ\). Therefore, we can write the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[5x + 6x + 7x = 180^\circ.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Combining like terms, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[18x = 180^\circ.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find \(x\), we divide both sides of the equation by 18:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[x = \frac{180^\circ}{18} = 10^\circ.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we substitute \(x = 10^\circ\) back into the expressions for the measures of the angles to find the measure of the smallest angle:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[5x = 5 \times 10^\circ = 50^\circ,\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[6x = 6 \times 10^\circ = 60^\circ,\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[7x = 7 \times 10^\circ = 70^\circ.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The smallest angle is \(50^\circ\). Therefore, the measure of the smallest interior angle is:
