[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the largest value of \( x \) that satisfies the equation \( |x-5|=12 \), we need to understand what the absolute value inequality means. The absolute value equation \( |y| = a \) represents all the numbers \( y \) such that \( y = a \) or \( y = -a \). Therefore, there are two possible solutions for \( |x-5|=12 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. \( x-5 = 12 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. \( x-5 = -12 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We solve these equations separately.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Case 1: \( x-5 = 12 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x-5 = 12
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Add 5 to both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x = 12 + 5
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x = 17
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Case 2: \( x-5 = -12 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x-5 = -12
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Add 5 to both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x = -12 + 5
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m x = -7
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Finding the Largest \( x \)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
