[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If $x$, $y$, and $z$ are positive with $xy=20\sqrt[3]{2}$, $xz = 35\sqrt[3]{2}$, and $yz=14\sqrt[3]{2}$, then what is $xyz$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the value of \(x \cdot y \cdot z\), we start with the given equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m xy = 20\sqrt[3]{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m xz = 35\sqrt[3]{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m yz = 14\sqrt[3]{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, we multiply all three equations together:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (xy) \cdot (xz) \cdot (yz) = (20\sqrt[3]{2}) \cdot (35\sqrt[3]{2}) \cdot (14\sqrt[3]{2})
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (xyz)^2 = 20 \cdot 35 \cdot 14 \cdot (\sqrt[3]{2})^3
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We know that \((\sqrt[3]{2})^3 = 2\), so we can rewrite the equation as:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (xyz)^2 = 20 \cdot 35 \cdot 14 \cdot 2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we calculate the product on the right-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 20 \cdot 35 \cdot 14 = 20 \cdot (5 \cdot 7) \cdot 14 = 20 \cdot 35 \cdot 14
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Unscaling the right-hand side, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 20 \cdot 35 \cdot 14 = (2 \cdot 5) \cdot (3 \cdot 7) \cdot (2 \cdot 7) = 2 \cdot 5 \cdot 3 \cdot 7 \cdot 2 \cdot 7 = 7^3 \cdot 5^2 = (7 \cdot 5)^2 \cdot 5^2 = 35^2 \cdot 5^2 = (7 \cdot 5 \cdot 7) \cdot 5^2 = 350 \cdot 5^2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We simplify further:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 350 \cdot 25 = 9250
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (xyz)^2 = 9250
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Taking the square root of both sides, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m xyz = \sqrt{9250}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We simplify \(\sqrt{9250}\) by factoring:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 9250 = 5^3 \cdot 107 \approx 9250 \approx 100^2 \approx 10^2 \cdot 10^2 = (10 \cdot 10) \cdot 10^2 = 10^4
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m xyz = 10^2 \cdot 10^2 = 3 \cdot 5^2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{3 \cdot 5^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
