[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's consider the vectors \(\mathbf{v}_1 = (2, 0, 0)\) and \(\mathbf{v}_2 = (0, -5, 0)\). The cross product \(\mathbf{v}_1 \times \mathbf{v}_2\) gives us the normal vector \(\mathbf{n}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \mathbf{n} = \mathbf{v}_1 \times \mathbf{v}_2 = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2 & 0 & 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 0 & -5 & 0
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = \mathbf{i}(0 \cdot 0 - 0 \cdot (-5)) - \mathbf{j}(2 \cdot 0 - 0 \cdot 0) + \mathbf{k}(2 \cdot (-5) - 0 \cdot 0)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m = (0, 0, -10)
