[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let $A,$ $B,$ $C$ be the angles of a non-right triangle.  Compute
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\begin{vmatrix} \tan A & 1  & 1 \\ 1 & \tan B & 1 \\ 1 & 1 & \tan C \end{vmatrix}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the determinant of the matrix \(\begin{vmatrix} \tan A & 1 & 1 \\ 1 & \tan B & 1 \\ 1 & 1 & \tan C \end{vmatrix}\), we will use the Cramer's Rule for Determinants. Cramer's Rule states that for a determinant \( D \) formed by a matrix \( M \) of order \( n \times n \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m D = \begin{vmatrix} m_{11} & m_{12} & m_{13} \\ m_{21} & m_{22} & m_{23} \\ m_{31} & m_{32} & m_{33} \end{vmatrix} = \frac{m_{11} \Delta_2}{m_{21} \Delta_3} - \frac{m_{12} \Delta_3}{m_{22} \Delta_1} + \frac{m_{13} \Delta_1}{m_{23} \Delta_2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m where \( m_{ij} \) represents the entry in the \( i \)-th row and \( j \)-th column of the matrix, and \(\Delta_i\) is the determinant of the \(i\)-th column.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given the matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A = \begin{vmatrix} \tan A & 1 & 1 \\ 1 & \tan B & 1 \\ 1 & 1 & \tan C \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m we will apply Cramer's Rule to the matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \begin{vmatrix} \tan A & 1 & 1 \\ 1 & \tan B & 1 \\ 1 & 1 & \tan C \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This matrix will be:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \Delta = \tan A \Delta_2 - 1 \Delta_3 + 1 \Delta_1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m where \(\Delta_1 = 1\), \(\Delta_2 = \tan B\), and \(\Delta_3 = \tan C\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, let's find each of the rows \(m_{11}\), \(m_{12}\), and \(m_{13}\) corresponding to the rows in the original matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m m_{11} = \tan A, \quad m_{12} = 1, \quad m_{13} = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m m_{11} \Delta_2 = \tan A \cdot \tan B \cdot \tan C
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m m_{12} \Delta_3 = 1 \cdot \tan C \cdot \tan C = \tan^2 C
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m m_{13} \Delta_1 = 1 \cdot \tan A \cdot \tan B = \tan A \tan B
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, apply Cramer's Rule:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \Delta = \frac{m_{11} \Delta_2}{m_{21} \Delta_3} - \frac{m_{12} \Delta_3}{m_{22} \Delta_1} + \frac{m_{13} \Delta_1}{m_{23} \Delta_2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Substitute the values:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \tan A \cdot \tan B \cdot \tan C - \tan^2 C
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since \(\Delta_2 = \tan B\) and \(\Delta_3 = \tan C\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \tan A \cdot \tan B \cdot \tan C - \tan^2 C
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the determinant of the given matrix is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \tan A \cdot \tan B \cdot \tan C - \tan^2 C
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the final answer is \(\boxed{\tan A \tan B \tan C - \tan^2 C}\)<|endoftext|>
