[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve the expression \(\frac{1}{2 \sin 10^\circ} - 2 \sin 70^\circ\), we will break it down into manageable steps.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Simplify the first part of the expression \(\frac{1}{2 \sin 10^\circ}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    The sine of 10 degrees is \(0.1736\). Therefore, the first part simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \frac{1}{2 \times 0.1736} = \frac{1}{0.3472} \approx 2.884
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Substitute this result into the second part of the expression, \(2 \sin 70^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    We know that \(\sin 70^\circ \approx 0.9397\). Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    2 \sin 70^\circ \approx 2 \times 0.9397 = 1.8794
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Subtract the second part from the first part.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    2.884 - 1.8794 \approx 0.0046
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, after performing the calculations, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{0.0046}
