[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The company needs 600 pounds of potatoes per week. The suppliers sell potatoes for $3.26 per pound. Express part of the cost per point as an expression that includes the word OR. OP
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine the cost per point expressed as an expression that includes the word "OR," we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Identify the given information:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - The cost per pound of potatoes is $3.26.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - The company requires 600 pounds of potatoes per week.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Calculate the cost per point:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - The supplier sells potatoes for $3.26 per pound.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - The company requires 600 pounds of potatoes per week.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    - Therefore, the cost per point is the product of the cost per pound and the quantity of potatoes required per week.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \text{Cost per point} = 3.26 \, \text{\$/pound} \times 600 \, \text{pounds}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Perform the multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    3.26 \times 600 = 1956
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Express the result as an expression using the word "OR":
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    3.26 \times 600 = 3.26 \text{(\$/pound)} \, \text{×} \, 600 \text{pounds} = 2.6 \text{(\$/$pound)} \, \text{×} \, 600 \text{pounds} = 1956 \text{()} \text{\/} \text{\/} \text{\/} \text{\/}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. Simplify the final expression to fit the required format:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    3.26 \times 600 = 1956 \, \text{dollars}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the cost per point expressed as an expression that includes the word "OR" is \boxed{1956.}
