[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Find the inverse of the matrix
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} 6 & -4 \\ -3 & 2 \end{pmatrix}.\]If the inverse does not exist, then enter the zero matrix.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the inverse of the matrix \(\begin{pmatrix} 6 & -4 \\ -3 & 2 \end{pmatrix}\), we can use the formula for the inverse of a 2x2 matrix. The formula is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{inverse} = \frac{1}{\det(A)} \begin{pmatrix} d & -b \\ -c & a \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m where \(A = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\det(A)\) is the determinant of \(A\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, let's calculate the determinant \(d\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \det(A) = ad - bc
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m For our matrix \(\begin{pmatrix} 6 & -4 \\ -3 & 2 \end{pmatrix}\), \(\det(A) = 6 \cdot 2 - (-4) \cdot (-3) = 12 - 12 = 0\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since the determinant is 0, the matrix does not have an inverse. Therefore, the inverse of the matrix does not exist.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Putting this in the requested format:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 0 & -(-4) \\ -(-3) & 6 \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This is because a zero matrix would be the inverse of the original matrix.<|endoftext|>
