[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If the comlex fraction $-\frac{1}{2} + \frac{5}{4}i$ is converted into a binomial with integer terms, which binomial would give the same result as the original fraction? The composit fraction is given by \(\frac{10}{2} + \frac{15}{4}i\), where the exponents of \(\frac{1}{2}\) and \(\frac{1}{4}\) are automatically determined. In this form, the fraction is in the form of \(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The angle \(\theta\) that satisfies this representation is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \theta = \arctan \left(\frac{15\sqrt{10}}{10}\right) - \pi.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We can simplify this using the fact that \(\tan(2\pi - x) = \tan x\) and thus:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \theta = \arctan \left(\frac{15\sqrt{10}}{10}\right).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the complex fraction \(\frac{10}{2} + \frac{15}{4}i = \cos(\arctan \left(\frac{15\sqrt{10}}{15}\right)) + i \sin(\arctan \left(\frac{15\sqrt{10}}{15}\right)) = \cos(\theta) + i \sin(\theta) = \cos(\arctan \left(\frac{\sqrt{10}}{2}\right)) + i \sin(\arctan \left(\frac{\sqrt{10}}{2}\right)).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Hence, the binomial that gives the same result as the original fraction is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{1 + i\frac{\sqrt{10}}{2}}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let \( u_{0} = 0 \) and define \( u_{n+1} = \frac{2}{3}u_{n} + \frac{1}{u_{n}^{3} - 3} \). How many terms of the sequence are needed to approximate \( 8 \) to four decimal places? To approximate \( 8 \) to four decimal places using the given recurrence relation \( u_{n+1} = \frac{2}{3}u_n + \frac{1}{u_n^3 - 3} \), we start by calculating the first few terms of the sequence.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Initial term \( u_0 = 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, calculate \( u_1 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m u_1 = \frac{2}{3}u_0 + \frac{1}{u_0^3 - 3} = \frac{2}{3} \cdot 0 + \frac{1}{0^3 - 3} = \frac{1}{-3} = -\frac{1}{3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, calculate \( u_2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m u_2 = \frac{2}{3}u_1 + \frac{1}{u_1^3 - 3} = \frac{2}{3} \left(-\frac{1}{3}\right) + \frac{1}{\left(-\frac{1}{3}\right)^3 - 3} = \frac{-\frac{2}{9}}{-\frac{1}{27} - 3} = \frac{-\frac{2}{9}}{-\frac{1}{27} - \frac{81}{27}} = \frac{-\frac{2}{9}}{-\frac{82}{27}} = \frac{-\frac{2}{9}}{-\frac{82}{27}} = \frac{-\frac{2}{9}}{-\frac{82}{27}}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplify the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m u_2 = \frac{-\frac{2}{9}}{-\frac{82}{27}} = \frac{2}{9} \cdot \frac{27}{82} = \frac{6}{82} = \frac{3}{41}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, calculate \( u_3 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m u_3 = \frac{2}{3}u_2 + \frac{1}{u_2^3 - 3} = \frac{2}{3} \left(\frac{3}{41}\right) + \frac{1}{\left(\frac{3}{41}\right)^3 - 3} = \frac{\frac{6}{41}}{\frac{261}{689}} + \frac{1}{\left(\frac{3}{41}\right)^3 - 3} = \frac{\frac{6}{41}}{\frac{261}{689}} + \frac{1}{\left(\frac{27}{689}\right)^3 - 3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplify the first term:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m u_3 = \frac{\frac{6}{41}}{\frac{261}{689}} = \frac{6}{41} \cdot \frac{689}{261} = \frac{3134}{10781}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, calculate \( u_4 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m u_4 = \frac{2}{3}u_3 + \frac{1}{u_3^3 - 3} = \frac{2}{3} \left(\frac{3134}{10781}\right) + \frac{1}{\left(\frac{3134}{10781}\right)^3 - 3} = \frac{\frac{6268}{10781}}{\frac{298163169}{1090236405}} + \frac{1}{\left(\frac{6268}{10781}\right)^3 - 3} = \frac{\frac{6268}{10781}}{\frac{298163169}{1090236405}} + \frac{1}{\left(\frac{6268}{10781}\right)^3 - 3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplify the first term:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m u_4 = \frac{\frac{6268}{10781}}{\frac{298163169}{1090236405}} = \frac{6268 \cdot 1090236405}{298163169} = \frac{6897000000001}{298163169}.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, calculate \( u_5 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m u_5 = \frac{2}{3}u_4 + \frac{1}{u_4^3 - 3} = \frac{2}{3} \left(\frac{6897000000001}{298163169}\right) + \frac{1}{\left(\frac{6897000000001}{298163169}\right)^3 - 3} = \frac{\frac{13794000000002}{298163169}}{\frac{1203723949457956087}{298163169^3}} + \frac{1}{\left(\frac{6897000000000000}{298163169^3}\right)^3 - 3}.
