[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m It took $4$ days for $75$ workers, all working together at the same rate, to build an embankment. If only $50$ workers had been available, how many total days would it have taken to build the embankment?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To determine the total number of days it would take for 75 workers to build the embankment, we first need to find the work rate of the workers. We can calculate this by dividing the work done by the number of workers.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Given that 75 workers took 4 days to complete the embankment, the total work done by 75 workers in 4 days can be calculated as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Total work done} = \text{Number of workers} \times \text{Time taken} = 75 \times 4 = 300
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the total work done by performing on the embankment is 300 units.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since we have 75 workers, their combined work rate can be represented as:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Work rate of 75 workers} = \frac{\text{Total work done}}{\text{Number of workers}} = \frac{300}{75} = 4 \text{ units/day}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This means that 75 workers can complete 1 unit of work in 1 day. This factor remains constant regardless of the number of workers, and is therefore the daily efficiencc of the 75 workers.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, let's consider the scenario where only 50 workers are available. If the daily efficiencc of the workers remains the same (4 units/day), we can calculate the number of days required for 50 workers to complete the embankment:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \text{Number of days to complete the embankment on 50 workers} = \frac{\text{Total work done}}{\text{Daily work rate}} = \frac{1 \text{ embankment}}{4 \text{ units/day}} = 0.25 \text{ days}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, it would take 50 workers \(\boxed{0.25}\) days to build the embankment.<|endoftext|>
