[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m How many ways are there to put 4 distinguishable balls into 2 distinguishable boxes?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If there are 4 distinguishable balls to place into 2 distinguishable boxes, the method to calculate the number of ways is to follow the following formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (n+r-1)/(r-1) = 4/1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Where n is the number of balls and r is the number of boxes. In this case, n=4 and r=2. Plugging these values into the formula gives us:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4/1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Rearranging it, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m n+r-1 = 4+2-1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m n+r-1 = 5
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m n + r = 5 + 1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m n + r = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the number of ways to arrange 4 distinguishable balls into 2 distinguishable boxes is exactly 8 possible ways.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
