[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Expand the left-hand side of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Combine like terms on both sides of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Isolate the term involving \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Solve for \(x\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's start with step 1: expanding the left-hand side.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (\sqrt{12x} + 12)(\sqrt{3x} - 6)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Using the distributive property (FOIL method):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (\sqrt{12x})(\sqrt{3x}) + (\sqrt{12x})(-6) + (12)(\sqrt{3x}) + (12)(-6)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sqrt{12x \cdot 3x} - 6\sqrt{12x} + 12\sqrt{3x} - 72
