[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the value of the infinite product \((2^{1/3})(4^{1/9})(8^{1/27})(16^{1/81}) \dotsm\), we start by expressing all terms in the product with the same base. We notice that each term can be written as \(2^{\frac{1}{9k}}\) for \(k\) ranging from 1 to infinity. This allows us to rewrite the product as:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \left(2^{\frac{1}{3}} \cdot 2^{\frac{1}{9}} \cdot 2^{\frac{2}{9}} \cdot 2^{\frac{4}{9}} \cdot 2^{\frac{8}{9}} \cdot \cdots\right)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m )^{\frac{1}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This can be simplified to:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2^{\frac{\frac{1}{3} + \frac{1}{9} + \frac{2}{9} + \frac{4}{9} + \cdots}{2}} = 2^{\frac{\frac{1}{3}(1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + \cdots)}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The series in the denominator is an infinite geometric series with the first term \(a = 1\) and common ratio \(r = 2\). The sum \(S\) of an infinite geometric series is given by \(S = \frac{a}{1-r}\). Substituting \(a = 1\) and \(r = 2\), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m S = \frac{1}{1-2} = \frac{1}{-1} = -1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Therefore, the exponent can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{\frac{1}{3}(1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + \cdots)}{2} = \frac{\frac{1}{3} \cdot 2}{2} = \frac{1}{3} \mod 2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{1}{3}^{(\frac{-1}{2})} = \left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{-\frac{1}{2}} = \sqrt[3]{\frac{1}{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the value of the infinite product is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{\sqrt[3]{\frac{1}{3}}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
