[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ## Step  1
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We are given that \\[ \lfloor x \rfloor = 5 + 100 \{ x \}, \\] where \\[ \{ x \} = x - \lfloor x \rfloor. \\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Step  2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We simplify the equation further:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \lfloor x \rfloor + 100 = x - \lfloor x \rfloor \\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \lfloor x \rfloor + 100 = x - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor \\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \lfloor x \rfloor + 100 = x - 2\lfloor x \rfloor \\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 100 = x - \lfloor x \rfloor - 2\lfloor x \rfloor \\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 100 = x - 3\lfloor x \rfloor \\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 3\lfloor x \rfloor = x - 100 \\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now we use the inequality \\[ \lfloor x \rfloor \leqslant x, \\] which can be rewritten using the fact:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # Answer:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 3\lfloor x \rfloor \leqslant x + 100 \\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \left\lfloor \frac{x + 100}{3} \right\rfloor \leqslant x, \] Hence, the greatest possible solution is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # Answer:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \boxed{x = \left\lfloor \frac{100 + 100}{3} \right\rfloor} = 77.<|endoftext|>
