[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Therefore, the total cost for Jamie is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \text{Total cost for Jamie} = c + 6
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. **Calculate the cost of one vanilla bar:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Kevin buys one vanilla bar.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \text{Cost of one vanilla bar} = 2 \text{ dollars}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. **Calculate the total cost for Jamie:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Jamie also buys three vanilla bars.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \text{Total cost for Jamie} = c + 3 \times 2 = c + 6
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. **Calculate the total cost for Kevin:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Kevin buys five chocolate bars.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \text{Total cost for Kevin} = 5 \times c = 5c
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 5. **Calculate the total amount of money spent by Jamie and Kevin:**
