[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Compute the following series: $\sum_{k=0}^{10} -\frac{31}{70}\sqrt{6}^k$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To compute the series \(\sum_{k=0}^{10} -\frac{31}{70}\sqrt{6}^k\), we first recognize that it is a geometric series. The general form of a geometric series is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sum_{k=0}^{n} ar^k = a \frac{1-r^{n+1}}{1-r}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m In our series, we can identify the first term \(a\) as:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m a = -\frac{31}{70}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m and the common ratio \(r\) as:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m r = \sqrt{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m The number of terms in the series is \(n+1 = 10 + 1 = 11\). Substituting these values into the formula for the sum of a geometric series, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \sum_{k=0}^{10} \left(-\frac{31}{70}\sqrt{6}\right)^k = -\frac{31}{70} \frac{1-(\sqrt{6})^{11}}{1-\sqrt{6}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, we simplify \(1 - \sqrt{6}\). Note that:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m (\sqrt{6})^2 = 6 \implies 6 - 6 = 0 \implies 1 - \sqrt{6} = -\sqrt{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m -\frac{31}{70} \frac{1-(-\sqrt{6})^{11}}{-\sqrt{6}} = -\frac{31}{70} \frac{1-(-6)^{11/2}}{-\sqrt{6}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since \((-6)^{11/2} = (-6)^{5 + 11/2} = (-6)^{5} \cdot (-6)^{11/2} = (-6)^5 \cdot (-6)^{5.5} = (-6)^5 \cdot (-6)^3 \cdot (-6)^{2.5} = (-6)^{18}\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1 - (-6)^{11/2} = 1 + 6^{11/2}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Calculating \(6^{11/2}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 6^{11/2} = (6^3)^{1/2} = 6^1 \cdot 6^{1/2} = 6 \cdot \sqrt{6} = 6\sqrt{6}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m -\frac{31}{70} \frac{1 + 6\sqrt{6}}{-\sqrt{6}} = \frac{31}{70} \cdot \frac{1 + 6\sqrt{6}}{\sqrt{6}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We can cancel \(\sqrt{6}\) in the numerator and the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{31(1 + 6\sqrt{6})}{70} = \frac{31}{70} + \frac{31 \cdot 6\sqrt{6}}{70} = \frac{31}{70} + \frac{186\sqrt{6}}{70} = \frac{31 + 186\sqrt{6}}{70}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{\frac{31 + 186\sqrt{6}}{70}}
