[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find how many digits are to the right of the decimal point in the decimal representation of the fraction \(\frac{1}{2^{10}}\), we first need to express the fraction in its simplest form. The denominator, \(2^{10}\), is a power of 10, which can be written as \(10^2\). Therefore, \(\frac{1}{2^{10}}\) can be rewritten as \(\frac{1}{1024}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
