[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m If $15\%$ of $N$ is $45\%$ of 2003, what is the value of $N$?
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the value of \( N \), we start by expressing the problem in mathematical terms. We know that \( 15\% \) of \( N \) is equal to \( 45\% \) of 2003. We can write this as:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 0.15N = 0.45 \times 2003 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, calculate \( 0.45 \times 2003 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 0.45 \times 2003 = 901.45 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ 0.15N = 901.45 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find \( N \), we need to isolate \( N \) on one side of the equation. We do this by dividing both sides of the equation by 0.15:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ N = \frac{901.45}{0.15} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, perform the division:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ N = 6012.3333 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Rounding to two decimal places, the value of \( N \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \boxed{6012.33} \]<|endoftext|>
