[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Certainly! Let's step through the process of finding the sum of all prime numbers between 1 and 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Step 1: Identify Prime Numbers
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A prime number is a natural number greater than 1 that has no positive divisors other than 1 and itself. We'll list all the prime numbers between 1 and 10:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 2 (only divisible by 1 and 2)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 3 (only divisible by 1 and 3)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 5 (only divisible by 1 and 5)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 7 (only divisible by 1 and 7)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m - 11 (only divisible by 1 and 11)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ### Step 2: Sum of Prime Numbers
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, we will sum these prime numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's add them step-by-step:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. Add the first and second numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    2 + 3 = 5
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. Add the result to the third number:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    5 + 5 = 10
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. Add the result to the fourth number:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    10 + 7 = 17
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. Add the result to the fifth number:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    17 + 11 = 28
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the sum of all prime numbers between 1 and 10 is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{28}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
