[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Find the minimum value of
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[(12 - x)(10 - x)(12 + x)(10 + x).\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the minimum value of the expression \[(12 - x)(10 - x)(12 + x)(10 + x),\] we start by rewriting it under a single factor form. Notice that we can factorize it as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[(12 - x)(10 - x)(12 + x)(10 + x) = (12 - x)(12 + x)(10 + x)(10 - x).\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, notice that \((12 - x)(12 + x)\) is a difference raised to the power of 2, and \((10 + x)(10 - x)\) is (at least) a product of 2 constant terms \((10 + x)(10 - x)\). Therefore, our expression simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[(12 - x)(12 + x)(10 + x)(10 - x) = (12 - x)(12 + x) \cdot (10 + x)(10 - x).\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Since the terms \((12 + x)\) and \((10 + x)\) cancel each other out, we are left with:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[(12 - x)(12 + x)(10 + x)(10 - x) = (10)^2 = 100.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the minimum value of the original expression is \(\boxed{100}\).<|endoftext|>
