[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To solve the problem, we need to use the given condition \(\cos 3A + \cos 3B + \cos 3C = 1\) and the lengths of the sides of the triangle \(AB = 10\), \(BC = 13\), and \(CA = 17\).
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m First, recall the sum of angles in a triangle:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m A + B + C = 180^\circ.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m We can use the identity for \(\cos 3\theta\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \cos 3\theta = 4\cos^3 \theta - 3\cos \theta.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \cos 3A = 4\cos^3 A - 3\cos A,
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \cos 3B = 4\cos^3 B - 3\cos B,
