[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To compute \(\binom{8}{6}\), we can use the formula for combinations:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Here, \(n = 8\) and \(k = 6\). Plugging these values into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \binom{8}{6} = \frac{8!}{6!(8-6)!}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Simplify the factorials. Notice that \(8! = 8 \times 7 \times 6!\), so the \(6!\) in the numerator and the denominator cancels out:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \binom{8}{6} = \frac{8 \times 7}{6 \times 5}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Now, divide the numbers in the numerator by the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \binom{8}{6} = \frac{8 \times 7}{6 \times 5} = \frac{56}{30}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Next, simplify \(\frac{56}{30}\). The greatest common divisor of 56 and 30 is 2, so we divide both the numerator and the denominator by 2:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \frac{56}{30} = \frac{56 \div 2}{30 \div 2} = \frac{28}{15}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, \(\binom{8}{6}\) simplified, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{\frac{28}{15}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
