[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the area of the shaded region, we need to first calculate the area of the larger circle and then subtract the area of the smaller circle.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 1. **Calculate the radius of the larger circle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    The radius of the larger circle is given as \(6\). Therefore, the radius \(R\) of the larger circle is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    R = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 2. **Calculate the area of the larger circle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    The area \(A_{\text{large}}\) of a circle is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    A_{\text{large}} = \pi R^2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Substituting the radius \(R = 6\):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    A_{\text{large}} = \pi \times 6^2 = \pi \times 36 = 36\pi
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 3. **Calculate the area of the smaller circle:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    The area \(A_{\text{small}}\) of a circle is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    A_{\text{small}} = \pi r^2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Substituting the radius \(r = 3\) (since the smaller circle touches the larger circle at its center):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    A_{\text{small}} = \pi \times 3^2 = \pi \times 9 = 9\pi
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 4. **Calculate the area of the shaded region:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    The shaded region is the area of the larger circle minus the area of the smaller circle:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    A_{\text{shaded}} = A_{\text{large}} - A_{\text{small}}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    Substituting the areas calculated:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    A_{\text{shaded}} = 36\pi - 9\pi = 27\pi
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Thus, the area of the shaded region is:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \boxed{27\pi}
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
