[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m When a number is written as a sum $(s+ t)^2$, the integer $s+t$ is the sum of two squares. If we take one of these sums and write it out in a geometric pattern, it seems to get progressively larger, explained by an interesting relationship between the terms of a sequence known as the triangular numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Consider the sequence $1, 3, 6, 10, \ldots$. If we take the $n^{\text{th}}$ term of this sequence, we get the number $1 + 2 \times (n-1) = 2n - 1$. By adding another one term, we simply add $2n$.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m What is the $20^{\text{th}}$ triangular number? Think geometrically.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m $\text{(A)}\ 2,020\qquad\text{(B)}\ 20,30\qquad\text{(C)}\ 203\qquad\text{(D)}\ 2,030\qquad\text{(E)}\ 20,300$
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m **Solution:**
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m To find the $20^{\text{th}}$ triangular number, we can use the formula for the $n^{\text{th}}$ triangular number, which is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Triangular Number} = 1 + 2 \times (n-1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Applying this formula to the $20^{\text{th}}$ triangular number, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Triangular Number} = 1 + 2 \times (20-1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Triangular Number} = 1 + 2 \times 19 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Triangular Number} = 1 + 38 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m \[ \text{Triangular Number} = 39 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m So, the $20^{\text{th}}$ triangular number is 39.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m Let's confirm this by using Python code to calculate it.
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # Function to calculate the n-th triangular number
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m def triangular_number(n):
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m     return n * (n + 1) // 2
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m # Calculate the 20th triangular number
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m tn_20 = triangular_number(20)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m print(tn_20)
[36m(main_task pid=1983818)[0m ```
